ns1:48309 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Starrcade was the thirteenth Starrcade professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event produced by World Championship Wrestling (WCW). It took place on 1995 at the Nashville Municipal Auditorium in Nashville. From the 1960s to the 1980s, it was tradition for Jim Crockett Promotions (JCP), a member of the National Wrestling Alliance (NWA), to hold major professional wrestling events at Thanksgiving and Christmas, often at the Greensboro Coliseum Complex in Greensboro, North Carolina in the center of JCP's Virginia, North and South Carolina territory. The 1995 event was the thirteenth show to use the Starrcade name and was the second Starrcade to take place in the Nashville Municipal Auditorium in Nashville." .

