ns1:42119 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Germany participated in the Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017 with the song \"Perfect Life\", performed by Levina and written by Lindsey Ray, Lindy Robbins and Dave Bassett. Prior to the 2017 Contest, Germany had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest sixty times since its debut as one of seven countries to take part in 1956. In Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016, the German entry \"Ghost\" performed by Jamie-Lee placed last out of twenty-six competing songs with eleven points; it was the second year in a row Germany placed last in the final. NDR confirmed that Germany would participate in the 2017 Eurovision Song Contest on 23 May Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016. For their 2017 entry, the broadcaster announced on 14 September Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016 that they would revert to a casting show format for the national final, similar to the format used in 2010 and 2012, which resulted in a first place and a top ten result respectively at Eurovision for Germany. Unser Song 2017 was the competition that selected Germany's entry for the Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017. One of them, Nathan Trent, was automatically eliminated from the selection since he was announced as the Austrian representative for the 2017 Eurovision Song Contest on 19 December Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016 and, according to regulations by the European Broadcasting Union, a performer can not represent more than one country in the same year. The Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017 took place at the International Exhibition Centre in Kyiv, Ukraine and consisted of two semi-finals on 9 May and 11 May and the final on 2017." .

