ns1:42473 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007–08 Paris Saint-Germain F.C. season was France association football club Paris Saint-Germain F.C.'s 35th professional season, their 35th season in Ligue 1 and their 34th consecutive season in France top-flight. Paris Saint-Germain F.C. was present in the 2007–08 Ligue 1, the 2007–08 Coupe de France and the 2007–08 Coupe de la Ligue. Paris Saint-Germain F.C.'s average home gate for the 2007–08 Paris Saint-Germain F.C. season was 36,947, the third highest in the Ligue 1. The group led by Sébastien Bazin in France became the majority shareholder of Paris Saint-Germain F.C.. Ligue 1 strugglers Paris Saint-Germain F.C. kick-started the New Year on a winning note in the France Cup. Paris Saint-Germain F.C. reached the quarter-finals of the France Cup thanks to two-goal hero Loris Arnaud, who found the net twice in a win over Bastia. The 2007–08 Paris Saint-Germain F.C. season was France association football club Paris Saint-Germain F.C.'s ninth season in Division 1 Féminine and their seventh consecutive season in the top division of France women's association football." .

