ns1:42662 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Bangladesh–Mali relations refer to the bilateral relations between Bangladesh and Mali. Bangladeshi peace keepers have been deployed in Mali since April 2014, as part of the United Nations Multidimensional Integrated Stabilization Mission in Mali, when the first contingent of 112 Bangladesh Army personnels left Dhaka for Mali. Bangladesh and Mali have shown mutual interest in expanding their bilateral trade and investments. Mali has shown keen interest to import fertilizer from Bangladesh. On the other hand, as Mali is a large producer of cotton, Bangladesh expressed its deep interest to import huge quantity of cotton for its large textile industry. In 2014, Bangladesh Tariff Commission prepared a feasibility study for the benefits of signing new Free/Preferential trade agreements with African states and recommended that Mali along with Nigeria are the most promising countries for signing such agreements." .

