ns1:42927 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Football League Two play-off Final was a association football match that was played at Wembley Stadium on 2010, at the end of the 2009–10 season. The match determined the fourth and final team to gain promotion from the League Two to the League One, and was contested by Rotherham United F.C. and Dagenham & Redbridge F.C.. Dagenham & Redbridge F.C. won the play-off final 3–2. Rotherham United F.C. reached the final after beating Aldershot Town 3–0 on aggregate in their semi-final. Dagenham & Redbridge F.C. secured their spot with an emphatic 6–0 victory, at home, in the first leg of their semi-final with Morecambe, eventually winning the tie 7–2 on aggregate. Dagenham & Redbridge F.C. achieved promotion to League One after a 3–2 victory over Rotherham United F.C., at Wembley Stadium, thanks to a 70th minute, deflected, Jon Nurse strike. Twice Dagenham & Redbridge F.C. had taken the lead, through goals from Paul Benson and Danny Green, only for Rotherham United F.C. forward Ryan Taylor to return The Millers back to level terms a few minutes later." .

