ns1:43236 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 United States presidential election in Utah was held on 08 November 2016, as part of the 2016 United States presidential election which was also held in the other 49 states and in the District of Columbia. Obama and Biden were reelected in the 2012 United States presidential election in Utah presidential election, defeating former Massachusetts Governor Mitt Romney with 51.1 percent of the popular vote and 61.7 percent of electoral votes. Trump received a much lower percentage of the vote in Utah than did Mitt Romney in 2012 United States presidential election in Utah. Trump received only 45 percent of the vote among Utah members of the LDS Church, barely half the proportion that Romney won in 2012 United States presidential election in Utah." .

