ns1:43664 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The first full-scale Ottoman Empire Siege of Constantinople as a result of the Byzantine Emperor Manuel II's attempts to interfere in the succession of Ottoman Empire Sultans, after the death of Mehmed I in 1421. According to a Byzantine short chronicle compiled in c. 1425, \"on 10 June, Wednesday, at the fourth hour after midday, Mihaloğlu attacked Constantinople\", thus beginning the siege of the city. Mustafa was thus able to gather a significant army, and in late August or early September laid siege to the Ottoman Empire capital, Bursa. As such, the next Ottoman Empire leader, Mehmed II, would be Fall of Constantinople." .

