ns1:43762 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963 Intercontinental Cup was a two-legged association football match contested between 1962–63 European Cup champions Milan and 1963 Copa Libertadores winners Santos F.C.. The first leg was played at the San Siro in Milan, on 1963. Milan won the home game 4–2. As Santos F.C. won the match 4–2, the two teams were level on points. After Milan's 4-2 victory at the San Siro stadium, the return leg took place at the Maracanã in Rio de Janeiro. Milan led 2-0 at half-time. Milan's subsequent attacks forward to the Santos F.C. box were fruitless, and Santos F.C. ran out winners in a controversial but undoubtedly legendary final." .

