ns1:43880 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "China–Maldives relations refer to foreign relations between People's Republic of China and Maldives. People's Republic of China has an embassy in Malé which opened in November 2011 and Maldives has an embassy in Beijing which opened in 2009. In 2002, Maldives Minister of Defense and National Security visited People's Republic of China. In December 2012, Maldives Minister of Defense and National Security visited People's Republic of China. In December 2017, in People's Republic of China, President Yameen signed a free trade agreement with People's Republic of China; notably this was Maldives' first free trade agreement. People's Republic of China and Maldives had announced the construction of the Joint Ocean Observation Station, which the Government of India and the Maldivian Democratic Party have argued will be used for military applications by People's Republic of China." .

