ns1:45844 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "SpoCon is a full-spectrum science fiction and fantasy science fiction convention held annually in Spokane, USA. SpoCon is a sister science fiction convention to MisCon (Missoula, Mont. The first SpoCon was held in 2008 at Gonzaga University. This was the first SpoCon to leave the college campus and make a new home in the Spokane Doubletree Hotel. In 2012, SpoCon changed from the traditional science fiction convention-committee style of leadership and operation to a business model, with the aim of creating a more efficient, forward-thinking and productive organization. In 2016 SpoCon changed back from a business model to a 501c3 non profit organization and the science fiction convention-committee style of leadership was reinstated. In 2017 SpoCon returned with a new science fiction convention committee and returned to the Doubletree Hotel. In 2019 the science fiction convention moved from the Spokane Doubletree Hotel to the Historic Davenport Hotel." .

