ns1:46175 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Layland v Ontario (Minister of Consumer and Commercial Relations) was a 1993 legal case brought towards the Ontario Divisional Court (Superior Court) after a same-sex couple was denied a marriage license at Ottawa City Hall. In a 2-1 decision, judges of the Ontario Divisional Court dismissed the application for an order requiring the issue of a marriage licence, ruling \"that under the common law of Canada applicable to Ontario a valid marriage can take place only between a man and a woman.\"" .

