ns1:46674 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Belgrade in 1688 was the fourth siege of that city, taking place during the Great Turkish War. The Ottoman forces were commanded by Yeğen Osman who was shortly before this battle appointed to the position of governor of Belgrade. Supported by the Christian population of Ottoman Serbia, his forces landed on Ada Ciganlija, a river island near Belgrade's suburb Ostružnica. From Niš, he wrote reports about the siege to the Ottoman government requesting urgent military and financial support necessary to defend Belgrade." .

