    rdfs:label "Costa Rican parliamentary election, 2010 were held in Costa Rica on 07 February 2010. At 9:08 p.m. local time on election day, 07 February 2010 second-placed candidate Otton Solis conceded defeat to Laura Chinchilla, who will become Costa Rica's first female president. Bruce M. Wilson and Juan Carlos Rodríguez-Cordero: \"The general election in Costa Rica, 07 February 2010\"." .

ns1:46696 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Iceland–Russia relations is the relationship between the two countries, Iceland and Russia. From 1975 to 1991 a trade representative of USSR was in Iceland and Russia had one in Iceland from 1991 to 1995. Former President of Iceland Ólafur Ragnar Grímsson went to Russia from April 18, 2002 to April 24, 2002. The loan was later renegotiated to $500 million after Iceland managed to secure loans from Scandinavian countries and the International Monetary Fund, but finally Russia refused to lend any amount to Iceland. Unlike other countries who took action against Russia in response to the incident, Russia did not respond to Iceland's approach. Export from Iceland to Russia was $US 13.8 million. Russia is the 9th largest exporter to Iceland. Iceland exports to Russia ships and vessels (25,1%), sea products (23,3%), textiles and garment (14,9%), chemical fertilizers (10,8%), and industrial equipment (9,5%)." .

ns1:46699 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Director of Revenue of Missouri v. CoBank ACB, 531 U.S. 316 (2001), was a Supreme Court of the United States case decided in 2001." .

ns1:46700 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Twentieth Century Music Corp. v. Aiken, 422 U.S. 151 (1975), was an important decision of the United States Supreme Court, out of the Third Circuit, that questioned whether the reception of a copyrighted song on a radio broadcast constitutes a copyright violation if the copyright owner has only licensed the broadcaster to \"perform the composition publicly for profit\". Grounds for overturning a precedent—Twentieth Century Music Corp. v. Aiken presents a direct contradiction to the Supreme Court decision in Buck v. Jewell-LaSalle Realty Co., which held that a hotel proprietor who made broadcast music available to his hotel guests did violate the Copyright Act of 1909." .

ns1:46701 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Azerbaijan–United Kingdom relations, are foreign relations between Azerbaijan and the United Kingdom. The Embassy of the United Kingdom in Azerbaijan opened in 1992. The Azerbaijan was recognized by the United Kingdom on December 31, 1991. The first official visit of the President of Azerbaijan Heydar Aliyev to the United Kingdom was on February 22–25, 1994. The Azerbaijan-United Kingdom Inter-Parliamentary Friendship Group in Azerbaijani Parliament is chaired by Chingiz Asadullayev. At the root of economic cooperation between the Republic of Azerbaijan and the United Kingdom lies the energy industry." .

