ns1:47631 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Football League Two play-off Final, also known as the 2008 Coca-Cola League Two play-off Final due to sponsorship from Coca-Cola, was a association football match played at Wembley Stadium on 2008, at the end of the 2007–08 season. It was the fourth League Two play-off final since the Football League's 2004 rebranding and the 22nd play-off final in all at the fourth level of English association football. The match determined the fourth and final team to gain promotion from League Two to League One, and was contested by Stockport County and Rochdale A.F.C.. While Rochdale A.F.C. picked up 45 points for their final 24 games and finished the season in fifth place with 80 points. In the penalty shoot out that followed Rochdale A.F.C. scored all five of their penalties while Darlington only managed to score 4 therefore putting Rochdale A.F.C. into the play-off final. Rochdale A.F.C. were without midfielder David Perkins after he was sent off in the 2nd leg of the play off semi final against Darlington. Over 35,000 fans made the 400-mile round trip from Greater Manchester to Wembley Stadium for this classic final. Rochdale A.F.C. missed out on promotion to League One after losing in the play-off semi-final against Gillingham." .

