ns1:47991 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "O Clássico (\"The Classic\") is the name given in association football to matches between Portuguese clubs S.L. Originally, the term O Clássico only referred to games played in the league, but now tends to include matches that take place in other domestic competitions such as the Taça de Portugal, Taça da Liga and Supertaça Cândido de Oliveira. The rivalry comes about as Lisbon and Porto are the two largest cities in Portugal, and the two clubs are two of the wealthiest and most decorated association football teams in Portugal. Benfica would meet Porto for the very first time in an official match in the domestic cup competition which during the early periods of Portuguese association football was the Campeonato de Portugal." .

