    rdfs:label "A 2008 Liberal Democratic Party (Japan) leadership election was held in the Liberal Democratic Party of Japan on 2008 after the incumbent party leader and Prime Minister of Japan Yasuo Fukuda announced that he would resign on 2008, only 11 months after taking office on 25 September 2007 following a 2008 Liberal Democratic Party (Japan) leadership election on 23 September 2007. Taro Aso, who had lost to Fukuda in the 2007 2008 Liberal Democratic Party (Japan) leadership election, was widely seen as the frontrunner to replace him, and announced on 2008 he was ready to take over as party leader. Some speculated that a general election would be called on 3 October for 2008 following the 2008 Liberal Democratic Party (Japan) leadership election, but this failed to materialise." .

