ns1:48321 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Malta participated in the Malta in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016 as the host country. Prior to the 2016 Contest, Malta had participated in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest eleven times since its first entry in 2003 only opting not to participate at the 2010, 2011 and 2012 contests. Malta has won on two occasions: in 2013 when Gaia Cauchi won with the song \"The Start\", and again in 2015 when Destiny Chukunyere came first with \"Not My Soul\" when it won the contest with 185 points, breaking the previous record held by Spain for the most points ever given to a winner. The jury members were as follow (in alphabetical order): On 2016, it was revealed that Christina's song for the Malta in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016 was revealed would be entitled \"Parachute\". She represented Malta at the Malta in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016 in Valletta, Malta on 2016 with the song \"Parachute\". It represented Malta during the Malta in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016. During the opening ceremony and the running order draw which took place on 2016, Malta was drawn to perform fifth on 2016, following Russia and preceding Bulgaria. During the press conference for the Malta in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016, held in Stockholm, the Reference Group announced several changes to the voting format for the 2016 contest." .

