ns1:50175 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1947 Sun Bowl was a post-season American college football bowl game between the VPI Gobblers (now the Virginia Tech Hokies) of the Southern Conference (SoCon) and the independent Cincinnati Bearcats. It took place on 1947, at Kidd Field in El Paso. The 1947 game was also the 13th edition of the Sun Bowl, which had been played every year since 1935. The 1947 Sun Bowl game was held as the culminating event of the Sun Carnival and was held at 15,000-seat Kidd Field on the campus of Texas Western University, today known as the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP). The 1947 Sun Bowl was the Bearcats' first official bowl game, although Cincinnati played two post-season games in New Orleans following the 1897 college football season." .

