ns1:52178 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996 United States presidential election in South Dakota took place on 05 November 1996. South Dakota was won by Kansas Senator Bob Dole, who was running against incumbent United States President of the United States Bill Clinton of Arkansas. The presidential election of 1996 was a very multi-partisan election for South Dakota, with more than ten percent of the electorate voting for third-party candidates. As of the 2020 presidential election, this is the last election in which South Dakota was seriously contested, as well as the last time Beadle County, Bon Homme County, Brule County, Charles Mix County, Deuel County, Grant County, Jerauld County, Kingsbury County, Sanborn County, and Union County voted for a Democratic presidential candidate." .

