ns1:52271 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Relations between Cuba–Solomon Islands relations and the Cuba have only a short history. Like other countries in Oceania, Cuba–Solomon Islands relations is a beneficiary of Cuban medical aid; bilateral relations between Havana and Honiara must be viewed within the scope of Cuba's regional policy in Oceania. He added that such relations had been \"on the drawing board between Cuba–Solomon Islands relations and Cuba since 2000\". According to a spokesman for Cuba–Solomon Islands relations' Ministry of Health, the Solomons are \"desperately in need\" of doctors, and hence grateful to Cuba for its \"much needed assistance\". In April 2011, the Cuba–Solomon Islands relations announced they would be opening an embassy in Cuba. In March 2013, Cuba–Solomon Islands relations Ambassador Simeon Bouro became the first resident ambassador for any Pacific Island country in Cuba. At that time, there were 98 Solomon Islanders studying medicine in Cuba, and the Cuban government announced it would provide 104 scholarships for Cuba–Solomon Islands relations medical students the following year." .

