ns1:52315 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Croatia–United States relations refer to the bilateral relationship between Croatia and the United States of America. Pompeo's visit was foreshadowed by statements made by Croatia's president Zoran Milanović, who harshly criticised the U.S. top leaders, saying, among other things, that Donald Trump had ruined the international reputation of the United States of America. The United States of America and Croatia have a bilateral investment treaty and investment protection agreement. Despite Croatia having numerous direct services to the United States of America when it was part of Yugoslavia prior to the outbreak of the Yugoslav wars in the early 1990s, it wasn't until July 2019 that direct services resumed. In addition, the United States of America has given more than $27 million since 1998 in humanitarian assistance to Croatia. Media related to Relations of Croatia and the United States of America at Wikimedia Commons." .

ns1:52316 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Owen Equipment & Erection Co. v. Kroger, 437 United States Reports 365 (1978), is a case that was decided by the Supreme Court of the United States regarding the civil procedure subject of ancillary jurisdiction. Whereas the Eighth Circuit relied on United Mine Workers of America v. Gibbs, 383 United States Reports 715 (1966), the Supreme Court in its 7 to 2 majority decision written by Justice Potter Stewart limited Gibbs to pendent jurisdiction, bringing state claims in addition to a federal claim." .

