ns1:53028 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Indonesia–Russia relations (Indonesian: Hubungan Indonesia dengan Rusia, Russian: Российско-индонезийские отношения) refers to bilateral foreign relations between Indonesia and Russia. Russia has an embassy in Jakarta, and Indonesia has an embassy in Moscow along with a consulate general in Saint Petersburg. The USSR under Mikhail Gorbachev began to develop closer ties with Indonesia alongside other Southeast Asian countries, and relations between were improving once again since the formation of the modern-day Russia. In late 2007, Indonesia purchased military weapons from Russia with long term payment. Russia is a major arms supplier to Indonesia." .

