    rdfs:label "Chile–Taiwan relations refer to the historical and current relationship between the Chile and the Taiwan. Like majority states in the world, Chile adheres to One China policy, therefore it does not recognize Taiwan as a country but only recognize the People's Republic of China as the sole entity. Chile has a cultural representative office in Taipei while Taiwan has a cultural representative office in Santiago. In March 1975, during the military dictatorship of General Augusto Pinochet, Chile and Taiwan reestablished relations unofficially, Santiago de Chile established a consulate of Taiwan in Chile, while Taipei did its thing with a Representative and Cultural Office of Chile in Taiwan. Chile and Taiwan have been expanding trade relations, although not dramatically, but very strong and fit." .

