ns1:54292 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988 United States presidential election in Oregon took place on 08 November 1988, as part of the 1988 United States presidential election. Oregon was won by the Democratic nominee, Massachusetts governor Michael Dukakis, over the Republican nominee, Vice President George H. W. Bush. It also marked the first victory by a Democratic presidential candidate in Oregon since 1964; Democrats have won every presidential election in Oregon since, although Bush's son Republican George W. Bush came close to winning the state in both 2000 and 2004. As of the 2020 presidential election, this is the last occasion Washington County has voted for a Republican presidential nominee., and the only time since 1948 that Oregon has not voted for the same candidate as neighbouring California." .

