ns1:54365 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sin Piedad (Spanish for \"No Mercy\") was an annual professional wrestling major event produced by Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), which took place on December 16, 2011, in Arena México, Mexico City and replaced CMLL's regular Friday night show Super Viernes (\"Super Friday\"). The 2011 Sin Piedad was the tenth event under that name that CMLL promoted as their last major show of the year, always held in December. All Sin Piedad shows have been held in Arena México in Mexico City which is CMLL's main venue, its \"home\". The event featured six professional wrestling matches with different wrestlers involved in pre-existing scripted feuds, plots and storylines. The incident led to the Distrito Federal Box y Lucha Commission announcing that Panther was suspended for two weeks, but that the suspension would not start until after the Sin Piedad event. On January 1, 2012, the rookies Hombre Bala Jr. and Super Halcón Jr. would defeat the veteran team of Los Rayos Tapatio, who then had to unmask as per the Luchas de Apuestas stipulation the two teams agreed on during the Sin Piedad event." .

