    rdfs:label "Toronto After Dark Film Festival is a showcase of horror, sci-fi, action and cult cinema held annually in Toronto, Canada. The inaugural festival was held October 20–24, 2006, at the Bloor Cinema in Toronto, Canada. Toronto After Dark announced the first eight Official Selections of its 2011 film line-up at Fan Expo Canada on August 25, 2011, then on its official website on August 31, 2011. The 2013 Toronto After Dark Film Festival Official Selections included the Opening Gala film and Toronto Premiere of Jim Mickle's We Are What We Are. This marked a return to Toronto After Dark for Mickle, as his 2006 film, Mulberry Street was a previous Toronto After Dark Official Selection. The 2014 Toronto After Dark Film Festival Official Selections included the Opening Gala film and Toronto premiere of Gerard Johnstone's Housebound." .

