ns1:56604 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1952 steel strike was a strike by the United Steelworkers of America against U.S. Steel and nine other steelmakers. The strike was scheduled to begin on 1952, but US President Harry Truman nationalized the United States of America steel industry hours before the workers walked out. The strike lasted 53 days and ended on 1952 on essentially the same terms that the union had proposed four months earlier. The union's strike committee declined to give Murray the authority to sign a wage pact without approval of the union's membership, and set its next meeting for 1952." .

