ns1:56725 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 United States presidential election in Texas took place on 02 November 2004, and was part of the 2004 United States presidential election. Texas was won by incumbent President of the United States George W. Bush by a 22.87% margin of victory. Prior to the election, all 12 news organizations considered Texas as a safe red state for President of the United States Bush. As of the 2020 presidential election, Texas has not voted for a Democratic candidate in a U.S. presidential election since Jimmy Carter's victory in 1976. Although John Kerry lost Texas, this is the last time, as of the 2020 presidential election, the Democratic candidate lost the state with less than 40% of the vote or a Republican has broken 60% of the vote in the Lone Star State." .

