    rdfs:label "The Fitzsimmons vs. Sharkey Heavyweight Championship boxing between Bob Fitzsimmons and Tom Sharkey was awarded by referee Wyatt Earp to Sharkey after Fitzsimmons knocked Sharkey to the mat. It was the first heavyweight championship fight since James J. Corbett, the prior champion, had retired from boxing the year before. He lived in San Francisco and promoted his protege, Australian Steve O'Donnell, as the next candidate for the heavyweight title, but he had been knocked out within the first minute by Peter Maher, who in turn was knocked out in the first round by Bob Fitzsimmons. He said that the San Francisco supervisors had no right to license a boxing, and that the license they issued was an illegal attempt to disobey the law." .

