ns1:58190 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 United States presidential election in New York took place on 07 November 2000 as part of the 2000 United States presidential election. New York was won by the Incumbent Democratic Vice President of the United States Al Gore in a landslide victory; Gore received 60.22% of the vote to Republican George W. Bush's 35.22%, a Democratic victory margin of 25.00%. Al Gore won an overwhelming landslide in fiercely Democratic New York City, taking 1,703,364 votes to George W. Bush's 398,726, a 77.90% - 18.23% victory." .

