ns1:58262 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Cold War (1962–1979) refers to the phase within the Cold War that spanned the period between the aftermath of the Cuban Missile Crisis in late 1962, through the détente period beginning in 1969, to the end of détente in the late 1970s. The breakaway white government retained power in Rhodesia until 1979, despite a United Nations embargo and a devastating civil war with two rival guerrilla factions backed by the Soviets and Chinese, respectively." .

