ns1:59423 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Australia participated in the Australia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017 with the song \"Don't Come Easy\" written by Anthony Egizii, David Musumeci and Michael Angelo. Australia was drawn to compete in the first semi-final of the Eurovision Song Contest which took place on 2017. On 1 November 2016, SBS confirmed Australia's participation in the 2017 Eurovision Song Contest after securing an invitation for the third year in a row. Isaiah Firebrace and \"Don't Come Easy\" were announced as the artist and song that would represent Australia at the Australia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017 on 2017. Australia was placed into the first semi-final, to be held on 2017, and was scheduled to perform in the first half of the show. Below is a breakdown of points awarded to Australia and awarded by Australia in the first semi-final and grand final of the contest, and the breakdown of the jury voting and televoting conducted during the two shows: The following five members will comprise the Australian jury: On 2017, it was announced that Natasha Cuppit had replaced Jordan Raskopoulos as a member of the Australian jury." .

