ns1:60526 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Derby de la Côte d'Azur is a association football match contested between Ligue 1 clubs AS Monaco and OGC Nice. The name of the derby derives from the fact that Monaco and Nice are the two major clubs in France that are situated on or near the Côte d'Azur, known in English as the French Riviera. Furthermore, Nice and Monaco have competed many years together in Division 1, including nine years in-a-row from 2002 to 2011 and both are among the most important association football clubs in France (Nice won 4 championships and 3 cups, while Monaco won 8 championships and 5 cups)." .

