ns1:61863 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIFA Beach Soccer World Cup qualification (CONMEBOL) (natively in Spanish: Eliminatorias CONMEBOL al Mundial de la FIFA de Fútbol Playa), also previously known as the South American Beach Soccer Championship (Spanish: Sudamericano de Fútbol Playa), is the main championship for beach soccer in South America, contested between the senior men's national teams of the CONMEBOL. The first edition was proceeded by a joint qualification tournament with CONMEBOL in 2005; a second and final joint event was held in 2007. In 2013, CONMEBOL began reporting on the event using the aforementioned Sudamericano title (which the tournament became informally known as) before taking organisational control under a new title in 2017. Since 2016, the Copa América has also been staged by CONMEBOL; however it is not used a qualification tournament to the World Cup." .

