ns1:41340 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 United States presidential election in Vermont took place on 08 November 1932, as part of the 1932 United States presidential election which was held throughout all contemporary 48 states. Vermont voted for the Republican nominee, incumbent President of the United States Herbert Hoover of California, over the Democratic nominee, Governor Franklin Delano Roosevelt of New York. Vermont historically was a bastion of liberal Northeastern Republicanism, and by 1932 the Green Mountain State had gone Republican in every presidential election since the founding of the Republican Party. From 1856 to 1928 United States presidential election in Vermont, Vermont had had the longest streak of voting Republican of any state, having never voted Democratic before, and this tradition continued even in the midst of a nationwide Democratic landslide in 1932." .

ns1:41345 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Japan Cuts is an annual festival of modern Japanese cinema held at New York City's Japan Society (Manhattan). The festival was first held in 2007, growing out of the Japan Society (Manhattan)'s popular bi-annual series, New Films from Japan. The year 2007 marked not only the launch of JAPAN CUTS, but also the first time Japan Society (Manhattan)'s film department teamed with the New York Asian Film Festival (NYAFF). JAPAN CUTS was founded in 2007 by Japan Society (Manhattan)'s Artistic Director Yoko Shioya with Film Program Officer Ryo Nagasawa, and programmed by Nagasawa through 2009." .

ns1:41350 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Gallant Bloom Handicap is a Grade III American Thoroughbred horse race for fillies and mares that are three years old and older run over a distance of 6 1⁄2 furlongs on the dirt held annually in late September at Belmont Park in Elmont, New York. The following year the event was not held but was resumed in 1994 at Belmont Park with handicap conditions for three-year-old and older fillies and mares to enter." .

ns1:41351 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Tayacoba, 30 June 1898, (also spelled Tayabacao) was an American special operations effort to land supplies and reinforcements to Cuban rebels fighting for their independence in the Spanish–American War." .

