ns1:41386 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sublimis Deus (English: The sublime God; erroneously cited as Sublimus Dei and occasionally as Sic Dilexit) is a papal bull promulgated by Pope Paul III on June 2, 1537, which forbids the enslavement of the indigenous peoples of the Americas (called Indians of the West and the South) and all other people. While some scholars see Sublimis Deus as a primary example of Papal advocacy of Indian rights, others see it as part of an inconsistent and politically convenient stance by Paul III, who later rescinded Sublimis Deus or the Pastorale in 1538. In Sublimis Deus, Paul III unequivocally declares the indigenous peoples of the Americas to be rational beings with souls, denouncing any idea to the contrary as directly inspired by the \"enemy of the human race\" (Satan). According to Falkowski (2002) Sublimis Deus had the effect of revoking Pope Alexander VI's papal bull Inter caetera but still leaving the colonizers the duty of converting the native people." .

ns1:41395 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Kaunas was laid by the Teutonic Order on the newly built Kaunas Castle in spring 1362." .

ns1:41396 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 AFC Futsal Club Championship was the 9th edition of the Asian Football Confederation Futsal Club Championship, an annual international futsal club tournament in Asia organised by the Asian Football Confederation (Asian Football Confederation). Of the 47 Asian Football Confederation member associations, a total of 16 associations teams entered the competition, each entering one team. All 14 associations which participated in the 2017 AFC Futsal Club Championship returned for 2018." .

