    rdfs:label "New Hollywood, sometimes referred to as the American New Wave or the Hollywood Renaissance, refers to a movement in cinema of the United States from the mid-1960s to the early 1980s, when a new generation of young filmmakers came to prominence in the United States." .

ns1:41431 a ns1:context_narration ;
