ns1:41435 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election was held on 07 November 2006 and included the races for the Governor of Pennsylvania and Lieutenant Governor of Pennsylvania. Ed Rendell and Knoll had the advantage of incumbency, important in the swing state of Pennsylvania. They also pointed out that no Pennsylvania governor had lost re-election since the 1950s, and that, as a sitting governor, Ed Rendell had all of the traditional advantages of an incumbent." .

ns1:41437 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Analytical Engine was a proposed mechanical general-purpose computer designed by English mathematician and computer pioneer Charles Babbage, with the assistance of Ada Lovelace. The Analytical Engine is one of the most successful achievements of Charles Babbage. The work on the design of the Analytical Engine started in c. 1833." .

ns1:41438 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Wilson-Kautz Raid was a cavalry operation in south central Virginia in late 22 June 1864, during the American Civil War." .

ns1:41441 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "war bond are debt securities issued by a government to finance military operations and other expenditure in times of war." .

ns1:41443 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1928 Summer Olympics – men's 110 metres hurdles event at the 1928 Olympic Games took place between 31 July 1928 & 01 August 1928." .

ns1:41447 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Clyde Engineering Co Ltd v Cowburn, is a High Court of Australia case about inconsistency between a Commonwealth and a State law, which is dealt with in s 109 of the Australian Constitution." .

ns1:41449 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 LSU Tigers baseball team represents Louisiana State University in the NCAA Division I baseball season of 2013. The following members and future members (denoted by *) of the LSU Tigers baseball program were drafted in the 2013 MLB Draft." .

ns1:41452 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 California Attorney General election occurred on 03 November 1998. The Democratic nominee, Bill Lockyer, defeated the Republican nominee, Dave Stirling, for the office previously held by incumbent Dan Lungren, who chose not to seek re-election in favor of running for governor." .

ns1:41457 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Seville (July 1247 – 30 November 1248) was a 16-month successful investment during the Reconquista of Seville by forces of Ferdinand III of Castile." .

ns1:41472 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 916, adopted unanimously on 05 May 1994, after reaffirming Resolution 782 (1992) and all subsequent resolutions on Mozambique, the Council decided to renew the mandate of the United Nations Operation in Mozambique (ONUMOZ) for a final period ending 15 November 1994, and discussed the implementation of the Rome General Peace Accords." .

ns1:41473 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Trophée Eric Bompard was the fourth event of six in the 2008–09 ISU Grand Prix of Figure Skating, a senior-level international invitational competition series. It was held at the Accor Arena in Paris on 13 November 2008–16." .

ns1:41476 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1904 Samos earthquake struck Greece on 11 August 1904 with moment magnitude of 6.8 and a maximum Mercalli intensity of X (Extreme)." .

ns1:41489 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1929 Norwegian Football Cup was the 28th season of the Norway annual knockout association football tournament. The tournament was open for all members of Norwegian Football Federation, except those from Northern Norway. The final was played at Stavanger Stadion in Stavanger on 1929, and was contested by the defending champions Ørn and Sarpsborg FK, who had last won the tournament in 1917. Sarpsborg FK won the final 2-1 after extra time, and secured their second Norway Cup championship." .

ns1:41492 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Temalaca was a battle of the Mexican War of Independence that occurred on 05 November 1815 in the area around Temalaca, Puebla. At the end of the battle, Morelos was captured by Spanish forces under whose control he was soon after executed ending the second phase of the Mexican War of Independence." .

ns1:41493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Facebook, Inc. v. Power Ventures, Inc. is a lawsuit brought by Facebook, Inc. in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California alleging that Power Ventures Inc., a third-party platform, collected user information from Facebook, Inc. and displayed it on their own website." .

ns1:41499 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pearson Cup (French: Coupe Pearson) was an annual midseason Major League Baseball rivalry between former Canadian rivals, the Toronto Blue Jays and Montreal Expos. Named after former Prime Minister Lester B. Pearson, it was originally created to raise money for minor league baseball in Canada." .

ns1:41500 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Clásica de San Sebastián, the 28th edition of the Clásica de San Sebastián road bicycle racing took place on 02 August 2008 in Spain and was won by Spaniard Alejandro Valverde of Caisse d'Epargne in a sprint finish on the Donostia avenue. He held off Russian Alexandr Kolobnev of Team CSC Saxo Bank and Italian Davide Rebellin of Gerolsteiner, from a group that had shrunk to less than 15 riders." .

ns1:41501 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Swiss Super League was the 118th season of top-tier association football in Switzerland. It began on 19 July 2014 and ended on 29 May 2015. A total of 10 teams competed in the league, the 9 best teams from the 2013–14 Swiss Super League and the 2013–14 Swiss Challenge League champion FC Vaduz." .

ns1:41507 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The United States at the 2015 Pan American Games in Toronto, Canada, from July 10 to 26, 2015. The United States women's national baseball team announced their roster for the 2015 ParaAmerican Games on 2015." .

ns1:41512 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985 Samoa National League, or also known as the Upolo First Division, was the 7th edition of the Samoa National League, the top league of the Football Federation Samoa." .

ns1:41520 a ns1:context_narration ;
