ns1:41522 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1984 United States presidential election in Massachusetts took place on 06 November 1984, as part of the 1984 United States presidential election, which was held throughout all 50 states and D.C. Massachusetts narrowly voted for incumbent Republican President of the United States Ronald Reagan of California over his Democratic challenger, former Vice President of the United States Walter Mondale of Minnesota." .

ns1:41533 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Molleindustria is an Italian guerrilla semiotics and culture jamming website that produces flash videogames based on provocative left-wing socio-political points of view, like on topics like labour market flexibility and Queer theory, in explicit opposition with the mainstream video game industry." .

ns1:41542 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Anime Expo, abbreviated AX, is an American anime convention held in Los Angeles, California and organized by the non-profit Society for the Promotion of Japanese Animation (SPJA). Anime Expo Tokyo (AX Tokyo) was held in 2004 at the Sunshine City Convention Center in Ikebukuro, Tokyo, Japan." .

ns1:41543 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Hurricane Sandra was the latest-forming major hurricane in the Northeast Pacific tropical cyclone, the strongest November Pacific hurricane on record, and the record eleventh major hurricane of the 2015 Pacific hurricane season." .

ns1:41548 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 Al-Oruba F.C. season is the Al-Oruba Football Club of Yemen season from 2011–2012 season." .

ns1:41553 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Commando (Air Ministry serial number AL504) was a very long range Consolidated Liberator II aircraft adapted for passenger transport, to serve as the personal aircraft of Prime Minister Winston Churchill. On delivery Commando had a regular Liberator nose and tail configuration despite the internal modifications but was later converted to have a covered nose and also the same single tail fin used on the Consolidated PB4Y-2. After the second extended trip, Churchill never again flew in Commando, instead switching to Ascalon, an Avro York (a transport aircraft based on the Lancaster bomber, with a larger fuselage) with an all-British crew. Commando had served as Churchill's official aircraft during a critical period and later in the war was also used on occasion by other VIP's for their business in connection with the war effort. Commando was the second of 139 VLR (Very Long Range) Liberator II aircraft delivered to the RAF mostly to be used by RAF Coastal Command on maritime patrol duty and anti-submarine warfare, escorting the supply convoys of merchant vessels and attacking and sinking German U-boats. Winston Churchill's former personal transport Commando was assigned as the VIP aircraft. When Commando failed to arrive at Lagens Field emergency calls were made by radio and air-sea searches initiated once the aircraft was classified as overdue. Close to the flight path which Commando would have been following over the ocean in towards Lagens Field aircrew of the searching RAF Coastal Command aircraft spotted some yellow dinghies, a small amount of wreckage and an oil patch on the surface." .

ns1:41572 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 RBC Pro Challenge was a professional tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It took place in Tyler, United States, on 2017–05 November 2017." .

ns1:41579 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Burkhanism or Ak Jang (Altay: Ак јаҥ), is a new religious movement that flourished among the indigenous people of Russia's Gorno-Altai region (okrug) between 1904 and the 1930s. The Altaian name for the religion is Ak Jang (\"White Faith\")." .

ns1:41582 a ns1:context_narration ;
