ns1:41763 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Thai Premier League (also known as Toyota Thai Premier League due to the sponsorship from Toyota) was the 19th season of the Thai Premier League since its establishment in 1996. Buriram United F.C. were the defending champions, having won their Thai Premier League title the 2014 Thai Premier League. A total of 18 teams contested the league, including 15 sides from the 2014 Thai Premier League and three promoted from the 2014 Thai Division 1 League. Police United, PTT Rayong, Songkhla United, Air Force Central and GSE Samut Songkhram were relegated to the 2015 Thai Division 1 League after finishing the 2014 Thai Premier League." .

ns1:41771 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The alpine skiing at the 2018 Winter Olympics – men's super-G competition of the alpine skiing at the 2018 Winter Olympics was held on 16 February 2018 at the Jeongseon Alpine Centre in PyeongChang." .

ns1:41772 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Damehåndboldligaen (known as the Boxer Dameligaen for sponsorship reasons) is the 79th season of the Danish Women's Handball League, Denmark's premier handball league. The following 12 clubs compete in the Danish Women's Handball League during the 2014–15 season: Following is the list of clubs competing in 2014–15 Damehåndboldligaen, with their manager, captain, kit manufacturer and shirt sponsor." .

ns1:41779 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "At the Battle of Taginae (also known as the Battle of Busta Gallorum) in June/July 552, the forces of the Byzantine Empire under Narses broke the power of the Ostrogoths in Italy, and paved the way for the temporary Byzantine reconquest of the Italian Peninsula. Having failed to turn Narses' position, and expecting 2,000 reinforcements from Teia, Totila used various expedients to delay the battle, including disingenuous offers of negotiation and duels enacted between the battle-lines. The course and duration of the subsequent battle are uncertain, but towards early evening Narses ordered a general advance, and the Ostrogoths broke and fled." .

ns1:41780 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cephalonia was a naval battle fought between the Byzantine and Aghlabid fleets near Kefalonia, off the western coast of Greece. John Skylitzes reports that it numbered sixty \"exceedingly large\" ships, and that it raided the Ionian Islands of Zakynthos and Kefalonia. Thanks to favourable wind, the fleet soon reached the port of Methone on the southern tip of Greece, but there was forced to halt, as many of the fleet's oarsmen had deserted in small groups out of fear of the impending battle." .

ns1:41782 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Treeing is a method of hunting where dogs are used to force animals that naturally climb up into trees, where they can be assessed or shot by hunting. Treeing is considered an undignified hunting practice and illegal in many places. Treeing is illegal at least in: Natural spaces law enforcement officers urged hunting or outdoor enthusiasts to call police and report any suspicious activity they witness." .

ns1:41786 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 NACAC Cross Country Championships took place on 11 March 2006. The races were held at the United States of America Triathlon National Training Center in Clermont, Florida, United States of America." .

ns1:41789 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1982 Irish Masters was the eighth edition of the professional invitational snooker tournament, which took place from 24 to 28 March 1982 1992." .

ns1:41791 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hausbergen took place on 08 March 1262 and marks the freeing of the city of Strasbourg from episcopal authority. The battle began with a challenge to single combat by the knight Marcus of Eckwersheim from the army of Strasbourg. Strasbourg was a free city of the Holy Roman Empire and its future was entrusted to its Council." .

ns1:41805 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 United States Senate election in Minnesota was held on 07 November 2000 to select the U.S. The race pitted incumbent Republican Senator Rod Grams against former Minnesota State Auditor Mark Dayton." .

ns1:41806 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Prairie II was a U.S. military operation in Quảng Trị Province, South Vietnam that sought to eliminate People's Army of Vietnam (PAVN) forces south of the Vietnamese Demilitarized Zone (DMZ) that took place from 1 February to 18 March 1967. Operation Prairie II concluded on 18 March 1967, the Marines had lost 93 killed, 483 wounded and claiming 694 PAVN killed and 20 captured 137 individual weapons were recovered during the campaign." .

ns1:41807 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Primeira Liga (also known as Liga NOS for sponsorship reasons) was the 82nd season of the Primeira Liga, the top professional league for Portuguese association football clubs. The season began on 14 15 August 2015 and concluded on 15 May 2016. For the second consecutive season, the league was contested by a total of 18 teams, which included the best 16 sides from the 2014–15 Primeira Liga and two promoted from the 2014–15 Segunda Liga." .

ns1:41811 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Japan Expo is a convention on Japanese popular culture - the largest of its kind in the world outside Japan - taking place in Paris, France, although it has branched out into a partnership festival - Kultima - and expanded to include some European and US pop culture as well. It is held yearly at the beginning of July for four days (usually from Thursday to Sunday) in the Parc des Expositions de Villepinte (the second-largest convention center in France). The first exposition took place in 1999 at the ISC Paris Business School and welcomed 2,400 visitors, a number which has grown steadily. In 2002, Japan Expo was hosted at the Center of New Industries and Technologies (CNIT) in La Défense, Paris. Other than the main convention in Paris, Japan Expo has expanded to 4 cities in 3 countries on 2 continents:" .

ns1:41814 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 World Championships in Athletics, under the auspices of the World Athletics, were held in the Mercedes-Benz Arena, Stuttgart, Germany between 13 August 1993 and 22 August 1993 with the participation of 187 nations. At subsequent Championships the race was replaced by the longer 5000 m. 1987 | 1991 World Championships in Athletics | 1993 | 1995 World Championships in Athletics | 1997. 1987 | 1991 World Championships in Athletics | 1993 | 1995 World Championships in Athletics | 1997. 1987 |1991 World Championships in Athletics |1993 |1995 World Championships in Athletics |1997. 1987 |1991 World Championships in Athletics |1993 |1995 World Championships in Athletics |1997." .

ns1:41817 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1989 Luxembourg general election were held in Luxembourg on 18 June 1989." .

ns1:41818 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1935 Emperor's Cup Final was the 15th final of the Emperor's Cup competition. The final was played at Meiji Jingu Gaien Stadium in Tokyo on 1935." .

ns1:41823 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "During the Siege of Genoa (1800) (1800 – 04 June 1800) the Austrians siege and captured Genoa. However, Napoleon needed time in order to bring his troops in Italy so he ordered Massena to hold Nice and Genoa at all costs until he arrived. Describing the situation at Genoa, Ott requested and received permission to continue the siege. On 04 June 1800, Masséna's negotiator finally agreed to evacuate the French army from Genoa. By forcing the Austrians to deploy vast forces against him at Genoa, Masséna made it possible for Bonaparte to cross the Great St Bernard Pass, surprise the Austrians, and ultimately defeat General Michael Melas's army at Marengo before sufficient reinforcements could be transferred from the siege site." .

ns1:41825 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Vissel Kobe season was Vissel Kobe's fourth consecutive season in the J1 League and their 19th J1 League season overall." .

ns1:41827 a ns1:context_narration ;
