ns1:41834 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 827, adopted unanimously on 25 May 1993, after reaffirming Resolution 713 (1991) and all subsequent resolutions on the topic of the former Yugoslavia, approved report S/25704 of Secretary-General Boutros Boutros-Ghali, with the Statute of the International Tribunal as an annex, establishing the International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia (ICTY)." .

ns1:41838 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bath International Music Festival was held late each spring in Bath, South West England between 1948 and 2016. The Bath International Music Festival is organized by Bath Festivals Ltd., a long-established charitably registered independent arts company with charitable status. It receives core funding from Bath and North East Somerset Council (B&NES) and Arts Council England. Since 1981, the Bath Fringe Festival has taken place at the same time as the music festival." .

ns1:41839 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 13 November 1943 was a submarine engagement of World War II. On the morning of 13 November 1943, 30 miles (48 km) off Penang the officer of the watch on Taurus sighted the large submarine I-34 running on the surface at fourteen knots despite a rain squall." .

ns1:41842 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 166, adopted on 25 October 1961, after examining the application of the Mongolian People's Republic for membership in the United Nations the Council recommended to the General Assembly that the Mongolian People's Republic be admitted." .

ns1:41844 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Anglo-Italian Cup (Italian: Coppa Anglo-Italiana, also known as the Anglo-Italian Inter-League Clubs Competition and from 1976–86 as the Alitalia Challenge Cup, Talbot Challenge Cup or Gigi Peronace Memorial) is a defunct European football competition. The competition was played intermittently between 1970 and 1996 between clubs from England and Italy. The initial Anglo-Italian Cup was played as an annual tournament from 1970 to 1973. Following the popularity of that event, dubbed the Anglo-Italian League Cup, and as a way to generate income to pay players' wages during the extended close season caused by the 1970 FIFA World Cup, the first Anglo-Italian Cup was inaugurated in 1970. It was a professional tournament for teams competing in the second tier of association football—the newly renamed First Division in England and Serie B in Italy." .

ns1:41869 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 U.S. Open was the 99th U.S. Open, held June 17–20 at Pinehurst Resort Course No. Payne Stewart won his second U.S. Open and third major championship, one stroke ahead of runner-up Phil Mickelson. This was the first U.S. Open at Pinehurst, which returned in 2005 and 2014." .

ns1:41874 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Connecticut–Georgetown men's basketball rivalry is an American college basketball rivalry between the UConn Huskies men's basketball team of the University of Connecticut and Georgetown Hoyas men's basketball team of Georgetown University." .

ns1:41876 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1974 Spanish Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 28 April 1974 at the Circuito del Jarama near Madrid, Spain." .

ns1:41886 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ask a Stupid Question Day is a holiday that is sometimes celebrated in the United States, usually by school students and teachers. Although Ask a Stupid Question Day's default date is September 28, in practice it is usually observed on the last school day of September." .

ns1:41887 a ns1:context_narration ;
