ns1:41916 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The World Conference on Women, 1980 or the Second World Conference on Women took place between 1980 and 1980 in Copenhagen, Denmark as the mid-decade assessment of progress and failure in implementing the goals established by the World Plan of Action at the 1975 inaugural conference on women. The 1980 Conference held from 14 July and 30 July in Copenhagen, Denmark was the direct result of the World Conference on Women, 1975, which had been held in Mexico City in 1975, establishing the World Plan of Action and Declaration of Mexico on the Equality of Women and Their Contribution to Development and Peace." .

ns1:41920 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "death of Nqobile Nzuza was a resident in the Marikana Land Occupation in Cato Crest, Durban, South Africa." .

ns1:41924 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Wladimir Klitschko vs. Ruslan Chagaev, billed as \"Knockout Auf Schalke\", was a professional boxing match contested on 20 June 2009 for the IBF, WBO, IBO, The Ring and lineal heavyweight championship. He had agreed to face former unified cruiserweight champion David Haye in Germany on 20 June 2009, but Haye withdrew because of a back injury. Veltins Arena with capacity of over 61,000 seats was sold out, making the audience the biggest for boxing in Germany since 1939, when Max Schmeling knocked out Adolf Heuser in front of 70,000 people in Stuttgart." .

