ns1:41968 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Bolimów was an inconclusive battle of World War I fought on 31 January 1915 between Germany and Russian Empire and considered a preliminary to the Second Battle of the Masurian Lakes. The German Ninth Army led by August von Mackensen attacked the Russian Second Army, under General Smirnov, near the Congress Poland village of Bolimów, lying on the railway line connecting Łódź and Warsaw." .

ns1:41975 a ns1:context_narration ;
