ns1:41989 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In software quality assurance, software performance testing is in general a software testing practice performed to determine how a system performs in terms of responsiveness and stability under a particular workload. Load software testing is the simplest form of software performance testing. Isolation software testing is not unique to software performance testing but involves repeating a test execution that resulted in a system problem. To ensure consistent results, the software performance testing environment should be isolated from other environments, such as user acceptance software testing (UAT) or development. This is true in the case of functional software testing, but even more so with software performance testing, due to the end-to-end nature of its scope. Performance software testing is mainly divided into two main categories: This part of software performance testing mainly deals with creating/scripting the work flows of key identified business processes." .

ns1:41999 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 LPGA Championship was the 37th Women's PGA Championship, played June 27–30 at Bethesda Country Club in Bethesda, a suburb northwest of Washington, D.C. Meg Mallon shot a final round 67 (−4) to win the first of her four major titles, one stroke ahead of runners-up Pat Bradley and Ayako Okamoto." .

ns1:42002 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "MegaCon was founded by James Breitbiel and first held in 1993. On April 7, 2015, it was announced that MegaCon had been sold to Informa." .

