ns1:42022 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Massachusetts gubernatorial election took place on 2018, to elect the Governor of Massachusetts and lieutenant Governor of Massachusetts of the Massachusetts. Baker was reelected with the highest vote total in the history of Massachusetts gubernatorial elections and by the widest margin since Bill Weld was reelected Governor of Massachusetts in 1994. GOP state committeeman Robert Cappucci told the Boston Herald that if Baker \"shuns conservatives there will be 100 percent an effort to try to find a conservative, viable candidate to challenge him in 2018 for Governor of Massachusetts\". David Kopacz, the president of the Massachusetts Republican Assembly, has also stated that Baker may face a conservative challenger in 2018. Samantha Lachman of The Huffington Post also identified Healey as a potential candidate for Governor of Massachusetts in 2018 or in a future United States Senate race." .

ns1:42033 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "tennis at the 2006 Asian Games – men's singles at the 2006 Asian Games was won by Danai Udomchoke of Thailand." .

ns1:42039 a ns1:context_narration ;
