ns1:42126 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In finance, a Convertible bond or convertible note or convertible debt (or a convertible debenture if it has a maturity of greater than 10 years) is a type of bond that the holder can convert into a specified number of shares of common stock in the issuing company or cash of equal value. To compensate for having additional value through the option to convert the bond to stock, a Convertible bond typically has a coupon rate lower than that of similar, non-convertible debt. These properties—and the fact that convertible bond trade often below fair value—lead naturally to the idea of convertible arbitrage, where a long position in the Convertible bond is balanced by a short position in the underlying equity. Any Convertible bond structure, on top of its type, would bear a certain range of additional features as defined in its issuance prospectus: Convertibles could bear other more technical features depending on the issuer needs: Due to their relative complexity, Convertible bond investors could refer to the following terms while describing convertible bond: The global Convertible bond market is relatively small, with about 400 bn USD (as of Jan 2013, excluding synthetics), as a comparison the straight corporate bond market would be about 14,000 bn USD. Out-the-money CB's are considered as being within Area of Debt (the left hand side of the diagram) From a valuation perspective, a Convertible bond consists of two assets: a bond and a warrant." .

ns1:42133 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 5th Daytime Emmy Awards were held on Wednesday, 1978, on ABC, to commemorate excellence in American daytime programming from the previous year (1977). The awards were hosted by Family Feud host Richard Dawson, who also won an award for best game show host." .

ns1:42134 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 Pontins Professional was the twenty-first edition of the professional invitational snooker tournament which took place in 07 May 1994 in Prestatyn, Wales." .

ns1:42143 a ns1:context_narration ;
