ns1:42278 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 DFL-Supercup was the seventh edition of the German Super Cup under the name DFL-Supercup, an annual football match contested by the winners of the previous season's Bundesliga and DFB-Pokal competitions. The match was played on 2016 at the Westfalenstadion in Dortmund. It featured FC Bayern Munich, the winners of the 2015–16 Bundesliga (and the 2015–16 DFB-Pokal), who had lost the three previous super cups and last won in 2012, and 2015–16 Bundesliga runners-up Borussia Dortmund, who last won in 2014. FC Bayern Munich won the DFL-Supercup 2–0 for their fifth title." .

ns1:42285 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 PGA Tour Latinoamérica was the sixth season of PGA Tour Latinoamérica, having converted from the Tour de las Américas which ceased to operate in 2012." .

ns1:42306 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 UEFA Super Cup was a association football match between German team Bayern Munich and English team Liverpool F.C. on 2001 at Stade Louis II, the annual UEFA Super Cup contested between the winners of the UEFA Champions League and UEFA Cup. Bayern won the 2000–01 UEFA Champions League, defeating Valencia 5–4 in a penalty shoot-out after the match had finished 1–1. Liverpool F.C. won the 2000–01 UEFA Cup, beating Deportivo Alavés 5–4. Liverpool F.C. scored immediately after the start of the second half to lead the match 3–0 after Michael Owen scored. Hasan Salihamidžić and Carsten Jancker scored in the second half, but Liverpool F.C. held out until the end of the match to win 3–2, their second Super Cup win. They had won the 2000–01 UEFA Champions League beating Valencia 5–4 in a penalty shoot-out after the match had finished 1–1. Liverpool F.C. had played two legs in the third qualifying round of the 2001–02 UEFA Champions League. As winners of the 2000–01 FA Cup, Liverpool F.C. faced Manchester United in the 2001 FA Charity Shield, which they won 2–1. Liverpool F.C. had also played one match in the 2001–02 FA Premier League; a 2–1 win over West Ham United. Hamann passed the ball to Heskey on the edge of the Bayern penalty area, Heskey subsequently moved past Bayern defender's Thomas Linke and Kovač, and shot low beyond Kahn to give Liverpool F.C. a 2–0 lead. No further goals were scored and the referee blew for full-time with the final score 3–2 to Liverpool F.C.." .

ns1:42312 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Singapore participated in the Singapore at the 2009 Asian Indoor Games held in Hanoi, Vietnam on 2009 – 2009." .

ns1:42314 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Malaysian Grand Prix (formally the II Petronas Malaysian Grand Prix) was a Formula One motor race held on 22 October 2000 at the Sepang International Circuit, in Sepang. It was the 17th and final race of the 2000 Formula One season, and the second Malaysian Grand Prix. The 56-lap race was won by Ferrari driver Michael Schumacher after starting from pole position. Mika Häkkinen, driving for McLaren, started from second position alongside Michael Schumacher. Michael Schumacher managed to hold off Coulthard and crossed the finish line on lap 56 to secure his ninth victory of the season in a time of 1'35:54.235, at an average speed of 120.648 miles per hour (194.164 km/h)." .

