ns1:42670 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pine Lake tornado was a deadly tornado in central Alberta which occurred on Friday, 14 July 2000 and struck a campground and a trailer park. Twelve people were killed, making it the first deadly tornado in Canada since 1987, when an F4 tornado killed 27 people in Edmonton, Alberta and injured 300+. On 14 July 2000 at approximately 7 PM, an F3 tornado tore through the Green Acres Campground at Pine Lake in central Alberta, killing 12 people and critically injuring more than 100 others. Canada ranks second in the world for tornado occurrences after the United States." .

ns1:42671 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Optik Software is a former game development company, best known for creating the MS-DOS game War Inc. in 1997." .

ns1:42677 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Illinois gubernatorial election took place on 07 November 2006. Incumbent Democratic Governor of Illinois Rod Blagojevich won re-election to a second four-year term scheduled to have ended on January 10, 2011. On 07 November 2006, 2005, Topinka announced that she would not seek re-election as state treasurer — instead, she entered the gubernatorial primary, hoping to challenge Democratic Governor of Illinois Rod Blagojevich. In February 2006, the candidates for the Republican nomination for Illinois Governor of Illinois began running their first TV ads for the March statewide primary election." .

ns1:42678 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The David Higham Prize for Fiction was inaugurated in 1975 to mark the 80th birthday of David Higham, literary agent, and was awarded annually to a citizen of the Commonwealth, Republic of Ireland, Pakistan, or South Africa for a first novel or book of short stories." .

ns1:42683 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The New York City Police Riot, known at the time as the Great Police Riot, was a conflict which occurred in front of New York City Hall between the recently dissolved New York Municipal Police and the newly formed Metropolitan Police on 16 June 1857. Arriving at New York City Hall to assume the office on 16 June 1857, Conover was informed that Mayor Wood had instead appointed Charles Devlin to the position." .

ns1:42687 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "murder of Melanie Carpenter (April 22, 1971 – 06 January 1995) was a Canadian 23-year-old woman who was abducted and murder in British Columbia, on 06 January 1995. On 06 January 1995, murder of Melanie Carpenter, a 23-year-old woman from Surrey, British Columbia, had received suspicious phone calls from a man feigning interest in a business deal." .

ns1:42700 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1942 United States Senate election in Massachusetts was held on 03 November 1942, with Republican incumbent Henry Cabot Lodge Jr. defeating his challengers." .

ns1:42706 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics competed at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics, in Nanjing, China from 16 August to 2014. Qualification Legend: Q=Final A (medal); qB=Final B (non-medal); qC=Final C (non-medal); qD=Final D (non-medal); qE=Final E (non-medal) Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified two athletes based on the 2014 BWF Junior World Rankings. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified a boys' team from their performance at the 2014 CEV Youth Continental Cup Final. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified one boxer based on its performance at the 2014 AIBA Youth World Championships. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified four athletes based on its performance at the 2014 FIE Cadet World Championships. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified one athlete based on its performance at the 2014 European WAG Championships. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified one athlete based on its performance at the 2014 Youth A World Championships. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified two athletes based on the 2014 ITF World Junior Rankings. Poland at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics qualified one athlete based on its performance at the 2014 European Cadet Championships." .

ns1:42711 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1971 San Fernando earthquake (also known as the Sylmar earthquake) occurred in the early morning of 09 February 1971 in the foothills of the San Gabriel Mountains in southern California. The San Fernando earthquake occurred on 09 February 1971, at 6:00:41 am Pacific Standard Time (14:00:41 UTC) with a strong ground motion duration of about 12 seconds. All these buildings had been previously inspected with regard to the requirements of the Act, and many were reinforced or rebuilt at that time, but earthquake engineering experts recommended further immediate refurbishment or demolition after a separate evaluation was done after the 09 February 1971 earthquake, and within a year and a half the district followed through with the direction with regard to about 100 structures." .

ns1:42717 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 FIRS Intercontinental Cup was the ninth edition of the roller hockey tournament known as the Intercontinental Cup, played on 2006 at Alcoy, Spain." .

ns1:42718 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Indian Creek massacre occurred on 21 May 1832 with the attack by a party of Native Americans on a group of United States settlers in LaSalle County, Illinois following a dispute about a settler-constructed dam that prevented fish from reaching a nearby Potawatomi village. Today, the site of the massacre is marked by memorials in Shabbona County Park in LaSalle County, about 14 miles (23 km) north of Ottawa, Illinois. The Indian Creek massacre resulted from a dispute between U.S. settlers and a Potawatomi Native American village along the Indian Creek in LaSalle County, Illinois. Hostilities in the Black Hawk War began on May 14, 1832, when Black Hawk's warriors soundly defeated Illinois militiamen at the Battle of Stillman's Run. Modern scholarly accounts of the Black Hawk War and the Indian Creek massacre make no mention of Mike Girty. The Indian Creek massacre was the most significant publicized incident during the Black Hawk War." .

ns1:42730 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Sharpie 500 was a NASCAR Sprint Cup Series stock car race that was held on 22 August 2009, at Bristol Motor Speedway in Bristol, Tennessee. Kyle Busch, of the Joe Gibbs Racing team, won the race, with Mark Martin finishing second, and Marcos Ambrose third. Mark Martin was the undisputed best driver in the 2009 Sprint Cup Series season after this event; even though he finished in second place behind Kyle Busch. Gambling pundits were marvelled over Kyle Busch's victory in the 2009 Spring Bristol race along with another previous win at the Spring 2007 Bristol race. The same critics would pan the inferior performance of Kevin Harvick at Bristol Motor Speedway; acquiring only an average finish of 11th place in the seventeen previous races at Bristol before this one." .

ns1:42734 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2020 UEFA European Under-19 Championship (also known as Union of European Football Associations Under-19 Euro 2020) was scheduled to be the 19th edition of the UEFA European Under-19 Football Championship (69th edition if the Under-18 and Junior eras are included), the annual international youth association football championship organised by Union of European Football Associations for the men's under-19 national teams of Europe. Due to the COVID-19 pandemic, the tournament was initially postponed, rescheduled and was cancelled in 2020. Northern Ireland, which last hosted the tournament in 2005, was selected as host by Union of European Football Associations on 9 December 2016. The final tournament was originally scheduled to be played between 19 – 2020. Due to the COVID-19 pandemic, Union of European Football Associations announced on 2020 that the tournament had been postponed until further notice. On 2020, Union of European Football Associations announced that the final tournament had been rescheduled and would be played in two periods, with the group stage played between 2020–2020, and the knockout stage, which would consist of the semi-finals, the FIFA U-20 World Cup play-off and the final, pl11 November 2020ed be14 November 2020November 2020. Union of European Football Associations then announced on 2020 that after consultation with the 55 member associations, the final tournament had been further postponed, with the group stage played in 2020 and the knockout stage played in March 2021. On 2020, Union of European Football Associations announced that the tournament would be played in March 2021 in straight knock-out format, consisting of the quarter-finals, semi-finals, final, and play-off matches to decide the fifth team to qualify for the FIFA U-20 World Cup. Finally, the tournament was cancelled by Union of European Football Associations on 2020." .

ns1:42737 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP) Challenger Tour was the secondary professional tennis circuit organized by the ATP. The 2012 ATP Challenger Tour calendar comprised 15 top tier ATP Challenger Tour tournaments, and approximately 150 regular series tournaments, with prize money ranging from $35,000 up to $150,000. These tables present the number of singles (S) and doubles (D) titles won by each player and each nation during the season, within all the tournament categories of the 2012 ATP Challenger Tour: the ATP Challenger Tour tournaments, and the regular series tournaments." .

ns1:42751 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Tour de l'Abitibi is a junior stage race taking place in the Abitibi-Témiscamingue region of Quebec, Canada." .

ns1:42759 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 IRB Nations Cup was the fourth edition of the international rugby union tournament, a competition created by the World Rugby. It pits the \"A\" Teams of the stronger (Tier 1) rugby nations (France A, Italy A and Scotland A national rugby union team) against some of the Tier 2 and 3 nations (Romania, Russia and Uruguay). Scotland A national rugby union team were the overall winners of the tournament." .

ns1:42769 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Falsterbo Swedish Coast Guard crash was the crash of a CASA C-212 Aviocar turboprop airplane belonging to the Swedish Coast Guard in Falsterbo Canal, Sweden, on 26 October 2006." .

ns1:42774 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Seven Days Battles were a series of seven battles over seven days from 25 June 1862 to 01 July 1862, near Richmond, Virginia, during the American Civil War. The army was in no condition for a renewed offensive; close to 16,000 men and officers had been killed or wounded between 25 June 1862 and 01 July 1862, particularly in the V Corps, which had done the heaviest fighting, while the survivors were extremely tired after a week of fighting and marching with little food or sleep, most of the artillery ammunition had been used up, and the summer weather was taking its toll with the army sick lists getting longer and longer." .

ns1:42778 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 219, adopted unanimously on 17 December 1965, after reaffirming previous resolutions on the topic, the Council extended the stationing in Cyprus of the United Nations Peacekeeping Force in Cyprus for an additional 3 months, now ending on March 26, 1966." .

ns1:42783 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bulgarian International Badminton Championships is an annual international badminton championships held in Bulgaria since 1985. The tournament belongs to the Badminton Europe elite circuit and become the highest level badminton tournament in Bulgaria." .

ns1:42788 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lennox Lewis vs. Vitali Klitschko, billed as \"Battle of the Titans\", was a heavyweight professional boxing match contested between WBC, IBO, The Ring, and lineal champion Lennox Lewis and former WBO champion Vitaliy Klitschko. The bout took place on 21 June 2003 at the Staples Center in Los Angeles, California." .

ns1:42790 a ns1:context_narration ;
