ns1:42945 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Second Battle of Newtonia was fought on 28 October 1864, near Newtonia, Missouri, between cavalry commanded by Major General James G. Blunt of the Union Army and Brigadier General Joseph O. Shelby's rear guard of the Confederate Army of Missouri. Following a set of three defeats in Missouri and Kansas on October 25, Price's column halted to rest near Newtonia on 28 October 1864. On 28 October 1864, Price halted his retreat near Newtonia, Missouri, hoping to give his weary men a rest." .

