ns1:42955 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "It has been played at the Nicklaus Golf Club at LionsGate in Overland Park and Blue Hills Country Club in Kansas City, Missouri. The tournament took a hiatus in 2010, and returned as the Midwest Classic in 2011 with the Kansas City Crusaders as the host organization. Their mission is to provide a positive economic impact on area businesses and offer support to local charitable organizations through the promotion of professional golf in Kansas City." .

ns1:42957 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Heywood and Middleton by-election was on 2014 in the Heywood and Middleton constituency following the death of its MP Jim Dobbin on 2014. During an interview on Daily Politics, after the leaflet was called \"divisive\" by his Labour opponent Liz McInnes, Bickley criticised McInnes for publishing a leaflet with the heading \"WAITING TO DIE\" after the death of Jim Dobbin, saying it was landing on the doorsteps of the terminally ill. On 2014, Rochdale Borough Council published the statement of persons nominated, which confirmed five candidates would contest the by-election." .

ns1:42970 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Grand National (known as the Martell Grand National for sponsorship reasons) was the 151st official renewal of the world-famous Grand National steeplechase that took place at Aintree Racecourse near Liverpool, England, on 1998. The main race was seen by the smallest Grand National attendance at Aintree Racecourse since 1985, with a crowd of just 46,679, over 11,000 less than two years prior. His preparation for the National had included four victories, including the Peter Cazelet/Anthony Mildmay memorial chase at Sandown in January before finishing third in the Singer & Friedlander Grand National trial at Uttoxeter and second ahead of Earth Summit, who finished fifth in the Red Square Vodka Gold Cup at Haydock in February. Samlee was a nine-year-old who came to prominence after winning the Becher Chase over one circuit of the Aintree Racecourse Grand National course in November, having been second in the Scottish Grand National earlier in the year." .

ns1:42978 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Killing Time (Temps mort) is a 2007 Canadian documentary film that tells the story of how Bhutan expelled a sixth of its population in 1990." .

ns1:42985 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2007 Shinwar shooting, was the killing of a number of Afghan people on 04 March 2007, in the village of Spinpul, in the Shinwar of the Nangarhar Province of Afghanistan. United States Marines, fleeing the scene of a car bomb attack and ambush by Afghan militants, fired on people and vehicles surrounding them, according to initial reports killing as many as 19 civilians and injuring around 50 more." .

ns1:42990 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 ATP German Open was a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts. It was the 85th edition of the German Open Tennis Championships (German Open Tennis Championships), and was part of the ATP Super 9 of the 1991 ATP Tour. It took place at the Rothenbaum Tennis Center in Hamburg, Germany, from 6 May until 1991." .

ns1:42993 a ns1:context_narration ;
