    rdfs:label "The Women's Junior NORCECA Volleyball Championship is a volleyball competition for national teams, currently held biannually and organized by the North, Central America and Caribbean Volleyball Confederation, the North America, Central America and Caribbean volleyball federation." .

ns1:43107 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Groenlo or Groenlo in 1595 was a siege of Groenlo by States forces under Maurice of Nassau during the Eighty Years' War in an attempt to capture it from the Spanish Empire. To form a bridgehead into Twente, Maurice planned a siege on Groenlo, despite discouragements of Maurice's nephew and military advisor, William Louis, Count of Nassau-Dillenburg, who thought that the fortifications of the city were as good as impregnable. Maurice had great difficulty to find enough funds and troops for his plans, whereby the campaign into Twente did not start until 1595, when the siege of Groenlo finally begun. The siege started on 14 July 1595, with the arrival of Maurice at Groenlo, along with 6000 foot soldiers, several companies of cavalry, and sixteen cannons. Aware that the reinforcement troops led by Mondragón posed a major threat to the campaign, Maurice started to bombard Groenlo on 24 July 1595 and ordered its immediate surrender. Maurice suspended his Twente campaign until 1597, when he lay siege on Groenlo successfully." .

ns1:43112 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1997 Summer Universiade – men's 110 metres hurdles event at the athletics at the 1997 Summer Universiade was held on 26 August–27 August at the Stadio Cibali in Catania, Italy." .

ns1:43113 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 New Mexico Lobos women's basketball team represented the University of New Mexico during the 2014–15 NCAA Division I women's basketball season. 2014–15 New Mexico Lobos men's basketball team." .

ns1:43116 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 22 December 2009, an American Airlines Boeing 737-800, operating American Airlines Flight 331 (Washington, D.C.–Miami–Norman Manley International Airport) and carrying 148 passengers and six crew, overran runway 12 on landing at Kingston in poor weather. Reports from Jamaica indicate that as of December 28, 2009, most passenger and crew property was yet to be returned due to the investigation; American Airlines provided each passenger $5,000 to compensate for the lengthy quarantine of baggage." .

ns1:43118 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016–17 Egyptian Second Division (also known as dmc League for sponsorship reasons) was the 37th edition of the Egyptian Second Division, the top Egyptian semi-professional level for association football clubs, since its establishment in 1977." .

ns1:43119 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1754 British general election returned members to serve in the House of Commons of the 11th Parliament of Great Britain to be summoned, after the merger of the Parliament of England and the Parliament of Scotland in 1707. The resulting eleventh Parliament of Great Britain was convened on 1754 and sat through eight sessions until its dissolution on 20 April 1761. The general election was held between 1754 and 1754." .

ns1:43128 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1951 World Figure Skating Championships is an annual figure skating competition sanctioned by the International Skating Union in which figure skating compete for the title of World Champion. The 1951 championships took place on 23 February 1951–25 in Milan, Italy." .

ns1:43131 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1953 All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final was the 66th All-Ireland Final and the culmination of the All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1953, an inter-county hurling tournament for the top teams in Ireland. The match was held at Croke Park, Dublin, on 1953, between Cork and Galway." .

ns1:43133 a ns1:context_narration ;
