ns1:43591 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Museum Night (Croatian: Noć muzeja) is an annual event in Croatia. Museum Night was first held in 2005, with only six museums from Zagreb area participating, drawing 10,000 visitors. In 2014, there were 360,000 museum-goers during the Museum Night, with 800 performances held." .

ns1:43596 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006–07 Danish Superliga season was the 17th season of the Danish Superliga league championship, which determined the winners of the Danish football championship. It took place from the first match on 19 July 2006 to the final match on 27 May 2007." .

ns1:43601 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Olomouc took place in 1758 when a Prussian army led by Frederick the Great besieged the Austrian city of Olmütz (now Olomouc, Czech Republic) during the Prussian invasion of Moravia in the Third Silesian War (Seven Years War). With a lack of supplies and the approach of an Austrian relief force following the Battle of Domstadtl, Frederick abandoned the siege and withdrew from Moravia." .

ns1:43604 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "judo competitions judo at the 2008 Summer Olympics in Beijing were held from August 9 to August 15 at the Beijing Science and Technology University Gymnasium." .

ns1:43608 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 World Archery Championships was the 32nd edition of the World Archery Championships. The event was held in Los Angeles, United States of America in 19 October 1983 and was organised by World Archery Federation (FITA)." .

ns1:43616 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 FINA Men's Water Polo World Cup was the fifth edition of FINA Water Polo World Cup, organised by the world's governing body in aquatics, the FINA (FINA)." .

ns1:43618 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Players Championship was a golf tournament in Florida on the PGA Tour, held May 8–11 at TPC Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, southeast of Jacksonville. It was the 35th The Players Championship and was won by Sergio García Fernández, in a sudden-death playoff over Paul Goydos. In the groups ahead, the pairing of Jeff Quinney and Sergio García Fernández produced some of the best golf of the day, and García became the clubhouse leader at 5-under-par 283." .

ns1:43620 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 All-Ireland Under-21 Hurling Championship Final was a hurling match that was played at Croke Park, Dublin on 2007 to determine the winners of the All-Ireland Under-21 Hurling Championship 2007, the 44th season of the All-Ireland Under-21 Hurling Championship, a tournament organised by the Gaelic Athletic Association for the champion teams of the four provinces of Ireland." .

ns1:43643 a ns1:context_narration ;
