ns1:43713 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1241 papal election (21 September to 25 October) saw the election of Cardinal Goffredo da Castiglione as Celestine IV. Celestine IV died on Sunday, 1241, just 17 days after his election, even before he had been enthroned. It took a year and a half before the cardinals were successful in reconvening in Anagni (Frederick II was in possession of Rome) and electing a successor to Celestine IV, due in no small part to Frederick II's continuing to keep da Pecorara and Oddone as hostages: choosing Cardinal Fieschi as Pope Innocent IV in 1243. Matthew was a friend of Cardinal Somercotes (who had once presided over the audientia litterarum contradictarum in Rome), and further claimed that Somercotes would have soon been elected pope himself had he survived." .

ns1:43714 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Tour of the Basque Country was the 23rd edition of the Itzulia Basque Country cycle race and was held from 04 April 1983 to 08 April 1983." .

ns1:43729 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Airlines Flight 624, a Douglas DC-6 airliner, registration NC37506, was a scheduled passenger flight that originated in San Diego, California with stops in Los Angeles and Chicago en route to LaGuardia Airport in New York City. The four-engine propeller-driven airplane crashed at 1:41 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time on 17 June 1948 outside of Aristes, Pennsylvania, killing all 4 crew members and 39 passengers on board." .

ns1:43731 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The UCI Road World Championships – Men's road race at the 1983 UCI Road World Championships – Men's road race was the 50th edition of the event. The race took place on Sunday 04 September 1983 in Altenrhein, Switzerland, over a distance of 269.89 km (167.7 mi)." .

ns1:43734 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Alternatively, there are special names given to gouttes of various tinctures, as in a goutte d'eau (literally \"a droplet of water\")." .

ns1:43738 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "MLS Cup '97 was the second edition of the MLS Cup, the post-season championship match of Major League Soccer (MLS) in the United States. It was played on 1997, between D.C. United and the Colorado Rapids to determine the champion of the 1997 season. During a rainstorm that mirrored the previous final, D.C. repeated as MLS Cup champions by winning 2–1. Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium in Washington, D.C., the home of defending champions D.C. United, was selected as the host of the second MLS Cup on December 17, 1996. The MLS Cup is the post-season championship of Major League Soccer (MLS), a professional club association football league based in the United States that began play in 1996. The winners of the Conference Finals advanced to the single-match MLS Cup final, which would be held at a predetermined neutral venue. MLS Cup '97 was contested by defending champions and hosts D.C. United, who finished first in the regular season standings, and the Colorado Rapids, who finished fourth in the Western Conference. The MLS Cup final kicked off at 3:30 p.m. with an announced sellout crowd of 57,431 spectators at Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium, setting a new attendance record for a single playoff match. Three days after the MLS Cup final, D.C. United played the Dallas Burn in the U.S. Open Cup Final with a chance to earn the league's first \"treble\"." .

ns1:43749 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Al-Mina'a SC season will be Al-Mina'a SC 39th season in the Iraqi Premier League, having featured in all 41 editions of the competition except two." .

ns1:43751 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ofira Air Battle was one of the first air battles of the Yom Kippur War. On 06 October 1973, Egypt launched a massive surprise attack on Israel that included over 200 Egyptian aircraft participating in an opening airstrike." .

ns1:43764 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Havana Jam was a three-day music festival that took place at the Karl Marx Theatre, in Havana, Cuba, on 2 March 1979–4 March 1979. With a real crisis in the music industry in the United States and the start of the salsa boom, in April 1978, CBS Records director, Bruce Lundvall, saw an open door to probe Cuban music and together with a group of the company's music enthusiasts made a four-day trip to Havana, where they were overwhelmed by the sound of Cuban music, but especially by Afro-Cuban jazz band Irakere, one of Cuba's most highly regarded and virtuoso musical acts." .

ns1:43767 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The tournament was contested in Nabeul city in Tunisia from 2017–15 October 2017. Unlike in the 2015 WMF World Cup, 24 teams from 5 continents are qualified for the final tournament: On 2017, the Executive bureau of the World Minifootball Federation had unanimously decided in Brno, Czech Republic that the 2017 World Cup will be organized from October 6 to 2017. On 2017, The final draw for 2017 WMF World Cup was made in Tunis." .

ns1:43769 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Capital Pride is an annual pride parade held in early June each year in Washington, D.C. It was founded as Gay Pride Day, a one-day block party and street festival, in 1975. The festival was the fourth-largest gay pride event in the United States of America in 2007. Capital Pride attracted more than 200,000 people in 2006, making it the fourth-largest gay pride event in the United States of America. On June 7, 2014, a United States of America Armed Forces color guard led the way and retired the colors in the Capital Pride parade. It was the first time in American history that an officially sanctioned United States of America Armed Forces color guard marched in a gay pride parade." .

ns1:43776 a ns1:context_narration ;
