ns1:43919 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2022 Hong Kong Chief Executive election is scheduled in March 2022 for the 6th term of the Chief Executive of Hong Kong (CE), the highest office of the Hong Kong (HKSAR). The winner of the 2022 Chief Executive election is scheduled to be inaugurated on 01 July 2022." .

ns1:43930 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Baidoa began on 20 December 2006 when the Somali Somali Transitional Federal Government's forces (Transitional Federal Government) allied with occupying Ethiopian forces attacked the Islamic Courts Union (Islamic Courts Union). On December 3, it was reported in an Amharic newspaper The Ethiopian Herald that 60 Islamic Courts Union militiamen had surrendered to Transitional Federal Government forces in Baidoa, along with their technicals, the newspaper reported that were dissatisfied by extremist policies arising within the Islamic Courts Union. Ethiopia, Kenya and Djibouti were barred from taking part in the peacekeeping operation, leaving it up to Uganda, Tanzania and Eritrea, primarily Uganda. In a press statement the Eritrea Permanent Mission to the United Nations officially denied its nation had any troops in Somalia. On December 8, Transitional Federal Government backed by Ethiopian troops (according to eyewitnesses) attacked the Islamic Courts Union militias in the town of Dinsoor, 110km southwest of Baidoa, sparking heavy fighting. The UN had accused Ethiopia of breaking the arms embargo and it was their intention to send more neutral foreign forces to support the Transitional Federal Government. He said that the deadline the Islamic Courts Union had given the Ethiopians to remove their armed forces from Somalia had been for guidance and that the Islamic Courts Union were still \"hoping for peace\". The Battle of Baidoa began on 20 December 2006 when the Transitional Federal Government allied with occupying Ethiopian forces attacked the Islamic Courts Union. Transitional Federal Government forces and the Islamic Courts Union militiamen exchanged mortar fire at Daynunay, 20km from Baidoa according to eyewitnesses. The Transitional Federal Government claimed that the Islamic Courts Union started the fighting, while the Islamic Courts Union said the Transitional Federal Government had done so." .

ns1:43938 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss World Italy 2018, the 13th Miss World Italy pageant, was held in the Teatro Italia, Gallipoli." .

ns1:43940 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Song conquest of Southern Han (Chinese: 宋灭南汉之战) occurred in 971, when the forces of the Song Dynasty captured the Southern Han capital of Guangzhou in present-day Guangdong Province." .

ns1:43946 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1919 West Virginia Mountaineers football team represented the West Virginia Mountaineers during the 1919 college football season." .

ns1:43947 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 19 October 1956, Japan and the Soviet Union signed a Soviet–Japanese Joint Declaration of 1956 providing for the end of the state of war, and for restoration of diplomatic relations between USSR and Japan. The Soviet–Japanese Joint Declaration of 1956 provided, in its article 9, for continuation of negotiations for the conclusion of a peace treaty after the restoration of diplomatic relations between the countries and further stipulated, that \"in this connexion, the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics, desiring to meet the wishes of Japan and taking into consideration the interests of the Japanese State, agrees to transfer to Japan the Habomai Islands and the island of Shikoton , the actual transfer of these islands to Japan to take place after the conclusion of a Peace Treaty between the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics and Japan\". The formula did not pass, however: in spite of preliminary agreement with the Soviets to shelve the territorial issue, Japan raised it at the negotiations and managed to get aforementioned territorial clause in the declaration, yet \"interpreted in such a manner as to preserve the plenipotentiaries' face at home\": \"Habomais and Shikotan were promised in the Soviet–Japanese Joint Declaration of 1956, and the question of Kunashiri and Etorofu was to be settled during negotiations for a peace treaty\"." .

ns1:43954 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Auckland Blackout was a major electrical blackout in Auckland, the largest city in New Zealand, on 12 June 2006. Power went off at around 8:30 am local time on 12 June 2006 over half of Auckland in New Zealand. Power was restored to the central business district of Auckland at 12:40 local time, 12 June 2006." .

ns1:43956 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 British Columbia general election (formally the 41st British Columbia general election) was held on 2017, to elect 87 members (MLAs) to the Legislative Assembly to serve in the 41st Parliament of the Canadian province of British Columbia. In the 40th Parliament prior to this general election, the British Columbia Liberal Party (BC Liberals) formed the government under the leadership of Christy Clark, while the BC New Democratic Party (BC NDP), under the leadership of Adrian Dix and then John Horgan, formed the Official Opposition; the BC Green Party were also represented in the legislature with sole MLA and later leader Andrew Weaver. The election was notable in that it marked the end of the Liberal majority government that had led the province since the 2001 election, and the first election in Canada at the federal or provincial level that saw more than one member of a Green party elected. Section 23 of British Columbia's Constitution Act provides that general elections occur on the second Tuesday in May of the fourth calendar year after the last election. As an election was held on May 14, 2013, the subsequent election was conducted on 2017. In preparation for the 2017 provincial election, the Electoral Boundaries Commission Amendment Act, 2014 increased the number of electoral districts from 85 to 87 and required that the number of electoral districts in the North, Cariboo-Thompson, and the Columbia-Kootenay regions not be decreased despite their lower populations since the last adjustment of electoral boundaries. On 2017, the New York Times published a story calling British Columbia the \"Wild West\" of Canadian political cash. According to the New York Times, \"critics of and her party, the conservative British Columbia Liberal Party, say the provincial government has been transformed into a lucrative business, dominated by special interests that trade donations for political favors, undermining Canada's reputation for functional, consensus-driven democracy.\" In terms of election spending, British Columbia currently has no spending limits ahead of the election period. Spending limits for the 2017 election period were adjusted for changes to the consumer price index before being confirmed during the second week in 2017. Summary of the 2017 British Columbia Legislative election." .

ns1:43961 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's coxed pair competition at the 2016 World Rowing Championships – men's coxed pair in Rotterdam took place at the Willem-Alexander Baan." .

ns1:43969 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Kilkim Žaibu (from Lithuanian \"arise/soar with the lightning\") is an extreme metal festival in the Baltic region, Europe held annually since 1999. From 2010, the festival takes place at Lūkstas lake in the town of Varniai, Lithuania. Before that, it had been happening at \"Plūgo broliai\" in Joniškis, Lithuania. The festival took place in Varniai, Lithuania on 28 June 2018 - 30 June 2018. The festival took place in Varniai, Lithuania on 29 June 2017 - 1 July 2017. The festival took place in Varniai, Lit23 June 2016a25 2016 2016. The line-up: The festival in 20111 June 2010y12 June 2010me took place at lake Lukstas 11 June 12 June, Lithuania on 11–2010.12 June 2009h13 June 2009e festival took place at \"Plūgo Bro12 Junea13 Juneiškis, Lithuania on 12–2009. The line-up: The festival took place at \"Plūgo Broliai\", Joniškis, Lithuania on 7 June 2008." .

ns1:43972 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The White Lotus (traditional Chinese: 白蓮敎; simplified Chinese: 白莲敎; pinyin: Báiliánjiào; Wade–Giles: Pai-lien chiao) was a religious and political movement that appealed to many Han Chinese who found solace in worship of Wusheng Laomu (\"Unborn Venerable Mother\" (traditional Chinese: 無生老母; simplified Chinese: 无生老母)), who was foretold to gather all her children at the millennium into one family. This fear of secret societies carried on in the law; the Great Qing Legal Code, which was in effect until 1912, contained the following section: ll societies calling themselves at random White Lotus, communities of the Buddha Maitreya, or the Mingtsung religion (Manichaeans), or the school of the White Cloud, etc., together with all who carry out deviant and heretical practices, or who in secret places have prints and images, gather the people by burning incense, meeting at night and dispersing by day, thus stirring up and misleading people under the pretext of cultivating virtue, shall be sentenced. He took the title Hongwu Emperor and founded the Ming dynasty, whose name echoes the religious sentiment of the White Lotus. While traditional historiography has linked many Maitreyist and millenarian uprisings during the Ming and Qing dynasty as all related to the White Lotus, there are reasons to doubt that such connections existed." .

ns1:43984 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gamaya is the fourth engineering educational institution established in Kerala, India. In addition to this, a 10% seats are provided for admission to the third semester classes for diploma holders (Lateral entry system) The alumni association has chapters in cities in India including Mumbai, Pune, Bangalore, Chennai, Kozhikode, Palakkad and Kochi." .

ns1:43988 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 Asian Men's Handball Championship was the second Asian Men's Handball Championship, which was taking place from 1 to 11 November 1979, in Nanjing, People's Republic of China." .

ns1:43990 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Primera División de Fútbol Profesional – Apertura 1998 season (officially \"Copa Pilsener Apertura 1999\") started on 1998, and finished on 1998. The season saw Alianza Fútbol Club win its 7th league title after a 1-0 victory over C.D." .

ns1:43991 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of the Ruhr of 1943 was a 5-month British strategic bombing during World War II during the Second World War against the Ruhr in Nazi Germany, which had coke plants, steelworks, and 10 synthetic oil plants. Although not strictly part of the Ruhr area, the battle of the Ruhr included other cities such as Cologne which were within the Rhine-Ruhr region and considered part of the same \"industrial complex\". Even after this switch of focus to Hamburg, there would be further raids on the Ruhr area by the RAF—in part to keep German defences dispersed, just as there had been raids on areas other than the Ruhr during the battle. During the battle of the Ruhr, Bomber Command estimated about 70% of their aircraft losses were due to fighters." .

ns1:43992 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 592, adopted on 08 December 1986, having considered a letter from the representative of Zimbabwe in his capacity as Chairman of the Movement of Non-Aligned Countries, the Council reaffirmed the Geneva Conventions and condemned the opening of fire at a student demonstration by the Israel Defense Forces, in which two students were killed at Birzeit University." .

