ns1:44272 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 Southern 500, the 30th running of the Bojangles' Southern 500, was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series race that took place on 03 September 1979, at Darlington Raceway in Darlington, South Carolina. Darlington Raceway, nicknamed by many NASCAR fans and drivers as \"The Lady in Black\" or \"The Track Too Tough to Tame\" and advertised as a \"NASCAR Tradition\", is a race track built for NASCAR racing located near Darlington, South Carolina." .

ns1:44275 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Icelandic Language Day (Icelandic: dagur íslenskrar tungu, English: \"day of the Icelandic tongue\") is a festival celebrated on 16 November each year in Iceland to celebrate the Icelandic." .

ns1:44276 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Neo-Manueline is a revival style of architecture which drew from the 16th century Manueline Late Gothic architecture of Portugal. Neo-Manueline constructions have been built across Portugal, Brazil, and the Lusofonia (the former Portuguese Empire). In the sequence of the Gothic Revival architecture fashion that spread for all over Europe since the middle of the 18th century, the Manueline style was considered the most authentical Portuguese architectural style. Another pioneering project was the restoration of the Jerónimos Monastery in Lisbon during the 1860s, in which the Manueline monastery gained a new tower and annexes built in Neo-Manueline style (which now house the Maritime Museum and the National Archaeology Museum). Other important Neo-Manueline buildings in Portugal are Rossio Railway Station, Lisbon (1886–90), Palace Hotel of Bussaco (1888–1907), the Sintra Town Hall (1906–09), the Counts of Castro Guimarães Palace in Cascais (1900) and the Quinta da Regaleira in Sintra (1904–10)." .

ns1:44279 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1967 Gabonese general election were held in Gabon on 19 March 1967 to elect a President and the National Assembly." .

