ns1:44315 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Soest Feud (German: Soester Fehde), or Feud of Soest, was a feud that took place from 1444 to 1449 in which the town of Soest claimed its freedom from Archbishop Dietrich of Cologne (1414–1463), who tried to restore his rule." .

ns1:44318 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The football at the 2005 Mediterranean Games was the 15th edition of the Mediterranean Games men's association football tournament. The association football tournament was held in Almería, Spain between 2005 and 2005 as part of the 2005 Mediterranean Games and was contested by 9 teams, all countries were represented by the U-23 teams (although in fact none of the players named were older than 21); Spain won the gold medal." .

ns1:44326 a ns1:context_narration ;
