ns1:44370 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007–08 A-League was the 31st season of top-flight association football in Australia, and the third season of the A-League competition since its establishment in 2004. Based on the 2007–08 season of the A-League, the Central Coast Mariners and Newcastle Jets FC qualified for the 2009 AFC Champions League, as the competition's Premiers and Champions respectively." .

ns1:44371 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1960 Saskatchewan general election was the fourteenth provincial election held in the Canadian province of Saskatchewan. It was held on 1960, to elect members of the Legislative Assembly of Saskatchewan. The Co-operative Commonwealth Federation of Tommy Douglas campaigned promising Medicare, a public medical insurance and delivery plan for all of Saskatchewan, and it was re-elected with a slightly increased majority. A year later, Douglas passed legislation making Saskatchewan the first province in Canada to have Medicare. The Liberals were concerned that the economic development of Saskatchewan had lagged behind the rest of Canada during the Douglas era." .

ns1:44381 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ragnarök Festival is a pagan metal music festival held annually in Germany since 2004 founded by Ivo Raab. From 2006 on the music festival took place in the significantly bigger town hall of Lichtenfels, Bavaria. With the hall now being far too small, the music festival moved in 2006 to the town hall of Lichtenfels with the capacity of 3500 people." .

ns1:44383 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Future Combat Systems Manned Ground Vehicles (MGV) was a family of lighter and more transportable ground vehicles developed by BAE Systems Inc and General Dynamics as part of the United States Army's Future Combat Systems (FCS) program." .

