ns1:44611 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Villafranca took place on 17 March 1809, during the French occupation of León in the Peninsular War. One remaining Spain formation, General Pedro Caro, 3rd Marquis of la Romana's division of regular infantry, established itself in Asturias and harassed the French in León and Galicia, capturing Imperial troops and supplies with impunity. A costly battle broke out that claimed the lives of several Spain officers." .

