ns1:44668 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 AFC Champions League Final was a two-legged association football tie to determine the 2007 AFC Champions League champions of Asian club football. Urawa Red Diamonds defeated Sepahan F.C. 3-1 on aggregate to take the title. The winners, Urawa Red Diamonds, received US$600,000 prize money and qualified to represent Asia in the 2007 AFC Champions League FIFA Club World Cup." .

