ns1:44782 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1911–12 FA Cup was the 41st season of the world's oldest association football competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup (more usually known as the FA Cup). Barnsley F.C. won the competition for the first time, beating West Bromwich Albion 1–0 after extra time in the replay of the 1912 FA Cup Final at Bramall Lane in Sheffield, through a goal from Harry Tufnell. The format of the FA Cup for the season had two preliminary rounds, five qualifying rounds, four proper rounds, and the semi finals and 1912 FA Cup Final. Both matches went to replays, which West Bromwich Albion and Barnsley F.C. won, going on to meet each other in the 1912 FA Cup Final." .

ns1:44783 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Siberian International Marathon (SIM) (Russian: Сибирский международный марафон) has been held in the city of Omsk since 1990, when the city was first opened to foreigners. It was organised in 1990 by Dmitri Khodko and Sergei Govrilov as an attempt to open Omsk to foreigners." .

ns1:44785 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Rainbow Bluff Expedition took place on 09 December 1864 during the American Civil War." .

ns1:44786 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Rallye de France-Alsace was the eleventh round of the 2013 World Rally Championship season, held from 3 to 6 October, 2013." .

ns1:44794 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Armory Show is an international art fair in New York City, established in 1994 and held annually in March on Piers 92 & 94. Art Apart Fair, is Singapore's first hotel-based boutique art fair and it was inspired by The Armory Show." .

ns1:44795 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Recopa Sudamericana (officially the 2013 Recopa Santander Sudamericana for sponsorship reasons) was the 21st edition of the Recopa Sudamericana, the association football competition organized by CONMEBOL between the winners of the previous season's two major South American club tournaments, the Copa Libertadores and the Copa Sudamericana. The competition was contested in two-legged home-and-away format between two Brazilian teams, S.C. Corinthians Paulista, the 2012 Copa Libertadores champion, and São Paulo FC, the 2012 Copa Sudamericana champion. The first leg was hosted by São Paulo FC at Estádio do Morumbi in São Paulo FC on 2013, while the second leg was hosted by S.C. Corinthians Paulista at Estádio do Pacaembu in São Paulo FC on 2013. S.C. Corinthians Paulista won both legs, the first leg by 2–1, and the second leg by 2–0, to win their first Recopa Sudamericana title." .

ns1:44797 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Armenian First League season began on 09 April 2010, and ended on 13 November 2010." .

ns1:44799 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 British Superbike Championship was the 28th British Superbike Championship season." .

ns1:44803 a ns1:context_narration ;
