ns1:44815 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1971 Cornell Big Red football team represented Cornell University in the 1971 college football season as a member of the Ivy League. On 1971, Cornell saw its largest home football crowd in the post-1970 era with 23,000 in attendance at Schoellkopf Field (which had a capacity of 25,597) for the day's rivalry match-up against Columbia." .

