    rdfs:label "The 1978 European Formula Three season was the fourth FIA European Formula 3 Championship season, contested over 16 rounds." .

ns1:44904 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Alexandria was fought on July 1 to July 30, 30 BC between the forces of Octavian and Mark Antony during the Final War of the Roman Republic." .

ns1:44907 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 WNBA All-Star Game was played on 17 July 2000 at Phoenix Suns Arena in Phoenix, Arizona." .

ns1:44914 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Jaffa Street bombing was a suicide bombing on 27 January 2002, in which Wafa Idris, a 28-year-old female Palestinian suicide bomber, blew herself up in the center of Jerusalem, killing one person and injuring about 100 others. On Sunday, 27 January 2002, the 28-year-old Palestinian suicide bomber Wafa Idris, who worked for the Palestinian Red Crescent in Ramallah, managed to pass through the Qalandiya checkpoint while she was driving a Red Crescent ambulance and dressed in the organization's uniform, while the explosive device was hidden in the ambulance." .

ns1:44917 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Tampere Film Festival (Finnish: Tampereen elokuvajuhlat) is a short film festival held every March in the Finnish city of Tampere. The first festival was held in 1969, and since 1970, it has been held in its current form, which makes it the oldest short film festival in Northern Europe. On December 15, 2020, it was announced that the Tampere Film Festival will open a new international short film competition called Generation XYZ for 2021, which has been developed in cooperation with an American film production company XYZ Films." .

ns1:44918 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 LPGA Championship was the 38th Women's PGA Championship, played May 14–17 at Bethesda Country Club in Bethesda, a suburb northwest of Washington, D.C. Betsy King won the fifth of her six major titles, eleven strokes ahead of runners-up JoAnne Carner, Liselotte Neumann, and Karen Noble." .

ns1:44922 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1980 European Athletics Indoor Championships – men's 3000 metres event at the 1980 European Athletics Indoor Championships was held on 2 March in Sindelfingen." .

ns1:44924 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Chrono Champenois–Trophée Européen was the 9th running of the Chrono Champenois - Trophée Européen, a women's individual time trial road bicycle racing. It was held on 16 September 2007 over a distance of 33.4 kilometres (20.8 miles) in France." .

ns1:44925 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The riot of Hoyerswerda Riots were xenophobic riots that lasted from 17 to 23 01 September 1991 in riot of Hoyerswerda, a town in the north-east of Saxony, Germany. In 1991, the word ausländerfrei (free of foreigners) became a synonym for the riot and Un-word of the year in Germany 1991." .

ns1:44930 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 MTV Video Music Awards aired live on 1993, honoring the best music videos from June 16, 1992, to 1993. The show was hosted by Christian Slater at the Gibson Amphitheatre in Los Angeles." .

ns1:44946 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 57th & 9th Tour is a world tour by British singer-songwriter Sting, in support of his twelfth solo studio album 57th & 9th." .

ns1:44950 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Zadwórze (sometimes referred to as the \"Polish Thermopylae\") was a battle of the Polish–Soviet War. It was fought on 17 August 1920 near the train station of Zadwórze, a small village located 33 kilometres from the city centre of Lviv (now Lviv). The battle, lasting roughly 24 hours, resulted in the complete destruction of the Polish forces but at the same time halted the Soviet advance, preventing the forces of Siemion Budionnyi from seizing Lviv and so contributing to the successful defence of Warsaw. Among the Polish soldiers killed in the battle was 19-year-old Konstanty Zarugiewicz, a student of the 7th course of primary school and a veteran of the 1918 defence of Lviv, for which he was awarded with Virtuti Militari and Krzyż Walecznych." .

ns1:44966 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Asian Men's Handball Championship was the twelfth Asian Men's Handball Championship and was held in Bangkok, Thailand from 12 to 21 February 2006." .

ns1:44967 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The boxing at the 1956 Summer Olympics – welterweight event was part of the boxing at the 1956 Summer Olympics at the 1956 Summer Olympics." .

ns1:44971 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The May 2012 battle of Rastan between the Syrian Armed Forces and the Free Syrian Army took place in the city of Al-Rastan on 2012, during the U.N. brokered cease-fire of the Syrian uprising." .

ns1:44975 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 BAFL season is the British American Football League. Based on the British American Football League, setup for the 2009 season there will be a 3 tier structure consisting of: W = Wins, L = Losses, T = Ties, PCT = Winning Percentage, PF= Points for, PA = Points against." .

ns1:44976 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2016 Gabonese presidential election were held in Gabon on 27 August 2016. Incumbent President Ali Bongo Ondimba ran for re-election and was challenged by former Minister of Foreign Affairs Jean Ping. President Ali Bongo Ondimba announced in Port-Gentil on 29 February 2016 that he would stand for re-election. The election was held on 27 August 2016." .

ns1:44984 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Syrian Revolt (Arabic: الثورة السورية الكبرى) or Great Druze Revolt (1925–1927) was a general uprising across Mandatory Syria and Lebanon aimed at getting rid of the French, who had been in control of the region since the end of World War I. In 1918, towards the end of World War I, the Ottoman Empire's forces withdrew from Syria after being defeated by the Allied Powers (Great Britain and French Third Republic) and their Hashemite Arab allies from the Hejaz. In the April 1920 San Remo Conference, the Allies were granted control over the Ottoman Empire's former Arab territories by the newly formed League of Nations, with Britain taking control of Palestine, Transjordan and Iraq, while French Third Republic took control of Syria. There was disquiet, even in Britain, when French Third Republic claimed Lebanon and Syria as \"colonies\". After initial rebel victories against the French, French Third Republic sent thousands of troops to Syria and Lebanon from Morocco and Senegal, equipped with modern weapons, compared to the meager supplies of the rebels. The Great Syrian Revolt is a widely remembered and commemorated event in Syria, and its leaders are remembered and respected by Syrians." .

ns1:44987 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United States v. Hubbell, 530 U.S. 27 (2000), was Supreme Court of the United States case involving Webster Hubbell, who had been indicted on various tax-related charges, and mail and wire fraud charges, based on documents that the government had subpoenaed from him. Oral arguments were heard February 22, 2000, and the Court announced its decision on 05 June 2000." .

ns1:44989 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "lawn bowls at the 2018 Commonwealth Games – men's singles was held at the Broadbeach Bowls Club in the Gold Coast, Australia from April 9 to 13." .

ns1:44991 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1912 Summer Olympics – men's decathlon was a track and field athletics event held as part of the athletics at the 1912 Summer Olympics programme. The competition was held from Saturday, 1912, to Monday, 15 July 1912. Thorpe's gold medal was stripped by the International Olympic Committee in 1913, after the IOC learned that Thorpe had taken expense money for playing baseball, violating Olympic amateurism rules, before the 1912 Games." .

ns1:44992 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Malta participated in the Malta in the Eurovision Song Contest 2013 in Malmö, Sweden. Malta Malta in the Eurovision Song Contest 2013 was the national final format developed by PBS to select the Maltese entry for the Malta in the Eurovision Song Contest 2013. The competition consisted of a semi-final and final held on 2013 and 2013, respectively, at the Malta Fairs & Conventions Centre in the nation's capital city of Valletta. Among the artists shortlisted were former Maltese Eurovision entrants William Mangion who represented Malta in 1993, Miriam Christine who represented Malta in Malta in the Eurovision Song Contest and Fabrizio Faniello who represented Malta in 2001 and 2006." .

ns1:44995 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The August 1942 Dunbeath Air Crash involved the loss of a Mark 3 Short S.25 Sunderland that crashed in the Scottish Highlands on a headland known as Eagle's Rock (Creag na h-Iolaire) near Dunbeath, Caithness, on 25 August 1942." .

ns1:45003 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The women's Laser Radial class at the 2014 ISAF Sailing World Championships – Laser Radial was held in Santander, Spain 12 September–18 September." .

ns1:45004 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1622 North Guyuan earthquake struck Ningxia, People's Republic of China on 25 October 1622 with a Richter magnitude of 7.0 and a maximum Mercalli intensity of X (Extreme). It was the only recorded big earthquake in western People's Republic of China for 148 years, between 1561 and 1709." .

ns1:45005 a ns1:context_narration ;
