ns1:45026 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Meath Senior Football Championship is the 121st edition of the Meath GAA's premier club Gaelic football tournament for senior graded teams in County Meath, Ireland, and also the 60th anniversary of the first use of the Keegan Cup, won by Navan O'Mahonys first in 1954. On 2013, Summerhill GFC claimed their 7th Senior Championship title, when defeating Na Fianna 1-13 to 1-10 in Pairc Tailteann, Navan." .

ns1:45027 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1951–52 season was the 37th in the history of the 1951–52 Isthmian League, an English association football competition. Leytonstone F.C. were champions for the third season in a row, winning their eighth 1951–52 Isthmian League title." .

ns1:45028 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tenshō Iga War (天正伊賀の乱, Tenshō Iga no Ran) is the name of two invasions of Iga Province by the Oda clan during the Sengoku period." .

ns1:45033 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "killing of Kevin McDaid was a community worker in Coleraine, Northern Ireland who was killed by a mob outside his home in 01 May 2009." .

ns1:45040 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 Coyote Lake earthquake occurred at 10:05:24 local time on 06 August 1979 with a moment magnitude of 5.7 and a maximum Mercalli Intensity of VII (Very strong)." .

ns1:45042 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1894 Meiji Tokyo earthquake (明治東京地震, Meiji-Tokyo jishin) occurred in Tokyo, Japan at 14:04 PM on 20 June 1894. The earthquake had its epicenter in Tokyo Bay, with a magnitude of 6.6 on the Richter magnitude scale. The death toll was 31 killed and 157 injured. The earthquake was mentioned by author Ichiyō Higuchi in her work Mizu-no-ue no nikki, in which she described damage to buildings in Yotsuya, and soil liquefaction in the Mita area of downtown Tokyo. By 1894, Tokyo and Yokohama had numerous foreign residents, many of whom commented on the earthquake in their writings and diaries. The National Science Museum of Japan in Tokyo has a collection of twenty two photographs of the earthquake in the form of albumen papers, lantern slides and dry plates." .

ns1:45046 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003–04 La Liga season, the 73rd since its establishment, started on 30 August 2003 and finished on 23 May 2004." .

ns1:45047 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1956 Scottish Cup Final in association football was played on 21 April 1956 at Hampden Park in Glasgow and was the final of the 71st staging of the Scottish Cup. Heart of Midlothian F.C. and Celtic F.C. contested the match. The match was won 3-1 by Heart of Midlothian F.C.." .

ns1:45052 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010–11 FC Braşov season was SR Brașov's third season in Liga I since their return to top-flight football in 2008." .

ns1:45058 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Danghangpo was a naval engagement during the Japanese invasions of Korea that resulted in Korean victory." .

ns1:45059 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 Irish Cup was the 134th edition of the premier knock-out cup competition in Northern Ireland association football since its introduction in 1881. The competition began on 07 September 2013 with the first round and ended on 03 May 2014 with the final. Regional league clubs from level 4 and below on the Northern Ireland association football league system entered in the first round and played against other regional league clubs in the first three rounds." .

