ns1:45093 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "M 24 was a political movement in the People's Republic of the Congo." .

ns1:45095 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1915 Avezzano earthquake or 1915 Fucino earthquake occurred on 13 January 1915 in central Italy at 07:52:42 local time. Central and southern Italy in particular have been struck by deadly earthquakes in the last 300 years, with the deadliest earthquake dating back to at least the 1693 Sicily earthquake. The earthquake had an estimated magnitude of 7.0–7.5 Ms, recalculated as 6.7 Mw. The earthquake took place at around 8:00 local time affecting thousands of people throughout central and southern Italy; the shaking was even felt in Rome. Damage of the earthquake was distributed throughout central and southern Italy." .

ns1:45101 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 NBL Canada season was the inaugural season of the National Basketball League of Canada." .

ns1:45104 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Asian Taekwondo Championships were the 22nd edition of the Asian Taekwondo Championships, and was scheduled from April 18 to 20, 2016 at the Marriott Convention Center Grand Ballroom in Pasay, Metro Manila, Philippines." .

ns1:45109 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 420, adopted on 30 November 1977, considered a report by the Secretary-General regarding the United Nations Disengagement Observer Force." .

ns1:45110 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Teen USA 2017 was the 35th Miss Teen USA pageant held at the Phoenix Symphony Hall in Phoenix, Arizona on 2017." .

ns1:45111 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Creole case was a slave rebellion aboard the American slave ship Creole in 01 November 1841, when the brig was seized by the enslaved persons onboard the ship, freeing 128 slaves who were aboard the ship when it reached Nassau in the British colony of the Bahamas where slavery was abolished. The Creole case generated diplomatic tension between the United Kingdom and the United States of America, and political rumblings within the United States of America." .

ns1:45120 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 34th Japan Academy Prize (第34回日本アカデミー賞) is the 34th edition of the Japan Academy Film Prize, an award presented by the Nippon Academy-Sho Association to award excellence in filmmaking. It awarded the best films of 2010 and it took place on 18 February 2011 at the Grand Prince Hotel New Takanawa in Tokyo, Japan." .

ns1:45130 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 772, adopted unanimously on 17 August 1992, after recalling Resolution 765 (1992) concerning the Boipatong massacre in South Africa and a report from the Secretary-General, the Council authorised Boutros Boutros-Ghali to deploy observers to the country after concerns raised in the report, known as the United Nations Observer Mission in South Africa." .

ns1:45132 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009–10 NBA season was the 64th season of the National Basketball Association (National Basketball Association). During the National Basketball Association All-Star Weekend, Nate Robinson of the New York Knicks won the Sprite Slam Dunk Contest for the third time in his career; Kevin Durant, who also won the inaugural event, won this year's H.O.R.S.E Competition and Boston's Paul Pierce beat rookie Stephen Curry to win the Three-Point Shootout. The 2009–10 NBA season was broadcast in the United States by ABC, ESPN, TNT and National Basketball Association TV." .

ns1:45133 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 European Beach Volleyball Championships were held from August 29 to 2003 in Alanya, Turkey." .

ns1:45137 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Women's South American Volleyball Championship was the 31st edition of the South American Volleyball Championship (women) held in Cartagena and organised by South America's governing volleyball body, the Confederación Sudamericana de Voleibol (CSV)." .

ns1:45147 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Arab Volleyball Clubs Champions Championship was the 32nd edition of Arab world's premier club volleyball tournament held in Tunis and Sidi Bou Said." .

ns1:45148 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 NC State Wolfpack football team represented North Carolina State University during the 2008 NCAA Division I FBS football season. The Wolfpack played its home games in 2008 at Carter–Finley Stadium in Raleigh, North Carolina, which has been NC State football's home stadium since 1966." .

ns1:45150 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Junior Iditarod Sled Dog Race, or Junior Iditarod, is a 148- to 158-mile (222 km) sled dog racing for mushers between the ages of 14 through 17, which is patterned after the 1,150-mile Iditarod Trail Sled Dog Race that is said to be 1,049 miles (1,688.2 km). With the encouragement of \"Go for it\" Joe Redington, Senior, the Junior Iditarod was established 1977 by Eric Beeman, Rome Gilman, Karl Clausen, Kenny Pugh, and Clarence Shockley, who were unable to compete in the Iditarod because they were less than 18 years of age. Junior Iditarod mushers are mostly from Alaska, though the U.S. states of Minnesota and Montana Montana, Massachusetts, Ohio, Georgia, Washington, Pennsylvania, Yukon Territory, Canada, have been represented, and Thomas Krejci of Czechoslovakia became the first international competitor in 1992, also winning the Humanitarian Award that year." .

ns1:45153 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Apple Inc. v. Pepper, 587 U.S. ___ (2019), was a United States Supreme Court case related to antitrust laws related to third-party resellers." .

ns1:45154 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The United Nations Security Council election, 2005 was held on 10 October 2005 during the 60th session of the United Nations General Assembly, held at United Nations Headquarters in New York City." .

ns1:45155 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Russian Professional Rugby League season was the sixth edition of Russia's newly formatted top-flight rugby union competition, the Russian Rugby Championship (\"Russian Rugby Championship\"). The 2010 Russian Rugby Championship season has seen a transition to a traditional one league round-robin format with 8 teams taking place between May and 2010. The 2010 edition of the Russian Rugby Championship saw the dropping of the first phase of the season, which split the league into East and West sections and saw the involvement of several amateur teams." .

ns1:45179 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Strikeforce: Melendez vs. Thomson was a mixed martial arts event promoted by Strikeforce. The event took place at the HP Pavilion at San Jose in San Jose, California on Friday, 27 June 2008." .

ns1:45185 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Sri Lankan parliamentary election was held on 17 August 2015, ten months ahead of schedule, to elect 225 members to Sri Lanka's 15th Parliament." .

ns1:45187 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Festival de Cornouaille (or just Cornouaille Kemper) is an annual festival taking place in the city of Quimper, located in the south-west of Brittany (France) in July (close at the 4th Sunday of the month). The festival has been held since 1923 and is one of the biggest cultural events in Brittany. About 180 shows, concerts and animations take place in the day and in the evening in the urban heart of the city of Quimper: \"a festival in the heart of a city and a culture\". For 1992, the famous guitarist Dan Ar Braz, who comes from Quimper, was asked to organize musical part of the festival : this resulted in the Héritage des Celtes project, in which 70 Celtic musicians worked together." .

ns1:45189 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Chișinău Marathon is an annual marathon and sport event hosted by the city of Chișinău, Moldova since 2015. In 2015, about 10,000 people participated, of whom almost 1,400 took the main three distances and 140 - the marathon. Journalists noticed among the participants the Mayor of Chișinău - Dorin Chirtoacă, the Head of Economic Department of EU Delegation to the Republic of Moldova - Wicher Slagter and the British Ambassador - Philip Batson." .

ns1:45190 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Formula Renault UK season was the 15th British Formula Renault Championship." .

ns1:45191 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 26th Directors Guild of America Awards, honoring the outstanding directorial achievements in film and television in 1973, were presented on 16 March 1974, at the Beverly Hilton Hotel." .

ns1:45196 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 6th Empire Awards ceremony, presented by the British film magazine Empire, honored the best films of 2000 and took place on 19 February 2001." .

ns1:45199 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 220 was a mixed martial arts event produced by the Ultimate Fighting Championship that was held on 20 January 2018, at TD Garden in Boston, Massachusetts." .

ns1:45202 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1875 Greek legislative election were held in Greece on 18 July 1875." .

ns1:45210 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 London Marathon was the 35th running of the annual marathon race in London, England, which took place on Sunday, 26 April 2015. It was the third time that McFadden had set a course record in London and it was her first global marathon title." .

ns1:45211 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013-14 Ukrainian Hockey Championship was the 22nd annual edition of the Ukrainian Hockey Championship." .

ns1:45212 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Queensland Cup season was the 13th season of Queensland's top-level statewide rugby league competition run by the Queensland Rugby League. Two new teams entered the Queensland Cup in 2008, as the competition expanded north with the Mackay Cutters and the Northern Pride. The 2008 Queensland Cup regular season featured 22 rounds, with one team receiving a bye in each round." .

ns1:45214 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Patagonian Expedition Race is an annual endurance adventure race that takes place in the remote wilderness of Chile Patagonia, run to help protect and raise awareness about the fragile environment in this region. Created by geologist Stjepan Pavicic, a pioneer of Chile Patagonia, the first race was run in 2004 and since then athletes from 26 different nations have taken part. Each edition takes place on a different course through the most remote and untouched regions of Chile Patagonia. The race is organized by NIGSA (Nómadas International Group S.A.), formerly known as, Nómadas Outdoor Services Ltda., an organization located in Punta Arenas, working for the goals of environmental protection and the advancement of eco-tourism in the region of Chile Patagonia. The mission of the race is to raise international awareness of the fragile environment of Chile Patagonia. Stjepan Pavicic, Race Director, explains: \"From the beginning, we have focused on creating an experience that is not only a physical and mental challenge, but one that sends a real message: we must protect and preserve this remote and pristine region of Chile Patagonia. Eventually the new trails will allow international tourists access to this region's unique features, increasing eco-tourism in Chile Patagonia. 2007: The longest race of its kind in history took the teams 1,112 km through the southern region of Chile Patagonia, from Torres del Paine National Park all the way to Puerto Williams on the Navarino Island. The race is also supported by the Chile Government, with the aim of promoting sustainable adventure travel in Chile Patagonia. The Patagonian Expedition Race entered an official partnership agreement with the Olympic Committee of Chile (Comité Olímpico de Chile, COCH) in October 2007." .

ns1:45216 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 2021, the decennial United Kingdom Census 2021, called Census 2021, will occur throughout most of the United Kingdom, with the rest of the nation being enumerated in 2022. The United Kingdom Census 2011 was the first decennial census in the United Kingdom to include the option of completing the census documentation online. Although it is a Crown Dependency, and not part of the United Kingdom, Jersey will carry out a census on the same day as the 2021 UK census." .

ns1:45220 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988 Brabantse Pijl was the 28th edition of the Brabantse Pijl cycle race and was held on 27 March 1988." .

ns1:45233 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Panam GP Series season is the revival of Panam GP Series." .

ns1:45242 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Chang-Sat Bangkok Open was a professional tennis tournament played on hardcourt. It took place in Bangkok, Thailand between 13 September 2010 and 2010." .

ns1:45245 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kazakh famine of 1919–1922, also referred to as the Turkestan famine of 1919–1922, was a period of mass starvation and drought that took place in the Kirghiz ASSR (present-day Kazakhstan) and Turkestan Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic as a result of war communism policy, in which 400,000 to 750,000 peasants died. The event was part of the greater Russian famine of 1921–22 that affected other parts of the Soviet Union, in which up to 5,000,000 people died in total. The famine was caused by severe intermittent drought conditions, aggravated by the Russian Civil War and the policy of Prodrazvyorstka adopted by the Soviet Union government." .

ns1:45246 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 Constitution of Romania was drafted by a committee of the Great National Assembly (MAN) and approved by a plenary session of the Central Committee of the Romanian Communist Party on 1965. It was Romania's sixth constitution, and the third of the Communist era." .

ns1:45249 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1953 Yugoslav Cup was the 7th season of the top association football knockout competition in SFR Yugoslavia, the Yugoslav Cup (Serbo-Croatian: Kup Jugoslavije), also known as the \"Marshal Tito Cup\" (Kup Maršala Tita), since its establishment in 1946." .

ns1:45251 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lebanon competed at the Lebanon at the 2012 Summer Paralympics in London, United Kingdom from August 29 to 2012. Lebanese Paralympian, Edward Maalouf, who was sponsored by the British Embassy in Beirut, became the only qualified Paralympic athlete representing Lebanon at the London 2012 Paralympics." .

ns1:45254 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1923 Estonian parliamentary election were held in Estonia between 5 07 May 1923 and 07 May 1923." .

ns1:45268 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "social realism was an art movement that came to the fore in the USA between the two world wars and was a reaction to the increasing hardship for ordinary people. social realism traces back to 19th-century European Realism, including the art of Honoré Daumier, Gustave Courbet and Jean-François Millet. In the more limited meaning of the term, Social Realism with roots in European Realism became an important art movement during the Great Depression in the United States in the 1930s. social realism has been summarized as follows: Social Realism developed as a reaction against idealism and the exaggerated ego encouraged by Romanticism. Social Realism became an important art movement during the Great Depression in the United States in the 1930s. Socialist Realism, representing socialist ideologies, was an art movement that represented social and political contemporary life in the 1930s, from a left-wing standpoint." .

ns1:45273 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The diving at the 1988 Summer Olympics – men's 3 metre springboard, also reported as springboard diving, was one of four diving events on the diving at the 1988 Summer Olympics programme." .

ns1:45282 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017–18 Nicholls State Colonels men's basketball team represented Nicholls State University during the 2017–18 NCAA Division I men's basketball season. 2017–18 Nicholls State 2016–17 Nicholls State Colonels men's basketball team women's basketball team." .

ns1:45291 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Colorado gubernatorial election was held on 03 November 1998 to select the governor of the state of Colorado. The Republican nominee, Colorado Treasurer Bill Owens, narrowly defeated the Democratic nominee, Colorado Lieutenant Governor Gail Schoettler, to flip the seat to the Republicans for the first time in 24 years." .

ns1:45296 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Irish Professional Championship was a professional invitational snooker tournament which took place in 25 September 2007. The tournament was held at the Red Cow Exhibition Centre in Dublin, and featured sixteen exclusively Ireland and Northern Ireland players." .

ns1:45297 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Copa del Rey de Baloncesto 2011–12 was the 76th edition of the Copa del Rey de Baloncesto. It was managed by the ACB League and was held in Barcelona, in the Palau Sant Jordi on 16 February 2012–19." .

ns1:45300 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The September 1988 Haitian coup d'état took place on 18 September 1988, when a group of non-commissioned officers in the Haiti Presidential Guard overthrew General Henri Namphy and brought General Prosper Avril to power. Namphy had overthrown Manigat in the June 1988 Haiti coup d'état when Manigat sought to exercise his constitutional right to control military assignments." .

ns1:45303 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Tripoli occurred in 1551 when the Ottomans besieged and vanquished the Knights of Malta in the fortress of Tripoli, modern Libya. The siege culminated in a six-day bombardment and the surrender of the city on 15 August 1551. The Siege of Tripoli succeeded an earlier attack on Malta in July, which was repelled, and the successful invasion of Gozo, in which 5,000 Christian captives were taken and brought on galleys to the location of Tripoli. The French Ambassador to the Ottoman Empire, Gabriel d'Aramon, joined the Ottoman fleet at Tripoli, with two galleys and a galliot, The declared mission of the ambassador was to dissuade the Ottomans from capturing the city, at the request of the Grand Master of Malta, as Malta was not identified as an enemy in the Franco-Ottoman alliance against the Habsburgs." .

ns1:45310 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ram fighting is a blood sport between two rams (large-horned male sheep), held in a ring or open field." .

ns1:45319 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Jerusalem tractor attack was a terrorist ramming attack that occurred on 04 August 2014, when a man drove an excavator type of tractor out of a construction site, injuring several pedestrians and killing one man before ramming the tractor into a public bus, overturning the bus and then hitting it repeatedly. The attack took place following a month that had seen over 360 attacks on Jews, a spate that was thought by The Jerusalem Post to have \"peaked\" on 04 August 2014 with this attack and the shooting of a uniformed soldier in the French Hill neighborhood, leading to an increase in security in the city." .

ns1:45325 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1969 French Open was a tennis tournament that was held at the Stade Roland-Garros in Paris in France from May 26 through 1969." .

ns1:45340 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Kerala Sahitya Akademi Award was announced on 11 July 2013." .

ns1:45342 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Portland Rose Festival is an annual civic festival held during the month of June in Portland, Oregon. It is organized by the volunteer non-profit Portland Rose Festival Association with the purpose of promoting the Portland region. In 1905, Portland Mayor Harry Lane is remembered for his rousing speech at the Lewis and Clark Exposition, telling the large crowd that Portland needed a \"festival of roses\". In 1907, Portland hosted its first official Portland Rose Festival. The 1907 festival also included an \"electric parade\" with illuminated floats; this evolved into the Merrykhana Parade but after a two-season suspension was renamed the Starlight Parade in 1976. The festival also hosts the Starlight Parade, a fireworks display, and carnival rides along the Portland waterfront, among other events." .

ns1:45348 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Cork Intermediate Hurling Championship was the 107th staging of the Cork Intermediate Hurling Championship since its establishment by the Cork County Board in 1909. The championship began on 2016 and ended on 30 October 2016. On 30 October 2016, Fr. O'Neill's GAA won the championship following a 1-18 to 0-14 defeat of Kildorrery in a replay of the final." .

ns1:45350 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999–2000 Taça de Portugal was the 60th edition of the Portuguese association football knockout tournament, organized by the Portuguese Football Federation (FPF). The 1999–2000 Taça de Portugal began in 01 September 1999. Futebol Clube do Porto defeated Sporting CP, 2–0 in the cup final replay to win their tenth 1999–2000 Taça de Portugal." .

ns1:45352 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Meistriliiga was the 11th season of the Meistriliiga, Estonia's premier football league. Lootus won on away goals and retained their Meistriliiga spot for the 2002 Meistriliiga." .

ns1:45355 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Durban Riot were an anti-Indian pogrom that took place between 1949–1949, primarily by African people targeting Indians in Durban, South Africa. The two days of rioting were exceptionally violent resulting in rape and massacre of Indians, looting, burning of their properties, claiming 142 lives and creating 40,000 Indian refugees. The riots resulted in the massacre of mostly Indians in which 142 people died and 1087 people were injured." .

ns1:45358 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1988–89 Galatasaray S.K. Volleyball season is the 1988–89 volleyball season for Turkey professional basketball club Galatasaray Men's Volleyball Team." .

ns1:45363 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Rammasun, known in the Philippines as Typhoon Butchoy, was recognized as the second typhoon of the 2008 Pacific typhoon season by the Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA) and the Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA). Rammasun was also recognised as the third tropical storm, the second typhoon and the first super typhoon of the 2008 Pacific typhoon season by the Joint Typhoon Warning Center (JTWC). In all, the typhoon killed four people, injured 40 others and caused $9.6 million (2008 USD) worth of damage in both the Philippines and Japan. Typhoon Rammasun's minimum pressure was officially estimated at 915 hPa which tied with Intense Tropical Cyclone Hondo as second strongest storm of 2008. The name was last used in the 2002 Pacific typhoon season, though it was retired in 2015 after Typhoon Rammasun (the same name used for the 2014 season, Typhoon Glenda in the Philippines) left considerable damages in the Philippines, China and Vietnam." .

ns1:45365 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Light Me Up Tour is the first headline tour by the hard rock band The Pretty Reckless." .

ns1:45367 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Millî Görüş (Turkish: , \"National Outlook\" or \"National Vision\") is a religio-political movement and a series of Islamist parties inspired by Necmettin Erbakan. Founded in 1969, the movement claimed to have \"87,000 members across Europe, including 50,000 in Germany,\" as of 2005. In 1969 the Turkish politician Necmettin Erbakan published a manifesto that he gave the title Millî Görüş. It warned against further rapprochement towards Europe, considering the Common Market to be a Zionist and Catholic project for the assimilation and de-Islamization of Turkey and called instead for Pan-Islamism. According to author Banu Eligur, Erbakan and the party \"used the code words national and culture to refer to Islam, and National Vision to refer to the project of Islamism\" as \"it is illegal\" in Turkey \"to use religious symbols for political purposes.\" The name of Millî Görüş would remain associated with a religio-political movement and a series of Islamist parties inspired by Erbakan, one succeeding the other as they were banned for violating Turkey’s secularist legislation. Milli Görüş' public profile shows considerable differences from one country to the next, suggesting that nature of the interaction with the 'host' societies may have as much of an impact on its character as a religious movement as the relationship with the 'mother' movement in Turkey. According to several sources in Germany the attitude of the German branch towards Turkey has completely changed." .

ns1:45369 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988 Open Clarins was a women's tennis tournament played on clay court in Paris, France, and was part of the Category 1 tier of the 1988 WTA Tour. It was the second edition of the tournament and was held from 19 September 1988 until 25 September 1988." .

ns1:45373 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Damascus International Film Festival is the 18th incarnation of the international film festival held in Damascus, Syria which ran from November 7 to 13, 2010. This edition of the Damascus International Film Festival, organised under the patronage of Syrian Minister of Culture Dr. Riad Ismat, opened with a ceremony at the Damascus Opera building, at which Turkish actress Türkan Şoray and Syrian actor Ghassan Massoud were among the guests of honor, and a screening of Honey (Turkish: Bal) directed by Semih Kaplanoğlu." .

ns1:45381 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The shooting at the 1956 Summer Olympics – men's 50 metre rifle, prone was a shooting sport event held as part of the shooting at the 1956 Summer Olympics programme. The competition was held on 1956 at the shooting ranges in Melbourne." .

ns1:45383 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The cycling at the 1988 Summer Olympics – men's individual pursuit was a cycling at the 1988 Summer Olympics event at the 1988 Summer Olympics in Seoul, South Korea which was held between 20 September and 22 September, 1988." .

