ns1:45441 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Truce or Truce of Pläswitz was a nine-week armistice during the Napoleonic Wars, agreed between Napoleon I of France and the Allies on 04 June 1813 (the same day as the Battle of Luckau was being fought elsewhere)." .

ns1:45442 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1976 Taxi Aereo el Venado Douglas DC-4 accident occurred on 15 January 1976 when DC-4 HK-127, crashed 50 km (31 mi) from Bogota when it hit a mountain and was destroyed killing all 13 on board." .

ns1:45443 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 2000 Guineas Stakes was the 203rd running of the 2,000 Guineas Stakes horse racing. It was run over one mile at Newmarket Racecourse on 30 April 2011." .

ns1:45454 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The December 1964 South Vietnamese coup took place before dawn on 19 December 1964, when the ruling military junta of South Vietnam led by General Nguyễn Khánh dissolved the High National Council (HNC) and arrested some of its members." .

ns1:45460 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Toyota Racing Series was the sixth running of the Toyota Racing Series. The Toyota Racing Series is New Zealand's premier open-wheeler motorsport category. The cars were also the category for the 2010 New Zealand Grand Prix, which was held as the third race of the Manfeild Autocourse round." .

ns1:45463 a ns1:context_narration ;
