ns1:45470 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1371, adopted unanimously on 26 September 2001, after reaffirming United Nations Security Council resolution 1244 (1999) and 1345 (2001) on the situation in the former Yugoslavia including Macedonia, the Council called for the full implementation of its Resolution 1345 concerning violence and terrorist activities in Macedonia and southern Serbia." .

ns1:45471 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1966 South African general election were held in South Africa on 30 March 1966." .

ns1:45474 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 36th Saturn Awards, honoring the best in science fiction, fantasy and horror film and television in 2009 were presented on 24 June 2010, in Burbank, California." .

ns1:45477 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Copa do Brasil was the 15th staging of the Copa do Brasil. The competition started on 2003 and concluded on 11 June 2003 with the second leg of the final, held at the Mineirão Stadium in Belo Horizonte, in which Cruzeiro E.C. lifted the trophy for the fourth time with a 3-1 victory over Flamengo." .

ns1:45481 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 FIFA World Youth Championship, known as the 1995 FIFA/Coca-Cola World Youth Championship for sponsorship purposes, was the 10th edition of the FIFA U-20 World Cup. Joseba Etxeberria of Spain won the FIFA U-20 World Cup award for scoring seven goals." .

ns1:45492 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1803 Gatton by-election was a by-election to the House of Commons of the United Kingdom that took place on 24 January 1803." .

ns1:45493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 IFK Göteborg season was IFK Göteborg 110th in existence, their 83rd season in Allsvenskan and their 39th consecutive season in the league. IFK Göteborg also participated in one competition in which the club continued playing in for the 2016 IFK Göteborg season, 2015–16 Svenska Cupen." .

ns1:45502 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1861 Sumatra earthquake occurred on 16 February 1861 and was the last in a sequences of earthquake that ruptured adjacent parts of the Sumatran segment of the Sunda megathrust." .

ns1:45507 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1912 German football championship, the 10th edition of the competition, was won by Holstein Kiel, defeating Karlsruher FV 1–0 in the final. The teams qualified through the regional championships: The quarter-finals, played on 05 May 1912 and 1912: The semi-finals, played on 1912:" .

ns1:45512 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Aaron's 499 was the ninth race of the 2006 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series season. Elliott Sadler won the pole position, while Jimmie Johnson won the race." .

ns1:45519 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Beach Soccer World Cup 1997 was the third edition of the Beach Soccer World Championships, the most prestigious competition in international beach soccer contested by men's national teams until 2005, when the competition was then replaced by the second iteration of a world cup in beach soccer, the better known FIFA Beach Soccer World Cup. For the third consecutive time, the tournament took place at Copacabana Beach in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Hosts Brazil won the tournament for the third time in a row by beating Uruguay 5–2 in what was a repeat of the final in the Beach Soccer World Cup 1996." .

ns1:45525 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Pakistan International Airlines Flight 404 was a Fokker F27 Friendship that disappeared shortly after takeoff on 25 August 1989." .

ns1:45527 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Montichiari (08 May 1373), is one of the most important episodes of the war waged by the papal league led by Gregory XI against the Visconti of Milan, preparing the return of the pope to Rome." .

ns1:45543 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1554, adopted unanimously on 29 July 2004, after reaffirming all United Nations Security Council resolution on Abkhazia and Georgia, particularly Resolution 1524 (2004), the Council extended the mandate of the United Nations Observer Mission in Georgia (UNOMIG) until 31 January 2005." .

ns1:45546 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIS Ski-Flying World Championships 1994 took place on 1994 in Planica, Slovenia for the record fourth time." .

ns1:45547 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The naval Battle of Palermo took place on 02 June 1676 during the Franco-Dutch War, between a French force sent to support a revolt in the city of Messina against the Spanish rule in Sicily, and a Spanish force supported by a Dutch maritime expedition force. As in the Franco-Spanish War of 1635-1659, in the Franco-Dutch War Spain retained its position in Italy and proved able to thwart French hopes of major gains." .

ns1:45549 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Teen USA 1986, the 4th Miss Teen USA pageant, was televised live from Ocean Center, Daytona Beach, Florida on 1986." .

ns1:45553 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1985 Guatemalan general election were held in Guatemala on 03 November 1985, with a second round of the presidential elections taking place on 8 December." .

ns1:45562 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cyclone Beni was an intense tropical cyclone that affected four countries, on its 18-day journey across the South Pacific Ocean during January and 05 February 2003. Later that day RSMC Nadi reported that Beni had explosively developed and peaked as a Category 5 severe tropical cyclone on the Australian scale, with 10-minute sustained winds of 205 km/h (125 mph). The remnant low of Cyclone Beni made landfall near Mackay on 05 February 2003." .

ns1:45563 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dream 11 was a mixed martial arts event promoted by Fighting and Entertainment Group's mixed martial arts promotion Dream held on 06 October 2009." .

ns1:45565 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 Big Sky Conference Men's Basketball Tournament was the twelfth edition, held March 5–7 at the Walkup Skydome at Northern Arizona University in Flagstaff, Arizona." .

ns1:45569 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dau al Set (Catalan pronunciation: ), the first post-World War II artistic movement in Catalonia, was founded in Barcelona in 1948 by poet Joan Brossa. Dau al Set first began as an avant-garde artistic collective led by Joan Brossa, a Catalan poet, in 1948. In an attempt to revive the avant-garde scene in Spain Dau al Set was formed. In 1949, with help from Joan-Josep Tharrats's private printing press, Dau al Set published its first self-entitled magazine journal. The magazine journal was delivered throughout Barcelona to those with subscriptions and served a niche population at the time. During this time from 1953 till 1956 Dau al Set continued to be created and published by Joan-Josep Tharrats. Another influence on Dau al Set was Surrealism, a cultural movement greatly influenced by Dadaism, which began in the 1920s. Dau al Set has had a lasting impact throughout history the most notable being the continuation of the avant-garde in Spain throughout Francoist Spain. Moreover, Dau al Set contributed to the creation of the Informalist movement seen in Spain during the fifties. Also the magical and fantasy elements of Dau al Set was seen to later emerge again in Spain in the eighties." .

ns1:45570 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 603, adopted unanimously on 25 November 1987, considered a report by the Secretary-General regarding the United Nations Disengagement Observer Force." .

ns1:45573 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Elite One is the 57th season of the Cameroon top-tier association football league. Elite One consists of 18 teams for the 2017 season with three clubs relegated to Elite Two and three promoted." .

ns1:45578 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 WNBA All-Star Game was played on 12 July 2003 at Madison Square Garden in New York City, home of the New York Liberty." .

ns1:45580 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 FFA Cup Final was the 2nd final of the premier association football knockout cup competition in Australia. Perth Glory FC qualified for the FFA Cup Final on 2015, with a 3–1 victory over Melbourne City at Nib Stadium. Melbourne Victory qualified for the FFA Cup Final on 2015, with a 3–0 victory over Hume City at AAMI Park. On 2015, Football Federation Australia announced the 2015 FFA Cup Final would be held at either AAMI Park in Melbourne or Perth’s nib Stadium. The choice of venue depended on the result of the second semi-final match between Hume City and Melbourne Victory. If Melbourne Victory defeat Hume City, the 2015 Final would be held at AAMI Park. Melbourne Victory and Perth Glory FC were among 648 teams who entered the inaugural FFA Cup competition, and as A-League clubs, both entered the tournament in the Round of 32. Melbourne doubled the advantage seven minutes later with Carl Valeri playing a through-ball into the path of striker Besart Berisha, whose first touch took him past the final defender and then fired the ball across Perth Glory FC keeper Ante Covic and inside the left post." .

ns1:45584 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Aubervilliers Congress (French: congrès d'Aubervilliers) of the Socialist Party (PS) was held on 07 April 2018 and 08 April 2018 near the Front Populaire station of the Paris Métro in Aubervilliers, Seine-Saint-Denis. On 9 December 2017, the National Council of the Socialist Party (PS) agreed to hold the next party congress near the Front Populaire station of the Paris Métro in Aubervilliers, Seine-Sain7 07 April 2018-Deni8 07 April 2018 07 April 2018. The Aubervilliers Congress took place on 07 April 2018 and 08 April 2018, designating the national leadership of the party." .

ns1:45585 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 ITTF World Tour was the 21st season of the International Table Tennis Federation's professional table tennis world tour. The Super Series events offered the highest prize money and the most points towards the ITTF World Tour standings, which determined the qualifiers for the 2016 ITTF World Tour Grand Finals in December." .

ns1:45602 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2005–06 Liga de Honra season was the 16th season of the competition and the 72nd season of recognised second-tier association football in Portugal. The league was contested by 18 teams with S.C. Beira-Mar winning the championship and gaining promotion to the Primeira Liga along with CD Aves." .

ns1:45603 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016–17 Handball-Bundesliga was the 52nd season of the Handball-Bundesliga, Germany's premier handball league and the 40th season consisting of only one league." .

ns1:45608 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The gymnastics at the 1904 Summer Olympics – men's combined was an artistic gymnastics event held as part of the gymnastics at the 1904 Summer Olympics programme." .

ns1:45611 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 National League Championship Series (NLCS), the second round of the 2005 National League playoffs, matched the Central Division champion and defending league champion St. Louis Cardinals against the wild card qualifier Houston Astros, a rematch of the 2004 NLCS. Both teams also played each other in consecutive National League Championship Series in 2004 and 2005." .

ns1:45612 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The archery at the 1980 Summer Olympics – women's individual at the 1980 Summer Olympics was part of the archery at the 1980 Summer Olympics." .

ns1:45614 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The IIHF Continental Cup 2010 was the 13th edition of the IIHF Continental Cup." .

ns1:45616 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIFA World Player of the Year was an association football award presented annually by the sport's governing body, FIFA, between 1991 and 2015. From 2010 to 2015, the equivalent men's award was the FIFA Ballon d'Or, following a merging of the FIFA World Player of the Year and the France Football Ballon d'Or awards." .

ns1:45620 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1985 Tuvaluan general election were held in Tuvalu on 12 September 1985. The general election was held on 12 September 1985, with nine members re-elected to the Parliament of Tuvalu or Palamene o Tuvalu, including Prime Minister Tomasi Puapua and Finance Minister Henry Naisali." .

ns1:45621 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Soviet occupation of Latvia in 1940 refers to the military occupation of the Republic of Latvia by the Soviet Union under the provisions of the 1939 Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact with Nazi Germany and its Secret Additional Protocol signed in August 1939. On August 22, 1996, the Latvian parliament adopted a declaration which stated that the Soviet occupation of Latvia in 1940 was a military occupation and an illegal incorporation. In spring 1940, 51,000 left Latvia for resettlement in Poland. Four months before the arrival of Soviet troops in Latvia, Vilhelms Munters, addressing an audience at the University of Latvia on 1940, stated, \"We have every reason to describe the relations existing between Latvia and the Soviet Union as very satisfactory. On 1940, all three Baltic parliaments passed initial resolutions on the nationalization of land, followed in Latvia by a Bill of Land Reform a week later. According to the European Court of Human Rights, the Government of Latvia, the United States, and the European Union, the occupation of Latvia by the USSR in 1940, and its subsequent re-incorporation in the Soviet Union in 1944, was illegal. According to this account, the lawful government of Latvia was overthrown in 1940 and Soviet rule was imposed by force. As reported by Time in 1940, those who had failed to have their passports stamped for voting Latvia into the USSR were allowed to be shot in the back of the head by Soviet NKVD, The country remained occupied by the Soviet Union until restoration of its independence in 1991." .

ns1:45629 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1954 Oregon gubernatorial election took place on 02 November 1956, 1954." .

ns1:45631 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Barcelona Open Banc Sabadell (also known as the Torneo Godó) was a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts. It was the 65th edition of Barcelona Open and part of the ATP World Tour 500 series of the 2017 ATP World Tour. It took place at the Real Club de Tenis Barcelona in Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain, from 24 April 2017 through 30 April 2017." .

ns1:45638 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2007 Empress's Cup Final was the 29th final of the Empress's Cup competition. The final was played at Japan National Stadium in Tokyo on January 1, 2008. Nippon TV Beleza won their 8th title, by defeating defending champion Tasaki Perule FC – with Homare Sawa and Eriko Arakawa goal." .

ns1:45639 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Never Ending Tour 2000 is the popular name for Bob Dylan's endless touring schedule since June 7, 1988. The 2000 Never Ending Tour 2000 started in North America with two performances in one day at the Anaheim Sun Theatre in Anaheim, California on 10 March 2000." .

ns1:45642 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1924 Estonian coup d'état attempt (Estonian: 1. detsembri riigipöördekatse), conducted by the Comintern, was a failed coup attempt in Estonia staged by Communists (mostly infiltrated from Soviet Union) on 01 December 1924. From the Soviet occupation of Estonia from 1940 to the era of Perestroika and Glasnost in the Soviet history of the Estonian SSR the communist coup attempt was referred to as Tallinn Uprising of 01 December 1924 against the Yoke of the National Bourgeoisie Government of Estonia and described as an event in the series of World revolution. On 01 December 1924 the Comintern attempted a communist coup in Estonia. In late 1924, about the time the Trial of the 149 concluded, Moscow decided to launch the uprising on 01 December 1924." .

ns1:45643 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Greek Basketball Cup competition was the 40th edition of the top-tier level professional national domestic basketball cup competition of Greece. The competition started on 21 September 2014, and ended on 05 April 2015. Panathinaikos B.C.' Loukas Mavrokefalidis was named the Greek Basketball Cup Most Valuable Player." .

ns1:45649 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006–07 Golden State Warriors season was the 61st National Basketball Association (NBA) season for the Golden State Warriors basketball franchise, and their 34th overall while based in Oakland, California." .

ns1:45656 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 World Wrestling Championships were held in Villeurbanne, France." .

ns1:45664 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Bang and Whimper 2017 - The Farewell Tour was a concert tour by the Finnish gothic rock band HIM. In 2017, HIM held a band meeting at a pub near their rehearsal place, where they discussed the future of the group. In conjunction with the band's announcement to retire, a photo exhibition by Ville Juurikkala, titled HIM: Right Here in My Eyes, was held at the Helsinki Art Museum in 2017, featuring new photographs of the band rehearsing for the farewell tour." .

ns1:45668 a ns1:context_narration ;
