    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 395, adopted unanimously on 25 August 1976, after hearing various points by the Foreign Minister's of Greece and Turkey regarding a territorial dispute in the Aegean Sea, the Council noted the ongoing tension and called on both sides to exercise restraint and enter negotiations." .

ns1:45863 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1571, adopted without a vote on 04 November 2004, after noting the resignation of International Court of Justice (ICJ) judge Gilbert Guillaume taking effect on 11 February 2005, the Council decided that elections to the vacancy on the ICJ would take place on 15 February 2005 at the Security Council and at a meeting of the General Assembly during its 59th session." .

ns1:45865 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Indie Fest is an international film festival. While the festival is based in La Jolla, San Diego, California, United States, the event takes place virtually." .

ns1:45867 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United States v. Paramount Pictures, Inc., 334 U.S. 131 (1948) (also known as the Hollywood Antitrust Case of 1948, the Paramount Case, the Paramount Decision or the Paramount Decree), was a landmark Supreme Court of the United States antitrust case that decided the fate of film studios owning their own theatres and holding exclusivity rights on which theatres would show their movies. The Paramount decision is a bedrock of corporate competition law law and as such is cited in most cases where issues of vertical integration play a prominent role in restricting fair trade." .

ns1:45874 a ns1:context_narration ;
