ns1:45953 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "(Los Angeles Lakers) | television = NBC (U.S.) | announcers = Marv Albert and Doug Collins | HOFers = Lakers:Shaquille O'Neal (2016) Kobe Bryant (2020)76ers:Dikembe Mutombo (2015)Allen Iverson (2016)Coaches:Larry Brown (2002)Phil Jackson (2007)Officials:Dick Bavetta (2015) | radio_network = ESPN | radio_announcers = Brent Musburger and Jack Ramsay | referees_1 = Dick Bavetta, Ron Garretson, Joe Crawford | referees_2 = Steve Javie, Bernie Fryer, Ronnie Nunn | referees_3 = Bennett Salvatore, Bob Delaney, Dan Crawford | referees_4 = Hugh Evans, Jack Nies, Eddie F. Rush | referees_5 = Dick Bavetta, Bernie Fryer, Joe Crawford | ECF result = 76ers defeat Bucks, 4–3 | WCF result = Lakers defeat Spurs, 4–0 }} The 2001 NBA Finals was the NBA Finals of the National Basketball Association (NBA)'s 2000–01 season." .

ns1:45963 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Fernie is a city in the Elk Valley area of the East Kootenay region of southeastern British Columbia, Canada, located on BC Highway 3 on the eastern approaches to the Crowsnest Pass through the Rocky Mountains. Fernie lies on the Elk River, along Canada's southernmost east-west transportation corridor through the Rockies that crosses the range via the Crowsnest Pass, 40 kilometres (25 miles) to the east. Fernie is the only city-class municipality in Canada that is fully encircled by the Rocky Mountains. The Lizard Range is home to Fernie Alpine Resort, one of the largest ski resorts in Canada, and Island Lake Catskiing, a resort. The Flathead Valley avalanche were two avalanche that buried 11 snowmobilers near Fernie on December 28, 2008. On October 17, 2017, there was an ammonia leak at the Fernie Memorial Arena which killed three workers (two 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches employees and one CIMCO refrigeration employee from Calgary) during the Ghostriders' regular season. The 'Riders were relocated because of this to the Elk Valley Leisure Centre in Sparwood, British Columbia during the 2017–18 KIJHL season until the 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches decided what to do. The 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches decided to replace ammonia for a synthetic refrigerant prior to the 2018–19 KIJHL season and moved the team back to the Fernie Memorial Arena. Influenced by chinook winds and being to the west of the continent, Fernie's winters are mild for its latitude in North America, although the climate is a lot more continental than coastal British Columbia." .

ns1:45966 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The St Crispin Street Fair is a fair held periodically in the Market Square of Northampton, England." .

ns1:45968 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The We Will Rock You: 10th Anniversary Tour is world tour started in 25 February 2013, by the We Will Rock You Musical celebrating the musical's tenth anniversary." .

ns1:45981 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Astute was an Australian-led military deployment to East Timor to quell unrest and return stability in the 2006 East Timor crisis. Operation Astute was established at the request of East Timor's government." .

ns1:45982 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Ohio State Buckeyes football team represented Ohio State University during the 2017 NCAA Division I FBS football season. 8 Ohio State Buckeyes (1–1, 1–0) took on the Army Black Knights (2–0) at Ohio Stadium in Columbus, Ohio. 10 Ohio State Buckeyes improved to 3–1 with a 54–21 win at Ohio Stadium over the UNLV Rebels, who fell to 1–2. 9 Ohio State Buckeyes (9–2, 7–1) defeated the Illinois Fighting Illini (2–9, 0–8) by a score of 52–14 to end their Big Ten West match ups for the 2017 regular season and clinch the Big Ten East title as well as a berth in the Big Ten Football Championship Game." .

ns1:45991 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "After discussions on whether Estonia should withdraw due to the Russian participation in the 2008 South Ossetia war in Georgia, Eesti Rahvusringhääling (ERR) announced that, due to public demand, they would participate at the Estonia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009, to be held in Moscow. Eesti Laul 2009 was the first edition of the Estonian national selection Eesti Laul, which selected Estonia's entry for the Estonia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009. Among the competing artists were previous Eurovision Song Contest entrants Köök, who represented Estonia as member of Ruffus in 2003, Laura, who represented Estonia in 2005 as part of the group Suntribe, and Lowry, who represented Estonia as member of 2XL in Estonia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2010 together with Tanel Padar and Dave Benton." .

ns1:46009 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1972 United States presidential election in the District of Columbia took place in order to select the District of Columbia's three electoral votes for President of the United States." .

