ns1:46067 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bombing of Rabaul in February and 1942 occurred when Allied forces launched counter-attacks against the Empire of Japan base at Rabaul, Papua New Guinea. The Japanese captured Rabaul in the Battle of Rabaul in 1942. On 1942, Vice Admiral Brown—under the lead of Admiral Leary en route to the objective—navigated the Southwest Pacific with plans to strike the recently conquered Japanese base in Rabaul, located in New Britain." .

