ns1:46179 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fiestas Patrias, or Peru National Holidays, are celebrations of Peru's independence from the Spanish Empire. They officially consist of two days: The celebration of Fiestas Patrias in Peru coincides with the vacation periods for the local schools as well as some businesses. July 28 in each year commemorates the day that Peru gained its independence. The mass officially begins at 9:00 A.M. On the morning of July 28 representatives of the Congress of the Republic of Peru go to the Government Palace to invite the President to give the traditional Address to the Nation." .

ns1:46186 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Slovakia in the Eurovision Song Contest first attempted to enter the Slovakia in the Eurovision Song Contest 1993 in Millstreet, Ireland, but were unsuccessful in qualifying. The independently recognised countries of Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, Estonia, Hungary, Romania, Slovakia in the Eurovision Song Contest, and Slovenia, took part at the Kvalifikacija za Millstreet which was held at the RTV SLO Broadcasting Centre in Ljubljana, Slovenia on 1993." .

