    rdfs:label "The Battle of Stołowicze was a battle of the Bar Confederation." .

ns1:46275 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A Massachusetts's 5th congressional district special election, 2013 took place on 10 December 2013, due to the resignation of Democratic Congressman Ed Markey following his election to the United States Senate in a special election on June 25, 2013." .

ns1:46277 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 18th International Adana Golden Boll Film Festival (Turkish: 18. Uluslararası Adana Altın Koza Film Festivali) was a film festival held in Adana, Turkey from September 17 to 25, 2011. This edition of the International Adana Film Festival, which was founded in 1969 and is organised by the Adana Metropolitan City Municipality and accredited by FIPRESCI, was the first to accept digital submissions from filmmakers for its national feature competition. The festival also played host to the 1st International Golden Boll Film Congress, coordinated by Dokuz Eylül University Faculty of Fine Arts Film Design Department and headed by Honorary Presidents Ö. Lütfi Akad, at the Adana Seyhan Hotel from September 21 to 24 on the theme of Turkish Cinema: Views from Turkey and the World, and the Adana Cinema Museum, also run by the Adana Metropolitan City Municipality, was officially opened in a restored historic mansion on Şeyhan Street." .

ns1:46280 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 4th 4th African Movie Academy Awards ceremony was held on 26 April 2008 at the Transcorp Hilton Hotel, Abuja, Nigeria, to honor the best African films of 2007." .

ns1:46293 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Canada 1981 is a beauty pageant for young women in Canada. According to the new Miss Canada 1981 and Miss Teen Canada web site, the title was re-established with a focus on personality over physical appearance. The Miss Canada 1981 competition is Canada's oldest extant beauty pageant. Dominique Dufour, the winner of the Miss Canada 1981 Pageant in 1981, co-hosted with Perry from 1982 until 1990. Miss Canada 1982, Karen Baldwin, is the only Miss Canada 1981 to also win Miss Universe." .

ns1:46302 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1983 Israeli presidential election were held in the Knesset on 22 March 1983." .

ns1:46317 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963–64 Georgetown Hoyas men's basketball team represented Georgetown University during the 1963–64 NCAA Division I college basketball season. Georgetown looked forward to having senior guard Jim Christy, the team's point guard and team captain, and junior forward Jim Barry – perhaps the best player of Georgetown men's basketball's \"Classic Era\" (1943–1972) – together again after their high-scoring performances the 1962–63 Georgetown Hoyas men's basketball team, raising hopes that they could lead the team to a postseason tournament berth." .

ns1:46330 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The UEFA Euro 2016 qualifying tournament was a association football competition that was played from 07 September 2014 to 17 November 2015 to determine the 23 Union of European Football Associations member men's national teams joining the automatically qualified host team France in the Union of European Football Associations Euro 2016 final tournament. All Union of European Football Associations member associations were eligible to compete in the qualifying competition, with the host team France qualifying directly to the finals tournament. Union of European Football Associations also stated in their regulations that \"the teams drawn into the group of five teams will have France added to their group for the purpose of playing centralised friendlies\". The seedings were as follows: The first legs were pl12 Novembere14 NovemberNovember, and the second legs were played on 15–17 November 2015. Union of European Football Associations unveiled the branding for the qualifiers on 15." .

ns1:46332 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Radio 1's Big Weekend (previously known as One Big Weekend, for 2012 as Radio 1's Hackney Weekend, and for 2018 as BBC Music's Biggest Weekend) is a music festival run by BBC Radio 1." .

ns1:46358 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "This is a record of the results of the Chile national football team at the Chile at the FIFA World Cup. The Chile at the FIFA World Cup, sometimes called the Football World Cup or the Soccer World Cup, but usually referred to simply as the World Cup, is an international association football competition contested by the men's national teams of the members of Fédération Internationale de Football Association (FIFA), the sport's global governing body. Chile have appeared in nine Chile at the FIFA World Cup finals to date, which were in 1930, 1950, 1962 (which they hosted), 1966, 1974, 1982, 1998, 2010 and 2014." .

ns1:46365 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Men's Youth World Handball Championship was the fourth edition of the world event for youth handballers, which was held in Argentina between 10 August 2011–20 2011. The draw took place at 2011 in Argentina." .

ns1:46366 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Eternal Light, MeK's codename), was the last major military operation of the Iran–Iraq War, conducted by and ending in a decisive victory for Iran. Led by Lieutenant-General Ali Sayad Shirazi, Operation Mersad began on 26 July 1988 and lasted only a few days, whereby the Iranian Armed Forces crushed the MEK in what was the last military operation of any major significance during the war. On 26 July 1988, the MEK, with the support of the Iraqi military, started Operation Forough Javidan (Eternal Light) in central Iran. Operation Mersad was the last land battle of the Iran–Iraq War." .

ns1:46368 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 Rand Grand Prix was a motor race, run to Formula One-style rules, held on 04 December 1965 at Kyalami, South Africa. The race was run over 50 laps of the circuit, and was won by Australian driver Jack Brabham in a Brabham BT11." .

ns1:46369 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hightower (also called Battle of Etowah Cliffs) in 1793 was part of the Chickamauga Wars, in which the Cherokee sought to defend tribal territory from increasing settlement by the citizens of the new United States." .

ns1:46377 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The year 2014 is the 3rd year in the history of the Glory, an international kickboxing event. 2014 starts with Glory 14: Zagreb, and ends with Glory 18: Oklahoma. Glory 14: Zagreb was a kickboxing event held on March 8, 2014 at the Arena Zagreb in Zagreb, Croatia. Glory 15: Istanbul was a kickboxing event held on April 12, 2014 at the Ülker Sports Arena in Istanbul, Turkey. Glory 16: Denver was a kickboxing event held on May 3, 2014 at the 1stBank Center in Broomfield, Colorado, USA. Glory 17: Los Angeles was a kickboxing event held on June 21, 2014 at The Forum in Inglewood, California, USA. Glory 18: Oklahoma was a kickboxing event, held on November 7, 2014 at the Grand Casino Hotel Resort in Shawnee, Oklahoma, USA." .

ns1:46381 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1992 Nauruan parliamentary election were held in Nauru on 14 November 1992." .

ns1:46384 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fossavatn Ski Marathon is an annual ski marathon held in Ísafjörður, northwestern Iceland, and is part of Worldloppet since 2014. In 2005 this 50 km marathon was added to the FIS, and that same year Fossavatn became a founding partner of the FIS Nordic Ski Marathon Cup, a series which includes the Holmenkollen Skimaraton in Norway, Tornedalsloppet in Sweden, Oulun Tervahiihto in Finland and the Fossavatn Ski Marathon in Iceland." .

ns1:46386 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Nuremberg or Siege of Nürnberg was a battle campaign that took place in 1632 about the Holy Roman Empire City of Nuremberg during the Thirty Years' War. In 1632, rather than face the numerically superior Holy Roman Empire army under the command of Albrecht von Wallenstein, Gustavus Adolphus of Sweden ordered a tactical retreat into the city of Nuremberg. Wallenstein's army immediately started to invest Nuremberg and laid siege to the city, waiting for hunger and epidemics to cripple the Swedish force." .

ns1:46388 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1142, adopted unanimously on 04 December 1997, after recalling resolutions 1105 (1997) and 1110 (1997), the Council extended the mandate of the United Nations Preventive Deployment Force (UNPREDEP) in Macedonia until 31 August 1998." .

ns1:46393 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Lega Pro is the second season of the unified Lega Pro division. Clubs will include 2 sides relegated from the 2014–15 Serie B season, 43 sides playing the 2014–15 Divisione Unica season, and 9 sides promoted from the 2014–15 Serie D season. Moreover, the Federal Council also reduced the league from 60 teams to 54 teams, making there was 2 vacancies left on 25 August." .

ns1:46400 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "As in previous years, the 1961 Thomas Cup – Pan American Zone qualifiers of the 1961 Thomas Cup were limited to a dual meet between the United States and Canada that was won as always by the former team. These games were held at Toronto, Canada, on the 1961 and 1961." .

ns1:46401 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lisfe is an annual short film festival held in the city of Leiden, The Netherlands. Lisfe (previously known as Leiden International Short Film Experience, LISFE) was founded in 2009 as a cineclub and has grown to become one of the Netherland's largest international short film festivals. Lisfe started off in 2009 as a spin-off of the University of Leiden Student Cinema Club. Next to the main festival in spring, Lisfe is involved in cultural events throughout the year in collaboration with several organizations in Leiden and surroundings." .

ns1:46405 a ns1:context_narration ;
