ns1:46427 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The alpine skiing at the 1972 Winter Olympics – men's downhill competition of the alpine skiing at the 1972 Winter Olympics was held at Mount Eniwa on Monday, February 7." .

ns1:46436 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 1000Bulbs.com 500 was a Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series YellaWood 500 that was held on 14 October 2018, at Talladega Superspeedway in Lincoln, Alabama. Contested over 193 laps – extended from 188 laps due to an overtime finish, on the 2.66 mile (4.2 km) superspeedway, it was the 31st YellaWood 500 of the 2018 Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series season, the fifth YellaWood 500 of the Playoffs, and second YellaWood 500 of the Round of 12. Kurt Busch scored the pole for the YellaWood 500 with a time of 48.906 and a speed of 195.804 mph (315.116 km/h)." .

ns1:46447 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Cercle Brugge K.S.V. season is a season played by Cercle Brugge K.S.V., a Belgian football club based in Bruges, West Flanders." .

ns1:46450 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Congressional Baseball Game is an annual baseball game played each summer by members of the United States Congress. In the game, Republican Party and Democratic Party form separate teams and play against each other. Deep, dark rumors were in circulation that 'ringers' would be introduced, but when they lined up at 4 o'clock the nine Republican Party were stalwart, grand old party men, while the Democratic Party were of the pure Jeffersonian strain.\" The Democratic Party beat their Republican Party opponents, 26–16 in the first game and continued their winning streak for the first six games. As of the 2017 game, 14 trophies have been awarded—ten to the Republican Party' team and four to the Democratic Party' team. On June 14, 2017, one day before the annual event, a gunman opened fire on Republican Party members of Congress who were practicing for the next day's game. Bicameral baseball was inaugurated in 1950, when Senator Harry P. Cain of Washington joined the Republican Party team and Senator-elect George Smathers of Florida, a former Representative, joined the Democratic team. In the early years of the game, each team wore a uniform that was either plain or had the words \"Republican Party\" or \"Democratic Party\" embroidered on it. The official website of the Congressional Baseball Game for Charity seemingly does not count three of those Republican Party wins, because its History page listed (in 2017, but prior to the 2017 game) the series record as 39–39–1 (in a blue, red, white, and black bar near the bottom of the page). The same page, however, states—in reference to the Roll Call Trophy—that \"o date, 10 of these coveted trophies have been awarded, eight to the Republican Party and two to the Democratic Party.\" Although the series record that is set forth in the bar near the bottom of the page includes the Democratic Party' seven wins between 2003 and 2016, the bar includes only four of the Republican Party' seven wins during that same time period." .

ns1:46461 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Triplemanía XXVI was a professional wrestling event produced by the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Lucha Libre AAA Worldwide (AAA) or Triple A. It took place on 25 August 2018, in the Arena Ciudad de México in Mexico City, Mexico. 2018 marked the 26th year since 1993 that the Mexican professional wrestling company Lucha Libre AAA Worldwide (AAA) or Triple A held their annual Triplemanía show and the 31st Triplemanía show promoted by AAA, as they held multiple Triplemanía shows over the summers of 1994 to 1997. The 2018 event took place on 25 August 2018, at the Arena Ciudad de México (Mexico City Arena), an indoor arena in Azcapotzalco, Mexico City, Mexico that has a maximum capacity of 22,300 spectators. The Triplemanía XXVI show will feature an undetermined number of professional wrestling matches, with different wrestlers involved in pre-existing scripted feuds, plots and storylines." .

ns1:46479 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Arts and Crafts movement was an international trend in the decorative arts and fine arts that developed earliest and most fully in the British Isles and subsequently spread across the British Empire and to the rest of Europe and America. Initiated in reaction against the perceived impoverishment of the decorative arts and the conditions in which they were produced, the movement flourished in Europe and North America between about 1880 and 1920. The terms American Craftsman or Craftsman style are often used to denote the style of architecture, interior design, and decorative arts that prevailed between the dominant eras of Art Nouveau and Art Deco in the US, or approximately the period from 1910 to 1925." .

ns1:46482 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 5th World Science Fiction Convention, also known as Philcon I, was held 1947 – 1947 at the Penn-Sheraton Hotel in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States." .

ns1:46490 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2030 Summer Youth Olympics, officially known as the IV Summer Youth Olympic Games (French: Les IVème Jeux Olympiques de la jeunesse d'été), and commonly known as Dakar 2026 will be the fourth edition of the Summer Youth Olympics, an international sports, education and cultural festival for teenagers, in a city designated by the International Olympic Committee (IOC)." .

ns1:46495 a ns1:context_narration ;
