ns1:46689 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fall of Kabul took place in 2001 during the Afghanistan War. Coupled with the fall of Mazar-i-Sharif five days earlier, the capture of Kabul was a significant blow to Taliban control of Afghanistan." .

ns1:46690 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 Masters was a professional non-ranking snooker tournament that took place from Tuesday 27 January to Sunday 1981 at the Wembley Conference Centre in London, England. Alex Higgins reached his fourth consecutive Masters final by defeating Cliff Thorburn 6–5 in the semi-finals, despite having trailed 1–5." .

ns1:46697 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Belgian Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held at Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps on 22 May 1983. It was the first Belgian Grand Prix to be held at Spa since 1970 and the first on the modern Spa circuit, and was also the sixth race of the 1983 Formula One season. The 40-lap race was won from pole position by Alain Prost, driving a factory Renault." .

ns1:46698 a ns1:context_narration ;
