ns1:46707 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Railroad Strike of 1922, commonly known as the Railway Shopmen's Strike, was a nationwide strike of railroad workers in the United States of America. Launched on 01 July 1922, by seven of the sixteen railroad labor organizations in existence at the time, the strike continued into the month of August before collapsing. The collective action of some 400,000 workers in the summer of 1922 was the largest railroad work stoppage since the American Railway Union's Pullman Strike of 1894 and the biggest American strike of any kind since the Great Steel Strike of 1919. Seven unions representing the railroad shopmen and maintenance of way workers voted to go on strike, however, and the date 01 July 1922, was set for the launch of a coordinated work stoppage. In the Eastern United States of America, a number of railroads attempted to bring pressure to end the strike by stripping strikers of seniority rights." .

ns1:46708 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Women's Roller Hockey South American Club Championship is an annual roller hockey club competition organized by CSP (South American Roller Confederation) with the most successful women's teams of South America." .

ns1:46722 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Black Company or the Black Troops (German: Schwarze Haufen) was a unit of Franconia farmers and knights that fought on the side of the peasants during the German Peasants' War in the 1520s, during the Protestant Reformation in Germany. The Black Company was formed in 1525 in Rothenburg, out of local, home guard farmers - maybe 600 men - and a company of mercenary knights. The leader of the Black Company, at least nominally, was nobleman Florian Geyer. In the Battle of Ingolstadt, in 1525, the Black Company found itself alone against the forces of the Swabian League after its allies had been destroyed." .

ns1:46726 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 South American Cross Country Championships took place on 21 February 2009. The races were held at the Parque del Stadio Italiano in Coronel, near Concepción, Bío Bío, Chile." .

