ns1:46762 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "ice hockey at the ice hockey at the 1986 Asian Winter Games took place in the city of Sapporo, Japan. The competition was held at the Tsukisamu Gymnasium from 1 to 8 March." .

ns1:46768 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Bosch Spark Plug Grand Prix was the fourth round of the 1999 CART season, held on 02 May 1999, on the Nazareth Speedway in Nazareth, Pennsylvania. Juan Pablo Montoya followed up on his win in Long Beach by taking his first CART pole in Nazareth, beating Hélio Castroneves by the minute margin of one-thousandth of a second." .

ns1:46772 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 MTV Video Music Aid Japan were held in Chiba on 25 June 2011 at the Makuhari Messe." .

ns1:46776 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1948 United States presidential election in Oklahoma took place on 02 November 1948. In the landslide election of 1952 United States presidential election in Oklahoma and 1956, Adlai Stevenson II won no antebellum free-soil or postbellum state; however Oklahoma remained more Democratic than the nation as a whole. As of the 2020 presidential election, this is the last occasion where Oklahoma did not go for the same candidate as neighboring Kansas." .

ns1:46783 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1930 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election occurred on 1930. Republican candidate and former governor Gifford Pinchot defeated Democratic candidate John M. Hemphill to win a second, non-consecutive term as Governor of Pennsylvania. In 1926, Gifford Pinchot (then Governor of Pennsylvania) and William Scott Vare (U.S. Representative and boss of the powerful Philadelphia political machine) both challenged incumbent United States Senator George W. Pepper in the Republican primary." .

ns1:46786 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Japanese Super Cup has been held on 2014 between the 2013 J. League champions Sanfrecce Hiroshima and the 2013 Emperor's Cup winners Yokohama F. Marinos." .

ns1:46787 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Acrobatic Gymnastics European Championships are the main acrobatic gymnastics championships in Europe." .

ns1:46795 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The BET Awards 2009 took place at the Shrine Auditorium in Los Angeles, California on 2009. The nominations were announced 2009 during 106 & Park's 2009 BET Award Nominations Special. On 2009, American recording artist and entertainer Michael Jackson succumbed to cardiac arrest just three days before the award ceremony aired. In honor of Jackson, BET announced, through their website, \"With the untimely passing of an incomparable legend, the 2009 BET Awards will be shifting gears to honor the late Michael Jackson and his contributions to not only the music industry, but to the entire world. The 2009 BET Awards will be dedicated to the life, legacy and legend of music icon, Michael Jackson\"." .

ns1:46800 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Virginia Slims of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts at the Manhattan Country Club in Manhattan Beach, California in the United States that was part of the 1983 Virginia Slims World Championship Series. The tournament was held from 08 August 1983 through 14 August 1983." .

ns1:46812 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 The Dominion Curling Club Championship was held from November 19 to 24 at the Scarboro Golf and Country Club in Scarborough, Ontario." .

ns1:46816 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Uruguay banking crisis was a major banking crisis that hit Uruguay in 2002." .

ns1:46827 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final was the 104th All-Ireland Final and the culmination of the All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1991, an inter-county hurling tournament for the top teams in Ireland. The match was held at Croke Park, Dublin, on 1991, between Tipperary and Kilkenny. The All-Ireland hurling final was the final match of the All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1991. The match was contested by Tipperary and Kilkenny on 1991 at Croke Park, Dublin, and had an attendance of 64,500." .

ns1:46832 a ns1:context_narration ;
