ns1:46905 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of El Buggar Ridge took place on 27 October 1917, when one infantry regiment and cavalry troops of the Yildirim Army Group, attacked the 8th Mounted Brigade of the Egyptian Expeditionary Force (EEF) in the last days of the stalemate in Southern Palestine during the Sinai and Palestine campaign of World War I." .

ns1:46906 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The CECAFA Women's Championship, also called Women's Challenge Cup, is an association football tournament for teams from Eastern Africa organized by CECAFA (CECAFA)." .

ns1:46912 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Treaty of Paris (formally the Treaty establishing the European Coal and Steel Community) was signed on 18 April 1951 between France, Italy, West Germany, and the three Benelux countries (Belgium, Luxembourg, and the Netherlands), establishing the European Coal and Steel Community (ECSC), which subsequently became part of the European Union." .

ns1:46939 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1931 Ryder Cup were held June 26–27, 1931 at Scioto Country Club in Columbus. In early 1931, it was announced that a selection committee of five would choose the Great Britain team for the 1931 Ryder Cup." .

ns1:46943 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "During the 1994–95 Wimbledon F.C. season English football season, Wimbledon F.C. competed in the FA Premier League, their ninth successive season in the top flight, and extended their stay at this level with a ninth-place finish." .

ns1:46945 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Moment of Truth World Tour was the second worldwide tour by American recording artist Whitney Houston and supported her multi-platinum hit album Whitney." .

ns1:46947 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The first version of the modern The Price is Right format first aired in Australia on the 0-10 Network from 1973–1974; this version was hosted by Garry Meadows and announcer Keith Livingston. The Price is Right later aired on Seven Network from 1981–1985 with host Ian Turpie and announcer John Deeks as The New Price Is Right. The following pricing games were played on the Seven Network version from 1981 to 1985: The following pricing games were played on the Network Ten version in 1989: The Price is Right was revived again from 13 December 1993 until 2 October 1998 on Nine Network, hosted by Larry Emdur with announcer Shawn Cosgrove . Some of these models include: The Price is Right was revived again in 2012 on Seven Network, hosted by Larry Emdur with announcer Brodie Young." .

ns1:46955 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1910 German football championship, the eighth edition of the competition and organised by the German Football Association, was won by Karlsruher FV, defeating Holstein Kiel 1–0 in the final." .

ns1:46963 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Johnny Benson, Jr. was the only rookie to make a full-time run in the 1996 season, making him the 1996 NASCAR Rookie of the Year." .

ns1:46971 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Malaysia FAM League (referred to as the FAM Cup or FAM League) is the 66th season of the Malaysia FAM League since its establishment in 1952." .

ns1:46975 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Zvečan was an 11th-century conflict over land and power between the ruling Byzantine Empire and the Serbians. The town of Zvečan, then situated at the border of the two states, was the site of constant skirmishes and border warfare between 1091–1094." .

ns1:46979 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1932 Summer Olympics – men's pole vault event at the 1932 Olympic Games took place 03 August 1932. The event was won by Bill Miller of the United States, the nation's ninth consecutive victory in the athletics at the 1932 Summer Olympics – men's pole vault." .

ns1:46988 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Israeli 25th Anniversary Cup (Hebrew: גביע הכ\"ה למדינה‎) was a stand-alone cup competition organized to celebrate the 25th anniversary of the Israeli Declaration of Independence." .

ns1:46991 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1982 Copa del Rey Final was the 80th final of the King's Cup. The final was played at Estadio Nuevo José Zorrilla in Valladolid, on 1982, being won by Real Madrid CF, who beat Sporting de Gijón 2–1." .

ns1:46999 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1893 Cheniere Caminada hurricane, also known as the Great October Storm, was a powerful hurricane that devastated the island of Chenière Caminada, Louisiana in early 05 October 1893." .

ns1:47011 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Kazakhstan Cup is the 23rd season of the Kazakhstan Cup, the annual nationwide association football cup competition of Kazakhstan since the independence of the country. The competition begins on 2014, and will end with the final in 22 November 2014. The draw was conducted in 2014 at the offices of the Football Federation of Kazakhstan." .

ns1:47013 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Challenger of Dallas was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Dallas, United States of America between 06 February 2012 and 2012." .

ns1:47020 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Saya (Turkish: Saya, Azeri Turkish: Saya) or Sayaqan (Turkish: Sayagan) is a summer feast and festival Turkic and Altai folklore. The Saya festival (literally it can be translated as abundance) is related to a cult of a solar deity, with a fertility cult." .

ns1:47022 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 United States Senate election in Colorado was held on 04 November 2014 to elect a member of the United States Senate to represent the Colorado, concurrently with the election of the Governor of Colorado, 2014 United States Senate elections to the United States Senate, elections to the United States House of Representatives, and various state and local elections. At the Republican state assembly on 2014, Cory Gardner received 73% of the votes of over 3,900 delegates." .

ns1:47025 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Daniels, et al. v. the City of New York was a class action lawsuit filed in 1999 against the New York Police Department (NYPD) and the City of New York, charging them with racial profiling and unlawful stop and frisk, and requesting the disbanding of the NYPD Street Crimes Unit." .

ns1:47036 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Scottish Open is a professional golf tournament in Scotland, and is one of eight tournaments that are part of the Rolex Series, which identifies it as one of the European Tour's premier events. The first Sunbeam Electric Scottish Open was part of the 1972 European Tour and was held at Downfield Golf Club near Dundee. From 1997 the Scottish Open's pre-Open place on the European Tour schedule was taken by the Loch Lomond World Invitational, which had been first held at Loch Lomond Golf Club in September 1996. From 2001, it was decided that the Loch Lomond event would be known as the Scottish Open and all prior editions, including the September 1996 event, would be granted Scottish Open status. The 2001 Scottish Open was run without a main sponsor but from 2002 it was known as the Barclays Scottish Open, and was played at Loch Lomond until 2010." .

ns1:47053 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1954 European Figure Skating Championships were held in Bolzano, Italy from January 28 to 31. Elite senior-level figure skating from European International Skating Union member nations competed for the title of European Champion in the disciplines of men's singles, ladies' singles, pair skating, and ice dancing." .

ns1:47055 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Irish Masters was the twenty-sixth edition of the professional invitational snooker tournament, which took place from 21 to 26 March 2000." .

ns1:47066 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1950 Japanese House of Councillors election were held in Japan on 04 June 1950, electing half the seats in the House." .

ns1:47071 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Prix La Flèche is a Listed flat horse race in France open to two-year-old thoroughbreds. The Prix La Flèche was held at Chantilly Racecourse from 1997 to 1999, and at Maisons-Laffitte from 2000 to 2003." .

ns1:47079 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Snooker Shoot-Out was a professional non-ranking snooker tournament that took place between 28 January 2011–30 January 2011 at the Blackpool Tower in Blackpool, England. It was played under a Snooker Shoot-Out of snooker." .

ns1:47080 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The swimming at the 1920 Summer Olympics – men's 100 metre backstroke was a swimming event held as part of the swimming at the 1920 Summer Olympics programme. A total of 12 swimmers from six nations competed in the event, which was held on Sunday, August 22 and on Monday, 1920." .

ns1:47089 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1947 Lebanese general election were held in Lebanon on 25 May 1947, with a second round in some constituencies on 1 June." .

ns1:47090 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1907 ECAHA season was the second season of the Eastern Canada Amateur Hockey Association (ECAHA)." .

ns1:47101 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Good Sam RV Insurance 500 was a NASCAR Sprint Cup Series stock car race held on 07 August 2011 at Pocono Raceway in Long Pond, Pennsylvania." .

ns1:47105 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1928 United States presidential election in Texas took place on 06 November 1928, as part of the 1928 United States presidential election which was held throughout all contemporary forty-eight states. In the meantime, Texas continued to vote solidly Democratic: between 1904 and 1924 United States presidential election in Texas no Republican nominee reached 24% of the statewide vote total. However, with all other prominent Democrats sitting the election out, the party nominated Al Smith, four-term Governor of New York as its nominee for 1928, with little opposition, despite disagreement among Texas Democrats like Governor Moody, plus \"Pa\" and \"Ma\" Ferguson. The traditionally Republican Texas German counties of Comal and Guadalupe, along with the former 1920 Ferguson counties of Lee and Washington voted overwhelmingly for Smith in appreciation of his views on Prohibition: in Comal County, which had been Robert La Follette's strongest nationwide in 1924 United States presidential election in Texas, the Democratic vote rose from 13 to 78%, thus supporting La Follette's family's endorsement of Smith after he died." .

ns1:47106 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Fastlane (2018) was a professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event and WWE Network event produced by WWE for the SmackDown brand division. It took place on 11 March 2018, at the Nationwide Arena in Columbus, Ohio. Storylines were produced on WWE's weekly television show WWE Friday Night SmackDown. During the match, there were tensions between Owens and Zayn as a result of General Manager Daniel Bryan scheduling them to face each other the following week to determine the number one contender for the WWE Championship at Fastlane (2018). Corbin and Ziggler won their respective matches, thus making it a fatal five-way for the WWE Championship at Fastlane (2018). Bryan gave him the opportunity to be added to the WWE Championship match at Fastlane (2018) if he could defeat Styles in a non-title match. Orton interrupted and said the U.S. title was the one title he had never held during his WWE career and would be taking it from Roode at Fastlane (2018)." .

ns1:47110 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Graham v. Richardson, 403 U.S. 365 (1971), was a Supreme Court of the United States case in which the Court determined that state restrictions on welfare benefits for legal aliens but not for citizens violated the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment. The 9-0 decision was written by Harry Blackmun." .

ns1:47114 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Platinum Tour presented by Crystal Light is the fifth headlining concert tour by American country music singer Miranda Lambert." .

ns1:47117 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Mason County War, sometimes called the Hoodoo War in reference to masked members of a vigilance committee was a period of lawlessness ignited by a \"tidal wave of rustling\" in Mason County, Texas in 1875 and 1876 The violence entailed a series of mob lynchings and retaliatory murders involving multiple posses and law enforcement factions, including the Texas Rangers. Johnny Ringo left the state for the Arizona Territory, where he again earned a reputation as a cattle rustler and criminal, and George Gladden was imprisoned for the murder of Peter Bader On January 21, 1877, the Mason County Courthouse was burned to the ground and the official records of the Mason County War were destroyed." .

ns1:47118 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Mae Lao earthquake occurred at 18:08:43 Indochina Time on 05 May 2014. The earthquake was a recorded as having a maximum intensity of strong (MMI VI), shaking both northern Thailand and Myanmar in the evening. It was the strongest earthquake ever recorded in Thailand according to National Disaster Warning Center Director Somsak Khaosuwan." .

ns1:47124 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Birmingham Classic (currently sponsored by Nature Valley) is a premier level women's tennis tournament on the WTA Tour held at the Edgbaston Priory Club in Edgbaston, Birmingham, United Kingdom. Previously, the event has been called the \"Aegon Birmingham Classic\", the \"DFS Classic\", the \"Dow Classic\", and the \"Edgbaston Cup.\"" .

ns1:47125 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Giro del Friuli is a road bicycle racing held annually in Friuli–Venezia Giulia, Italy." .

ns1:47128 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007–08 CJHL season was the 47th sports season of the Central Canada Hockey League (CJHL)." .

ns1:47137 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Conservative Party of Canada leadership election was held on 27 May 2017." .

ns1:47140 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Money in the Bank was a professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event produced by WWE, which took place on 14 July 2013 at the Wells Fargo Center in Philadelphia. The professional wrestling matches at Money in the Bank featured professional wrestlers performing as characters in scripted events pre-determined by the hosting promotion, WWE." .

ns1:47142 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Jeonbuk Hyundai Motors season was Jeonbuk Hyundai Motors FC' nineteenth season in the K-League in South Korea." .

ns1:47145 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1989 Maldivian parliamentary election were held in the Maldives on 24 November 1989." .

ns1:47147 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1406, adopted unanimously on 30 April 2002, after recalling all previous resolutions on the situation on Western Sahara, particularly Resolution 1394 (2002), the Council extended the mandate of the United Nations Mission for the Referendum in Western Sahara (MINURSO) until 31 July 2002." .

ns1:47149 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final was the 78th All-Ireland Final and the culmination of the All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1965, an inter-county hurling tournament for the top teams in Ireland. The match was held at Croke Park, Dublin, on 1965, between Wexford and Tipperary." .

ns1:47153 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 868, adopted unanimously on 29 September 1993, after expressing concern at the increasing number of attacks and use of force against persons engaged in United Nations peacekeeping operations, the Council established new safety mandates for United Nations peacekeepers." .

ns1:47166 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Rugby League Four Nations tournament was played in Australia and New Zealand national rugby league team in October and 2010. England also faced the New Zealand national rugby league team Māori rugby league team in a curtain raiser to the New Zealand national rugby league team-Samoa test." .

ns1:47181 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "killing of Bernard Whitehurst was shot in the back and killed on 02 December 1975 by Donald Foster, a Montgomery police officer who said he thought Whitehurst was the suspect in the robbery of a neighborhood grocery store. From the date of the killing, the Montgomery Advertiser covered the shooting of killing of Bernard Whitehurst by police and later investigated the subsequent controversy, publishing news stories and editorials that questioned the original police reports." .

ns1:47185 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The King George Street bombing was a suicide bombing which occurred on 21 March 2002 outside a clothing store and toy shop on King George Street in Jerusalem. On Thursday afternoon, 21 March 2002, a Palestinian suicide bomber detonated the explosive device, hidden underneath his jacket, in the middle of Jerusalem's shopping district in the King George Street in downtown Jerusalem amongst a crowd of shoppers." .

ns1:47189 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's hammer throw event at the 1998 World Junior Championships in Athletics – men's hammer throw was held in Annecy, France, at Parc des Sports on 31 July and 1 August." .

ns1:47190 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The handball at the 2018 Asian Games – men's tournament at Jakarta, Indonesia, was held from 13 to 31 August 2018 at the POPKI Sports Hall." .

ns1:47195 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The gymnastics at the 1932 Summer Olympics – men's tumbling event was part of the gymnastics at the 1932 Summer Olympics at the 1932 Summer Olympics." .

ns1:47203 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "This is the first season of 1921 Malaya Cup (later known as Malaysia Cup). The final were held at Selangor Club Padang on 1921 where the southern champ, Singapore Lions defeated the northern champ, Selangor FA with 2-1 scoreline. In 1921, the British Royal Navy battleship H. M. S. Malaya called at Port Swettenham (now Port Klang), Singapore Lions, Malacca, Penang and Port Dickson. A 1921 Malaya Cup committee was set up and it was decided to run the association football competition in northern and southern sections. Six teams participated the inaugural 1921 Malaya Cup, Malacca, Negeri Sembilan, Singapore Lions, Penang, Selangor and Perak. The first 1921 Malaya Cup match was played on 1921, with Selangor defeating Penang 5–1 in front of an estimated crowd of 5,000 in Kuala Lumpur. Singapore Lions and Selangor topped their respective sections, and met in the first 1921 Malaya Cup final on 1 October at the Selangor Club field (now Merdeka Square)." .

ns1:47208 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016–17 Guam Soccer League (Budweiser Soccer League for sponsorship reasons) is the 28th season of Guam Men's Soccer League, Guam's First tier professional football league." .

ns1:47215 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Novi Sad Jazz Festival (Serbian Cyrillic: Новосадски Џез фестивал or Novosadski jazz festival) is an annual jazz festival in Novi Sad, Serbia. The festival was first held in 1999 in the Novi Sad Cultural Centre. The first jazz festival was held in the Cultural Centre of Novi Sad, from November 25 to 1999. More than 100 ensembles from Serbia and abroad have performed at the Novi Sad Jazz Festival for the past seven years, and nearly 600 musicians, including Johnny Griffin, Jimmy Cobb, Al Foster, Benny Bailey, Andy Bay, Tania Maria, Trilok Gurtu, Steve Coleman, Keith Copeland, Eddie Henderson, Al Di Meola, Jerry Bergonzi, Kenny Garrett, Erik Rothenstein, Sheila Jordan, and Curtis Fuller to name a few." .

ns1:47222 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dansk Melodi Grand Prix is an annual music competition organised by Denmark public broadcaster DR, which determines the country's representative for the Eurovision Song Contest. In 2005, DR made a bold step for Dansk Melodi Grand Prix. For the 2009 of Dansk Melodi Grand Prix, DR reverted to their one-night final, that was held on 31 January 2009. Almost all winners of Dansk Melodi Grand Prix have gone on to represent Denmark at Eurovision." .

ns1:47226 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 United Kingdom general election was held on 01 May 1997. The incumbent governing Conservative Party led by Prime Minister of the United Kingdom John Major was defeated in a landslide by the Labour Party led by Tony Blair. The final result of the election on 2 01 May 1997 revealed that Labour had won a landslide majority, making a net gain of 146 seats and winning 43.2% of the vote. Immediately following the election Major resigned both as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom and as party leader. Although the Conservatives lost many ministers such as Michael Portillo, Tony Newton, Malcolm Rifkind, Ian Lang and William Waldegrave and controversial MPs such as Neil Hamilton and Jonathan Aitken, some of the Conservative newcomers in this election were future Prime Minister of the United Kingdom Theresa May, future Chancellor of the Exchequer Philip Hammond as well as future Speaker John Bercow. Therefore, the latest date the election could have been held on was 22 01 May 1997 (which happened to be a Thursday). Prime Minister of the United Kingdom John Major called the election on Monday 17 March 1997, ensuring the formal campaign would be unusually long, at six weeks (Parliament was dissolved on 8 April). The election was scheduled for 01 May 1997, to coincide with the local elections on the same day. The election was fought under new boundaries, with a net increase of eight seats compared to the 1992 United Kingdom general election (651 to 659). Between the 1992 United Kingdom general election and the 1997 election there had also been major steps to \"modernise\" the party, including scrapping Clause IV that had committed the party to extending public ownership of industry." .

ns1:47227 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The gymnastics at the 2015 European Games – women's floor exercise competition at the 2015 European Games was held in the National Gymnastics Arena, Baku on 2015." .

ns1:47231 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Kaya Tour were a Jamaican reggae band led by Bob Marley. Bob Marley formed Kaya Tour with himself as guitarist, songwriter and main singer, the Wailers Band as the backing band, and the I Three as backup vocalists." .

ns1:47235 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 UCI Juniors Track World Championships was the annual Junior World Championship for track cycling held at Trexlertown, United States of America, from 25 to 29 July 2001." .

ns1:47238 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Army Black Knights women's basketball team represented the United States Military Academy during the 2014–15 NCAA Division I women's basketball season. 2014–15 Army Black Knights men's basketball team." .

ns1:47240 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012–13 Serie A (known as the Serie A TIM for sponsorship reasons) was the 111th season of top-tier Italian association football, the 81st in a round-robin tournament, and the 3rd since its organization under a league committee separate from Serie B. It began on 25 26 August 2012 and ended on 19 May 2013. A total of 20 teams contested the league, comprising 17 sides from the 2011–12 Serie A and three promoted from the 2011–12 Serie B. On 21 26 August 2012, FIGC allowed Serie A teams to have up to 12 substitution players on the bench for each game." .

ns1:47243 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 17 December 1967, Harold Holt, the Prime Minister of Australia, disappeared while swimming in the sea near Portsea." .

ns1:47248 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 Virginia Slims of Houston was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts at the Westside Tennis Club in Houston, Texas in the United States that was part of Tier II of the 1991 WTA Tour. It was the 21st edition of the tournament and was held from 15 April 1991 through 21 April 1991." .

ns1:47251 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 HEW Cyclassics was the second edition of the EuroEyes Cyclassics cycle race and was held on 10 August 1997." .

ns1:47254 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2020 Venezuelan parliamentary election were held in Venezuela on 06 December 2020. In 2020, the Committee of Electoral Candidacies, in charge of appointing a new National Electoral Council of Venezuela (CNE), announced that it would suspend its meetings because of the pandemic. The United States sanctioned Alfonzo and three others on 2020, accusing them of facilitating the illegitimate Maduro regime’s efforts to undermine the independence and democratic order of Venezuela. As of 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic, electoral organizations such as the Venezuelan Electoral Observatory and the Education Assembly Electoral Observation Network, assured that there were many obstacles in Venezuela left to surpass before an electoral process takes place by 06 December 2020, including conditions, technological problems and a lack of agreement between political factions, saying that having the elections in 2020 did not appear feasible." .

ns1:47257 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 UAW-DaimlerChrysler 400 was the third race in the 2006 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series season which took place at Las Vegas Motor Speedway on 12 March 2006." .

ns1:47275 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2006 Palestinian legislative election were held in the Palestinian territories on 25 January 2006 in order to elect the second Palestinian Legislative Council (PLC), the legislature of the Palestinian National Authority (PNA). On 20 August Abbas set election day as 25 January 2006. On 15 25 January 2006, Abbas declared that, despite unrest in Gaza, he would not change the election date unless Israel prevented Palestinians in East Jerusalem from voting. On 31 25 January 2006, Israel's Defence Minister Mofaz said Hamas' election victory gives Israel an incentive to decide in favour of a unilateral withdrawal from the West Bank and that Israel would have to set new defensible borders for itself." .

ns1:47276 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Padel Tennis World Championship is an international competition of padel which has been held every three years since 1992." .

ns1:47280 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 2008 Summer Olympics – men's triple jump at the 2008 Olympic Games took place on 18 August 2008–21 August at the Beijing National Stadium. The event was won by Nelson Évora of Portugal, the nation's first medal and victory in the athletics at the 2008 Summer Olympics – men's triple jump." .

ns1:47282 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The death of Hollywood actor James Dean occurred on September 30, 1955, near Cholame, California. The cause of death listed on James Dean's death certificate is listed as a broken neck, multiple fractures of the upper and lower jaw, both right and left arms broken, and internal injuries. On September 30, 2005, the junction at Highways 46 and 41 was dedicated as the James Dean Memorial Junction as part of the State of California's official commemoration of the 50th anniversary of his death. On February 15, 2009, all three of the California Highway Patrol (CHP) officers who dealt with Dean on the day of his death – Officer Otie Hunter, who ticketed Dean for speeding, and Officers Ernie Tripke and Ronald Nelson, who investigated the fatal crash – participated and shared their memories of that fateful day in an SCVTV documentary titled The Stuff of Legend: James Dean's Final Ride, co-produced by the Santa Clarita Valley Historical Society." .

ns1:47285 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The United Nations Operation in the Congo (French: Opération des Nations Unies au Congo, abbreviated to ONUC) was a peacekeeping force established by the United Nations to maintain order in the Republic of the Congo on 14 July 1960 amid the Congo Crisis." .

ns1:47286 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Horki was a series of three clashes between Polish-Lithuanian insurgent forces and units of the Imperial Russian Army during the January Uprising. It took place between May 17–25, 1863 in the village of Horki near Kobryn, Russian Empire (now Belarus)." .

ns1:47290 a ns1:context_narration ;
