ns1:47426 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The International Ski Federation (International Ski Federation) 2018–19 FIS Alpine Ski World Cup was the premier circuit for alpine skiing competition. The inaugural season launched in January 1967, and the 2018–19 season marks the 53rd consecutive year for the International Ski Federation FIS Alpine Ski World Cup. This season began in October 2018 in Sölden, Austria, and concluded in mid-March 2019 at the finals in Soldeu, Andorra. During the season, the most successful female skier of all time, four-time overall FIS Alpine Ski World Cup champion Lindsey Vonn of the United States of America, retired after the World Championships, at which she won a bronze medal in downhill. Prior to the start of the season, 4-time overall FIS Alpine Ski World Cup champion (and 20-time crystal globe winner) Lindsey Vonn of the United States of America announced her retirement effective as of the end of the season." .

