ns1:47734 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2010 Burundian presidential election were held in Burundi on 28 June 2010. Following the Burundi Civil War, between the Tutsi and Hutu (similar to Rwanda), the National Liberation Forces (FNL) were brought into the legal political sphere and were said to be the incumbent Pierre Nkurunziza's most viable opposition. The East African Community – comprising Burundi, Rwanda, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania – urged all parties to ensure a smooth and democratic election." .

ns1:47744 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 53rd Baeksang Arts Awards ceremony was held on 03 May 2017 at the COEX Convention & Exhibition Center in Seoul." .

ns1:47745 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018–19 Top 14 season competition was the 120th season of the French domestic rugby union club competition operated by the National Rugby League (LNR). The Top 14 final was contested between the top two teams in the league stage – Stade Toulousain (1st) and Clermont (2nd) – who both won their semi-finals with relative ease. In terms of attendances, the Top 14 once again proved to be the most popular rugby union league in the world, with over 2.7 million supporters watching games that season. The team finishing in 13th place faces the runner-up of the Pro D2, with the winner of this match playing in the 2019–20 Top 14 season and the loser in the 2019–20 Pro D2." .

ns1:47752 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Lowland Football League was the second season of the Lowland Football League, the fifth tier of the Scottish football pyramid system." .

