ns1:47821 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Siberian Baroque is an architectural style common for ambitious structures in 18th-century Siberia, where 115 stone churches in Siberia were recorded in 1803, most of which were built in this provincial variant of the baroque architecture, influenced by the Ukrainian Baroque and in some cases even incorporating lamaist motifs." .

ns1:47823 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Iranian local elections took place on 14 June 2013 to elected members of the fourth council of the City and Village Councils of Iran. The original date of the election was in June 2010 but Parliament of Iran voted to increase age of the councils from 4 to 7 years." .

ns1:47824 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jazzahead is an annual trade fair and festival for jazz, held in the German city of Bremen. Since its premiere in 2006, the event has grown to include a culture festival in and around Bremen, in addition to the four-day trade fair. The international music trade fair with its integrated showcase festival focusses in jazz, while the festival in Bremen is for a broad audience. Jazzahead is organized by a team of Messe Bremen, a division of M3B GmbH Bremen. The artistic direction team is formed by Ulrich Beckerhoff, former professor for jazz trumpet and renowned jazz trumpeter and Peter Schulze, director of Sendesaal Bremen and former director of Jazzfest Berlin. As a meeting point for the international jazz scene Jazzahead includes an exhibition, showcase festival, panels and conferences. The showcase festival has included the following modules: European Jazz Meeting – with jazz music from around Europe, a German Jazz Expo, Overseas Night – focusing on bands from outside Europe; and a showcase module which presents jazz from the Jazzahead partner country. Furthermore, a focus is set on the partner country program, presenting the cultural scene of the annually changing Jazzahead partner country in Bremen's cultural institutions. During Jazzahead, the German jazz scene presents itself in its wide diversity with the aim to make new contacts, especially abroad. Worth 15,000 Euro, the Jazzahead Award has been awarded to distinguished personalities from the international jazz business and honors their outstanding work promoting jazz as object of cultural value." .

ns1:47827 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 14th 1959 Vuelta a España (Tour of Spain), a long-distance bicycle stage race and one of the three grand tours, was held from 24 April 1959 to 10 May 1959." .

ns1:47831 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "During the 1997–98 Mansfield Town F.C. season English football season, Mansfield Town F.C. competed in the Football League Third Division where they finished in 12th position on 65 points." .

ns1:47839 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Vuelta a Murcia was the 21st professional edition of the Vuelta a Murcia cycle race and was held on 2 March to 6 03 March 2005." .

ns1:47842 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Davis v. Washington, 547 U.S. 813 (2006), was a case decided by the Supreme Court of the United States holding that hearsay statements made in a 911 call asking for aid were not \"testimonial\" in nature and thus their introduction at trial did not violate the Confrontation Clause as defined in Crawford v. Washington. In a decision authored by Justice Antonin Scalia, the Court ruled that the Confrontation Clause of the Sixth Amendment, as interpreted in Crawford v. Washington, does not apply to \"non-testimonial\" statements not intended to be used in a future criminal prosecution." .

ns1:47845 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1904 Missouri gubernatorial election was Missouri's 26th gubernatorial election. The election was held on 08 November 1904 and resulted in a victory for the Democratic nominee, Joseph W. Folk, over the Republican candidate, former Mayor of St. Louis Cyrus Walbridge, and several other candidates representing minor parties." .

ns1:47849 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 European Cross Country Championships was a continental cross country running competition that took place on 12 December 2010 in Albufeira, Portugal. Albufeira was chosen as the host at the 120th European Athletic Association Council Meeting in October 2008, defeating a rival bid from Velenje (which was chosen for the 2011 European Cross Country Championships instead)." .

ns1:47850 a ns1:context_narration ;
