ns1:47860 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Watkins v. United States, 354 U.S. 178 (1957), is a decision of the Supreme Court of the United States that held that the power of the United States Congress is not unlimited in conducting investigations and that nothing in the United States Constitution gives it the authority to expose the private affairs of individuals. The Supreme Court heard arguments on March 7, 1957 and announced its decision on 17 June 1957." .

