ns1:47880 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Israeli Sign Language, or ISL, is the most commonly used sign language in the deaf community of Israel. Today ISL is the most used and taught sign language in Israel, and serves as the main mode of communication for most deaf people in Israel, including Jewish, Muslim and Christian Arabs, Druze, and Bedouins. The community grew as refugees from World War Two fled to Israel, and the association helped new arrivals integrate into the Israeli community by helping them learn Israeli Sign Language and helping them find work. The emphasis on oralism began to change in the 1970s, when Izchak Schlesinger began to research ISL, and with Israel hosting the Fourth International Conference on Deafness in 1973." .

ns1:47882 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992–93 Football League Cup (known as the Coca-Cola Cup for sponsorship reasons) was the 33rd EFL Cup, a knockout competition for England's top 92 association football clubs. Arsenal F.C. won the competition, beating Sheffield Wednesday 2–1 in the 1993 Football League Cup Final." .

