ns1:48163 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1935 FA Charity Shield was the 22nd FA Community Shield, a association football match between the winners of the previous season's First Division and FA Cup competitions. The match was contested by league champions Arsenal F.C. and FA Cup winners Sheffield Wednesday F.C., and was played at Arsenal Stadium, the home ground of Arsenal F.C.. Sheffield Wednesday F.C. won 1–0. Arsenal F.C. were making their fifth appearance out of six Charity Shields, and they had won the previous four in which they had played, including a 2–1 victory over Sheffield Wednesday F.C. in the 1930 final." .

ns1:48164 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Khan el-Khalili bombing was a terrorist attack that took place at 6:30 p.m. local time on 22 February 2009 in Khan el-Khalili, a souq in eastern Cairo, Egypt, killing a 17-year-old French teenager and injuring 24 other people. It was the first of the 22 February 2009 Cairo terrorist attacks." .

