ns1:48310 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 season is the 122nd year in the club's history, the 106th season in 2017 Clube de Regatas do Flamengo season football existence, and their 47th in the Brazilian Série A, having never been relegated from the top division. After finishing 2016 Brazilian Série A in 3rd place Clube de Regatas do Flamengo earned a spot to play CONMEBOL Libertadores Bridgestone 2017, returning to the South America top club competition since last played in 2014. On 30 August 2016 Clube de Regatas do Flamengo announced that would take part of 2017 Florida Cup, although on 2017 the club forfeit from the pre-season competition due to the reschedule of its pre-season training, instead the club would have all the preparation to the 2017 season in its recently opened training ground, Ninho do Urubu. On 30 December 2016 Primeira Liga announced the 2017 season schedule with Clube de Regatas do Flamengo playing its first match against Grêmio. As Clube de Regatas do Flamengo played in the 2017 CONMEBOL Libertadores, the club only entered the competition in the round of 16. Clube de Regatas do Flamengo position on the Club World Ranking during the 2017 season, according to clubworldranking.com." .

