    rdfs:label "The 1994 Paris Open was a tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts. It took place at the Palais omnisports de Paris-Bercy in Paris, France, from 31 October to 1994. 1, Indian Wells, Key Biscayne, Rome, Wimbledon, U.S. Open titlist, Queen's finalist, Australian Open semi-finalist Pete Sampras, Kitzubhel, Tokyo (1994 ATP Tokyo Indoor winner), Stockholm, Bucharest, Wimbledon runner-up, 1993 Paris Open Goran Ivanišević and Rotterdam (1994 ABN Amro World Tennis Tournament), Munich, Halle champion, 1993 Tennis Masters Cup winner Michael Stich." .

