    rdfs:label "Sydney New Year's Eve 2013–14 is an annual multi-tiered event held every New Year's Eve in Sydney, Australia. ABC, ABC HD and ABC Australia had the rights since 2013. The City of Sydney put its Sydney New Year's Eve 2013–14 fireworks coverage to tender following the conclusion of ABC's two-year contract, with the broadcaster having continued as broadcaster since." .

ns1:48951 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 Dushanbe riots were an anti-government unrest in Dushanbe, the capital of Tajikistan, from February 12–14, 1990. In 1990, the Armenian influx became a subject of the rumour that triggered riots in Dushanbe. Despite the fact that Armenian refugees resettled not in public housing but with their relatives, and by 1990 had already left Tajikistan for Armenia, official denouncement of the rumours was not able to stop the protests. On 1990 Mahkamov and Prime Minister of Tajikistan Izatullo Khayoyev submitted their resignations, but they were not accepted by the Central Committee of the Tajik Communist Party. During the Dushanbe riots, a period lasting a couple of days, 26 people were killed and 565 were injured." .

ns1:48954 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990–91 Lebanese Premier League season was the 31st season of the Lebanese Premier League, the top Lebanese professional league for association football clubs in the country, established in 1934." .

ns1:48957 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Back to Bass Tour was a concert tour by English musician and singer-songwriter Sting. On 22 January 2013 it was announced that Sting would continue to tour as part of the Back to Bass Tour in the Summer of 2013, with various shows being announced for Europe and Northern America." .

ns1:48958 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 DEL season was the 18th season since the founding of the Deutsche Eishockey Liga." .

ns1:48964 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "13th Anniversary Show was the 13th ROH Anniversary Show professional wrestling pay-per-view event produced by Ring of Honor (ROH), which took place on 01 March 2015 at The Orleans, a hotel and casino in the Las Vegas Valley community of Paradise, Nevada. This professional wrestling event featured nine professional wrestling matches, which involved different wrestlers from pre-existing scripted feuds, plots, and storylines that played out on ROH's television programs." .

ns1:48971 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 FIVB Men's World Cup was played from 13 to 19 September 1965 in Poland. In the decisive match in 19 September 1965, the Soviet Union men's national volleyball team team defeated hosts Poland to claim a narrow 3-2 victory." .

ns1:48974 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1973 Paris–Roubaix was the 71st edition of the Paris–Roubaix cycle race and was held on 15 April 1973. The race started in Compiègne and finished in Roubaix." .

