ns1:49113 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Investiture controversy, also called Investiture Contest, was a conflict between church and state in medieval Europe over the ability to choose and install bishops (investiture) and abbots of monasteries and the pope himself." .

ns1:49114 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Peking to Paris motor race was an automobile race, originally held in 1907, between Peking (now Beijing), then Qing People's Republic of China and Paris, France, a distance of 14,994 kilometres (9,317 mi)." .

ns1:49116 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Newport Jazz Festival is a music festival held every summer in Newport, Rhode Island. Elaine Lorillard established the festival in 1954, and she and husband Louis Lorillard financed it for many years. In 1954, the first Newport Jazz Festival (billed as the \"First Annual American Jazz Festival\") was held at Newport Casino, in the Bellevue Avenue Historic District of Newport, Rhode Island. He was a music festival pioneer and would run many festivals besides the Newport Jazz Festival during his career. The Saratoga addition began a trend of using the \"Newport Jazz Festival\" name outside of Newport, as in the Newport Jazz Festival in Madarao, Japan, from 1982 to 2004. In 1981, George Wein brought the Newport Jazz Festival back to Newport, partly to preserve the Newport Jazz Festival legacy and to protect his interest in the Newport Jazz Festival name. Newport, now quite keen to tourism, was extremely receptive to the resumption of its Newport Jazz Festival. In 1988, the festival temporarily moved to the Newport Casino, where the first festival was held in 1954, and featured a lineup that included Tony Bennett, Mel Tormé, Illinois Jacquet, k.d. That company now owns and operates the Newport festival and controls the legacy \"Newport Jazz Festival\" brand." .

ns1:49123 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jefferson's Birthday officially honors the birth of the third U.S. president, Thomas Jefferson on April 13, 1743." .

ns1:49128 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Cumbrian Run is an annual half marathon road running event held in Carlisle, United Kingdom." .

ns1:49131 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Pequereque was a clash which took place on 19 June 1813, during the second Upper Peru campaign of the Argentine War of Independence, between scouting forces of the United Provinces Army of the North and the royalist Army of Peru. After the capitulation of General Pio de Tristan in the battle of Salta, on 24 February 1813, the United Provinces' Army of the North gained the upper hand not only in northern Argentina, but also in southern Upper Peru (present-day Bolivia)." .

ns1:49135 a ns1:context_narration ;
