    rdfs:label "The Cienega Affair, or the Battle of Cienega Creek, was the last engagement of the Taos Revolt during the Mexican–American War." .

ns1:49234 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 40th Saturn Awards, honoring the best in science fiction, fantasy and horror film and television in 2013, was held on 26 June 2014, in Burbank." .

ns1:49238 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Losail Superbike World Championship round was the opening round of the 2008 Superbike World Championship season. It took place on the weekend of February 21–23, 2008 at the 5.38 km Losail International Circuit in Qatar." .

ns1:49239 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Isani flat siege was a confrontation between the Georgia police and security forces and an armed group of four Chechen men, including the former ISIS officer Akhmed Chatayev, in and around a flat on Gabriel Salosi Street in the Isani district of Tbilisi, from 21 to 22 November 2017. A special operation, involving the Georgia police and State Security Service, to disarm an armed group entrenched in a rented flat in a block in Gabriel Salos Street in Tbilisi's Isani district began late on 21 November 2017 and escalated to a gunfight and explosions overnight after hours of futile attempts by the authorities to convince the men to surrender. According to the head of the Georgia State Security Service Vakhtang Gomelauri, Chatayev and his associates made their way to Georgia in 2017, bypassing a border checkpoint, but declined to specify the country from which they crossed into Georgia. Four more men, all Georgia nationals, detained from 2017 to January 2018, were found guilty of providing logistical support to the Chatayev group and sentenced from 10 to 12 years in prison." .

ns1:49242 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Women's European Water Polo Championship was held from 10 to 22 January 2016 in Belgrade, Serbia." .

ns1:49244 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1879 Wimbledon Championship took place on the outdoor grass courts at the All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club in Wimbledon, London, United Kingdom. It was the 3rd staging of the Wimbledon Championships, and the first Grand Slam tennis event of 1879." .

ns1:49247 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Hurricane Jimena /hiˈmɛnə/ was the second-strongest hurricane of the 2009 Pacific hurricane season, and tied with Hurricane Norbert as the strongest tropical cyclone to make landfall on western portion of the Baja California Peninsula. By the evening of August 31, Hurricane hunters measured winds of 155 mph (250 km/h) and a pressure of 931 mbar (hPa; 27.49 inHg) while the powerful cyclone began to turn to the north due to nearby 2009 Pacific hurricane season and a low pressure area west of Baja California." .

ns1:49249 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Puerto Armuelles earthquake occurred on 25 December 2003 at 02:11 local time (07:11 UTC). This earthquake could also be felt in Panama City." .

