ns1:49284 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Belgian Grand Prix (officially the 2007 Formula 1 ING Belgian Grand Prix) was the fourteenth race of the 2007 Formula One World Championship, returning to the Formula One calendar after a year's absence. It was held on 16 September 2007 at the Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps, Spa, Belgium. Fernando Alonso pipped McLaren teammate Lewis Hamilton to 3rd place, but Ferrari dominated, with Kimi Räikkönen beating Felipe Massa to get his 14th career pole and lock out the front row for the Italian team. The order from the start remained fairly unchanged with the Ferraris of Kimi Räikkönen and Felipe Massa led away from Fernando Alonso and Lewis Hamilton, although there was a lot of pushing between the McLarens as Hamilton attempted to pass around the outside of turn one, but Alonso pushed him wide onto the tarmac on the outside of the corner." .

ns1:49288 a ns1:context_narration ;
