ns1:49332 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Universe Slovenia 2007, the 7th Miss Universe Slovenia pageant held at Exhibition and Convention Centre, Ljubljana in Ljubljana, Slovenia on 2007. The winner was the representative for Slovenia at the Miss Universe 2007 pageant in Mexico City, Mexico. In the final round, Tjaša Kokalj, was crowned Miss Universe Slovenia 2007 by Nataša Pinoza, Miss Universe Slovenia 2006." .

ns1:49333 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Barcelona Open Banc Sabadell (also known as the Torneo Godó) is a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts. It is the 62nd edition of Barcelona Open and part of the ATP World Tour 500 series of the 2014 ATP World Tour. It will take place at the Real Club de Tenis Barcelona in Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain, from 21 April 2014 through 27 April 2014." .

ns1:49334 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Beverbeek Classic is a single-day road bicycle racing held annually in Hamont-Achel, in the Belgian region of Limburg." .

ns1:49335 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Australian Open – Men's Singles final was the championship tennis match of the 2009 Australian Open – Men's Singles at the 2009 Australian Open. Following the final, tennis analyst Bud Collins proposed that Federer might never win another major as long as Nadal was playing tennis. It would not be until the 2017 Australian Open that two would meet again in a Grand Slam final, that time ending in the 35 year-old Federer's five-set victory that claimed his 18th singles major and subsequently set new tennis records from it. Until his 2017 Australian Open victory, Federer had not beaten Nadal in a Grand Slam since the 2007 Wimbledon final and many analysts pointed to the 2009 Australian Open final as the match which severely compromised Federer's belief that he could win against Nadal in a major." .

ns1:49343 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Rochdale Metropolitan Borough Council election took place on 03 May 2012 to elect members of Rochdale Metropolitan Borough Council in the North West, England." .

ns1:49345 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Philippines at the 1982 Asian Games participated in the 1982 Asian Games held in New Delhi, India from November 19 to 1982." .

ns1:49354 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992–93 Swindon Town F.C. season was Swindon Town F.C.'s 6th consecutive season in the second tier of English football after winning promotion in 1986-87." .

ns1:49362 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Florent Serra defeated Xavier Malisse, 6–3, 6–4 to win the 2006 Next Generation Adelaide International – singles men's singles competition." .

ns1:49363 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Bob Carmichael defeated Allan Stone 7–6, 7–6, 6–3 to win the 1971 New Zealand Open – singles singles competition." .

ns1:49365 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Campo Tenese (10 March 1806) saw two divisions of the Imperial French Army of Naples led by Jean Reynier attack the left wing of the Royal Neapolitan Army under Roger de Damas. The battle was fought during the War of the Third Coalition, part of the Napoleonic Wars." .

ns1:49366 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hochsprung mit Musik (English: High Jump with Music) is an annual indoor high jump meeting which takes place in February in Arnstadt, Germany." .

ns1:49369 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1926 United States Senate special election in Massachusetts was held on 02 November 1926." .

ns1:49380 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Severe Tropical Storm Khanun, known in the Philippines as Tropical Storm Khanun, was the first tropical cyclone to directly impact Korea in two years." .

ns1:49391 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Strawberry Fair is a local festival of music, entertainments, arts and crafts which has been held in Cambridge, England, since 1974." .

ns1:49394 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 25th G8 summit was held in Cologne, Germany, on 18 June 1999–20, 1999. The Group of Seven (G7) was an unofficial forum which brought together the heads of the richest industrialized countries: France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom, the United States and Canada starting in 1976. The summits were not meant to be linked formally with wider international institutions; and in fact, a mild rebellion against the stiff formality of other international meetings was a part of the genesis of cooperation between France's President Giscard d'Estaing and West Germany's Chancellor Helmut Schmidt as they conceived the initial summit of the Group of Six (G6) in 1975. The G8 is an unofficial annual forum for the leaders of Canada, the European Commission, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, Russia, the United Kingdom and the United States." .

ns1:49397 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Chinese cardboard bun hoax was a falsified news report broadcast in 12 July 2007 on Beijing Television's BTV-7 (the Lifestyle Channel)." .

ns1:49399 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Saorgio (1793–1793) saw a Republican French army commanded by Gaspard Jean-Baptiste Brunet attack the armies of the Kingdom of Sardinia-Piedmont and Habsburg Austria led by Joseph Nikolaus De Vins. Saorge is now located in France about 70 kilometres (43 mi) northeast of Nice, but in 1793 Saorge belonged to Piedmont. In fact, the French tried to diplomatically drive a wedge between Sardinia and Austria, but the execution of King Louis XVI by guillotine on 1793 caused Victor Amadeus to rebuff France. However, an order of battle exists for the Austro-Sardinian army on 1793 that placed the Duke of Chablais in command over the Left Division of Saint-André and the Right Division of Colli." .

ns1:49402 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The archery at the 1920 Summer Olympics – individual moving bird, 50 metres event was part of the archery at the 1920 Summer Olympics at the 1920 Summer Olympics. The event, like all other archery events in 1920, was open only to men." .

ns1:49408 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1931 Philippine Senate elections happened on 02 June 1931 in the Philippines under the Jones Law provisions." .

ns1:49423 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Lompoc Valley Flower Festival is an annual flower festival held in the city of Lompoc, located northern Santa Barbara County." .

ns1:49431 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 FEI European Jumping and Dressage Championships, also known as the 2009 Alltech FEI European Jumping and Dressage Championships, is the 30th edition of the European Show Jumping Championships and the 26th edition of the European Dressage Championship. It was held at Windsor Castle in Windsor, England, from August 25 to 2009." .

ns1:49434 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bengali Hindu diaspora is the worldwide population of the Bengali Hindus of Indian and Bangladeshi origin." .

ns1:49436 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "October Road Tour is singer-songwriter James Taylor's fifteenth studio album. October Road Tour would become James Taylor's last album of original material until the 2015 Before This World." .

ns1:49440 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2001 Zambian general election were held in Zambia on 27 December 2001 to elect a President and National Assembly." .

ns1:49444 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Monte Grappa were a series of three battles which were fought during World War I between the armies of the Austro-Hungarian Empire and the Kingdom of Italy for control of the Monte Grappa massif, as it covered the left flank of the Italian Piave front. When the Austrian summer offensive of 1917 routed the Italians, Cadorna's foresight saved Italy from total defeat, as the Austrians, with help from the German Army's Alpenkorps failed to take the mountain's summit during the first battle of Monte Grappa from 1917 to 1917. The second battle of Monte Grappa was complementary to the wider Austrian summer offensive of 1918, which was the last offensive operation of the Austro–Hungarian Army in World War I. The third battle of Monte Grappa started on 1918, as part of the final Italian offensive of the war, when 9 Italian divisions attacked the Austrian positions on Monte Grappa. The map is set during the final Italian offensive in the Third Battle of Monte Grappa pitting Austro-Hungarian forces against the Kingdom of Italy." .

ns1:49445 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 IAAF Continental Cup was an international track and field sporting event that was held in Marrakesh, Morocco, on 2014–2014." .

ns1:49447 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Spanish and Taíno War of San Juan–Borikén, also known as the Taino rebellion of 1511, was the first major conflict to take place in modern-day Puerto Rico after the arrival of the Spaniards on November 19, 1493. On 1511, Ponce de León wrote to the Monarchy informing them of his involvement in the battles of the first stages in the conflict." .

ns1:49449 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1989 Svenska Cupen Final took place on 29 June 1989 at Råsunda Stadium in Solna. The match was contested by Allsvenskan sides Malmö FF and Djurgårdens IF. Djurgården played their first final since 1975 and their third final in total, Malmö FF played their first final since 1986 and their 16th final in total. Malmö FF won their 14th title with a 3–0 victory." .

ns1:49450 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Missouri State Lady Bears basketball team represented Missouri State University during the 2015–16 NCAA Division I women's basketball season. 2015–16 Missouri State Bears basketball team." .

ns1:49453 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The USA Act and the Financial Anti-Terrorism Act are the legislative precursors to the Patriot Act. The USA Act and the Financial Anti-Terrorism Act were combined to become the Patriot Act on October 26, 2001." .

