    rdfs:label "Flexible glass is a purported lost invention from the time of the reign of the Roman Emperor Tiberius Caesar (between 14–37 AD)." .

ns1:49626 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Euroflora is an exhibition of flowers and ornamental plants. Euroflora takes place every five years (quinquennial), with the first edition in 1966. Euroflora was designed inspired by the famous floralie of Ghent, thanks to the ingenious intuition of the President of the Ente Fiera di Genova Carlo Pastorino that involved the Genoese and Ligurian floriculturists in this ambitious project. Fiera di Genova, Genova, 1966 - 1966 In this inaugural edition they were also attendant the actress Grace Kelly, Princess of Monaco and Prince Rainier III of Monaco." .

ns1:49633 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1950 Oregon gubernatorial election took place on 07 November 1950 to elect the governor of the U.S. state of Oregon. In the Democratic primary, Portland attorney and state senator Austin F. Flegel defeated Oregon State Treasurer Walter J. Pearson and former state senator and 1942 and 1948 Oregon gubernatorial special election Democratic gubernatorial nominee Lew Wallace." .

