ns1:49719 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1974 Scottish Cup Final was played on 04 May 1974 at Hampden Park in Glasgow and was the final of the 89th Scottish Cup. Celtic F.C. and Dundee United F.C. contested the match, Celtic F.C. won the match 3–0 with goals from Harry Hood, Steve Murray and Dixie Deans. The game was Celtic F.C.'s sixth successive appearance in the final, and Dundee United F.C.'s first cup final appearance. In a poor game Celtic F.C. rarely looked troubled by the young Dundee United F.C. team who appeared nervous in their first cup final appearance." .

ns1:49721 a ns1:context_narration ;
