ns1:49734 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 World Series was the World Series of Major League Baseball's (MLB) 1981 Major League Baseball season. The 78th edition of the World Series, it was a best-of-seven playoff played between the American League (AL) champion New York Yankees and the National League (NL) champion Los Angeles Dodgers. After combining for 10 division titles and eight World Series appearances between 1974 and 1981, the 1981 World Series marked the end of an era for both teams as they soon were without key contributors. 1981 World Series (4–2): Los Angeles Dodgers (N.L.) Yankees pitcher George Frazier tied a World Series record for losing three of the six games in 1981. Michaels became ABC's lead baseball play-by-play announcer (and exclusive World Series announcer) by the time the network next aired the World Series in 1983." .

ns1:49741 a ns1:context_narration ;
