ns1:49956 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Ellamy was the codename for the United Kingdom participation in the 2011 military intervention in Libya. The UN Security Council Resolution 1973 passed on the evening of 17 19 March 2011 gave a mandate to countries wishing to enforce a 2011 military intervention in Libya over Libya militarily." .

ns1:49959 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2009 Argentine legislative election were held in Argentina for half the seats in the Chamber of Deputies and a third (24) of the seats in the Senate on 28 June 2009, as well as for the legislature of the City of Buenos Aires and other municipalities. In 2009, the Mayor of Buenos Aires, Mauricio Macri, moved to bring forward the date of elections to the Buenos Aires City Legislature to 28 June 2009, saying that it would increase transparency and democratic quality." .

ns1:49960 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1964–65 FA Cup was the 84th staging of the world's oldest association football cup competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup, commonly known as the FA Cup. Liverpool F.C. won the competition for the first time (despite having reached two finals previously), beating Leeds United 2–1 after extra time in the 1965 FA Cup Final at Wembley. Leeds United and Liverpool F.C. came through the semi 1965 FA Cup Final round to meet at Wembley. The 1965 FA Cup Final was contested by Liverpool F.C. and Leeds United at Wembley on Saturday 1 May 1965." .

ns1:49964 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Copa Colsanitas was a women's tennis tournament played on clay court. It was the 18th edition of the Copa Colsanitas, and part of the WTA International tournaments of the 2015 WTA Tour. It took place at the Centro de Alto Rendimiento in Bogotá, Colombia, from 13 April 2015 through 19 April 2015." .

ns1:49968 a ns1:context_narration ;
