ns1:50717 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Killing of Patrick Harmon was a 50-year-old African-American man fatally shot from behind by police officer Clinton Fox in Salt Lake City, Utah, on 13 August 2017. The incident led to protests in Salt Lake City, some organized by Black Lives Matter." .

ns1:50723 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Thirty Mile Fire was first reported on July 9, 2001 in the Okanogan National Forest, approximately 30 miles (48 km) north of Winthrop, Washington, United States. The Entiat IHC had spent July 9 suppressing a fire near Spokane, Washington, and was dispatched to the Thirty Mile Fire with almost no rest. After arriving in Twisp, Washington at 7 am, the crew was informed they would instead be sent to the Thirty Mile Fire." .

ns1:50724 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 Big South Conference Men's Basketball Tournament took place from March 2–4, 1989 at the Winthrop Coliseum in Rock Hill, South Carolina." .

ns1:50725 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Shubra Khit, also known as the Battle of Chobrakit, was the first major engagement of Napoleon's campaign in Egypt that took place on 13 July 1798, 1798." .

ns1:50728 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004–05 Scottish Second Division was won by Brechin City F.C. who, along with second placed Stranraer, gained promotion to the First Division." .

ns1:50729 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 KC Masterpiece 400 was a Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series Kansas 400 held on 12 May 2018, at Kansas Speedway in Kansas City, Kansas. Contested over 267 laps on the 1.5 mile (2.4 km) asphalt speedway, it was the 12th Kansas 400 of the 2018 Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series season. Kansas Speedway is a 1.5-mile (2.4 km) tri-oval Kansas 400 track in Kansas City, Kansas. Kevin Harvick scored the pole for the Kansas 400 with a time of 28.600 and a speed of 188.811 mph (303.862 km/h). Fox Sports covered their eighth Kansas 400 at the Kansas Speedway." .

ns1:50730 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pan-European Picnic (German: Paneuropäisches Picknick; Hungarian: páneurópai piknik; Slovak: Paneurópsky piknik) was a peace demonstration held on the Austrian-Hungarian border near Sopron, Hungary on 19 August 1989. The Pan-European Picnic is considered a significant milestone on the road to German reunification, and commemorative ceremonies are held annually on 19 August 1989 at the border." .

ns1:50734 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Clades Lolliana or Lollian disaster was a battle in 16 BCE, when the consul Marcus Lollius Paulinus was defeated by the Sicambri, Tencteri and Usipetes, Germanic tribes who had crossed the Rhine." .

ns1:50737 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "World Sparrow Day is a day designated to raise awareness of the house sparrow and then other common birds to urban environments, and of threats to their populations, observed on 20 March. World Sparrow Day also has a broader vision to provide a platform where people who are working on the conservation of the house sparrow and other common birds can network, collaborate and exchange conservation ideas which will lead to better science and improved results." .

ns1:50766 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Lucheng of 213 was part of a rebellion led by Yang Fu against the warlord Ma Chao in the late Eastern Han dynasty." .

ns1:50767 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1968 Memorial Cup was the 50th annual Memorial Cup competition, organized by the Canadian Amateur Hockey Association (CAHA) to determine the champion of junior A ice hockey. The George Richardson Memorial Trophy champions Niagara Falls Flyers of the Ontario Hockey Association in Eastern Canada competed against the Abbott Cup champions Estevan Bruins of the Western Canada Junior Hockey League in Western Canada." .

ns1:50769 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cyclone Olivia was a powerful cyclone that produced the highest non-tornadic winds on record on Barrow Island, 408 kilometres per hour (254 mph), breaking the record of 372 km/h (231 mph) on Mount Washington in the United States in April 1934. The 13th named storm of the 1995–96 Australian region cyclone season, Olivia formed on 03 April 1996 to the north of Australia's Northern Territory. Shortly thereafter, the BoM upgraded the system to a Category 1 cyclone, designating the storm as Tropical Cyclone Olivia." .

ns1:50771 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The cross-country skiing at the 1968 Winter Olympics – women's 3 × 5 kilometre relay event was part of the cross-country skiing at the 1968 Winter Olympics at the 1968 Winter Olympics, in Grenoble, France." .

ns1:50776 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 30 June 1798 was a minor naval engagement fought along the Biscay coast of France during the French Revolutionary Wars." .

ns1:50778 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 UEFA European Under-17 Football Championship was the tenth edition of Union of European Football Associations's UEFA European Under-17 Football Championship. Serbia hosted the tournament between the 03 May 2011 and 15 May 2011." .

ns1:50797 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Algerian Cup Final saw Entente Sportive Sétifienne beat CA Batna to win their seventh Algerian Cup. The match took place on Wednesday, 2010 at the Stade 5 Juillet 1962 in Algiers and ended 3–0 with a brace by Hocine Metref and an own goal from Saber Chebana. Prior to the 2010 final, Entente Sportive Sétifienne had reached the final of the Algerian Cup six times, winning all six of them, while CA Batna had reached the final just once in 1997, losing to USM Alger in the final. Entente Sportive Sétifienne won both of the games between the two sides in the 2009–10 Algerian Championnat National, winning 2–1 at home and 3–0 in Batna." .

ns1:50802 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006–07 Magyar Kupa (Hungarian: Magyar Kupa) had involved professional teams at all levels throughout the country." .

ns1:50804 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Vijay Amritraj defeated Tim Wilkison 7–6, 5–7, 6–1, 6–2 to win the 1977 New Zealand Open – singles singles competition." .

ns1:50805 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1975 Scottish League Cup Final was played on 25 October 1975 and was the final of the 30th Scottish League Cup competition. It was contested by the Old Firm rivals, Rangers F.C. and Celtic F.C.. Rangers F.C. won the match 1–0, with the only goal scored by Alex MacDonald." .

ns1:50809 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 African U-20 Cup of Nations for Women was the 4th edition of the African U-20 Cup of Nations for Women, the biennial international youth association football competition organised by the Confederation of African Football (CAF) to determine which women's under-20 national teams from Africa qualify for the FIFA U-20 Women's World Cup. The First Round matches were played from 4 to 2008." .

ns1:50816 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 GoDaddy.com Bowl the thirteenth edition of the GoDaddy.com Bowl, an American college football bowl game. Part of the 2011 NCAA Division I FBS football season, and one of the 2011–12 NCAA football bowl games, it took place on 2012, at Ladd–Peebles Stadium in Mobile, Alabama." .

ns1:50818 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 BWF International Challenge is the twelfth season of the BWF International Challenge." .

ns1:50831 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The ITU World Triathlon Series is World Triathlon's annual series of triathlon events used to crown an annual world champion. With the establishment of the International Triathlon Union (International Triathlon Union) in 1989 it was quickly established that the governing body should host a yearly world championship to establish the men's and women's world champion. With a world championship and a regular season established the International Triathlon Union's attention moved onto other issues including earning the sport a place at the Olympics. Then in 2008 the day after the 2008 men's Olympic triathlon race the International Triathlon Union announced starting next year it would be replacing the single race world championship with a six-race World Championship points super series culminating in a Grand Final, it was to be called the World Championship Series (WCS). The final race of each season is known as the grand final and has extra points, prize money and prestige associated with it, when a city bids to host the grand final it also bids to host many International Triathlon Union events such as the amateur Age-group world championships and the Paratriathlon world championship." .

ns1:50838 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 UCI Track Cycling World Cup Classics is a multi race tournament over a season of track cycling. The season ran from 2003 to 18 May 2003." .

ns1:50840 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The San Luis Obispo International Film Festival (SLOIFF) is an American film festival held in San Luis Obispo. The San Luis Obispo International Film Festival was founded in 1993 by Mary Harris, Cathy Peacock, Jim Dee, Patty Dee and Lee Cogan." .

ns1:50842 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1995 Icelandic parliamentary election were held in Iceland on 08 April 1995." .

ns1:50845 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 Hungarian parliamentary election were held in Hungary on 25 March 1990, with a second round of voting taking place in all but five single member constituencies on 8 April." .

ns1:50855 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1405, adopted unanimously on 19 April 2002, after recalling resolutions 242 (1967), 338 (1973), 1397 (2002), 1402 (2002) and 1403 (2002), the Council emphasised the necessity of humanitarian access to the Palestinian population." .

ns1:50862 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1961 European Cup Winners' Cup Final was an association football match contested between ACF Fiorentina of Italy and Rangers F.C. of Scotland. It was the final match of the 1960–61 European Cup Winners' Cup and the first European Cup Winners' Cup final. The first leg was played at Ibrox Park, Glasgow and the second leg at the Stadio Comunale in Florence. It was Rangers F.C. first European final and in doing so became the first British team to reach the final of a European football competition. It was ACF Fiorentina's second European final having previously reached the 1957 European Cup Final. ACF Fiorentina won the final 4–1 on aggregate. Rangers F.C. were required to play a preliminary round in the competition where they beat Ferencváros from Hungary 5-4 on aggregate. In the semi final Rangers F.C. were then required to play English team Wolverhampton Wanderers. Rangers F.C. won the tie 3-1 on aggregate to reach their first ever European final. ACF Fiorentina, who were managed by Hungarian Nándor Hidegkuti, were the recent Coppa Italia winners and had reached the final of the European Cup four years earlier. Rangers F.C. were managed by Scot Symon and had reached the semi-final of the European Cup the previous year." .

ns1:50865 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Dilam was a major battle of the Unification of Saudi Arabia between Rashidi and Saudi rebels." .

ns1:50868 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 197 was a mixed martial arts event held on 23 April 2016, at MGM Grand Garden Arena in Las Vegas. The event's number was initially planned for an event taking place on March 5, 2016 at HSBC Arena in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, before being cancelled on December 29, 2015 and moved to MGM Grand Garden Arena in Las Vegas, to take place on February 6, 2016; the February event became UFC Fight Night: Hendricks vs. Thompson rather than a numbered pay-per-view after Vitor Belfort declined to fight Anderson Silva, and the March show was renumbered as UFC 196." .

ns1:50869 a ns1:context_narration ;
