ns1:50948 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Schweinschädel was a minor engagement of the Austro-Prussian War of 1866, during the Königgrätz/Sadowa campaign in Bohemia on 29 June." .

ns1:50956 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of York was fought on 27 April 1813, in York (present-day Toronto), the capital of the colonial province of Upper Canada (present-day Ontario), during the War of 1812. York, the capital of Upper Canada, stood on the north shore of Lake Ontario. During the War of 1812, the lake was both the front line between Upper Canada and the United States, and also served as the principal British supply line from Quebec to the various forces and outposts to the west. Historians such as John R. Elting have pointed out that this change of plan effectively reversed Armstrong's original strategy, and by committing the bulk of the American forces at the western end of Lake Ontario, it left Sackett's Harbor vulnerable to an attack by British reinforcements arriving from Lower Canada. The library books that were looted from the battle in 27 April 1813, were returned to the settlement during the second incursion into York. The burning and looting of York after the battle, along with the destruction of other Upper Canadian settlements during the war, saw public opinions on Americans shift among the residents of Upper Canada. On 27 April 1813, 2013, the City of Toronto government and the Canadian Armed Forces commemorated the 200th anniversary of the battle with a Presentation of Colours to the 3rd Battalion, The Royal Canadian Regiment. The ceremony and parade were organize in conjunction with other War of 1812 bicentennial commemorations held in Toronto, and the other municipalities in Ontario. During the bicentennial celebrations, the City of Toronto Museum Services commissioned the creation of the exhibit Finding the Fallen: the Battle of York Remembered at Fort York." .

ns1:50957 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 NCAA Division I Men's Tennis Championships were the 56th annual NCAA Division I Men's Tennis Championship to determine the national champions of NCAA Division I men's singles, doubles, and team collegiate tennis in the United States of America." .

ns1:50960 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Aaron's 499 was the ninth race in the 2008 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. It was held on 27 April 2008 at Talladega Superspeedway in Talladega, Alabama." .

ns1:50966 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "speed skiing was a Olympic demonstration sport competition at the speed skiing at the 1992 Winter Olympics." .

ns1:50975 a ns1:context_narration ;
