ns1:51493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1956 United States presidential election in Pennsylvania took place on 06 November 1956 as part of the 1956 United States presidential election. Pennsylvania strongly voted for the Republican nominee, President of the United States Dwight D. Eisenhower, over the Democratic nominee, former Illinois Governor Adlai Stevenson II. Pennsylvania was the home state of President of the United States Eisenhower, as he moved to the Gettysburg area after World War II." .

ns1:51505 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Algeciras Campaign (sometimes known as the Battle or Battles of Algeciras) was an attempt by a French naval squadron from Toulon under Contre-Admiral Charles Linois to join a French and Spanish fleet at Cadiz during June and 14 July 1801 during the French Revolutionary War prior to a planned operation against either Egypt or Portugal. Saumarez ordered that the most damaged of the surviving ships, Pompée and Caesar, be laid up in dock and their crews distributed among the remaining ships to ensure that they could be repaired as rapidly as possible, a situation made necessary in part due to the seizure of many of Gibraltar's shipwrights in the Bay of Gibraltar when they were sent to aid Hannibal in the last stages of the battle." .

ns1:51510 a ns1:context_narration ;
