ns1:51518 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss USA 1997, the 46th Miss USA pageant, was held at Shreveport, Louisiana in January and February, 1997. At the conclusion of the final competition, Brook Lee of Hawaii was crowned by outgoing titleholder Ali Landry of Louisiana, becoming the fourth Hawaiian to win the Miss USA pageant and the first win in 19 years, since Judi Andersen in Miss USA 1978. After Lee won the Miss Universe 1997 title three months later, first runner-Up Brandi Sherwood of Idaho inherited the Miss USA title. Upon Sherwood inheriting the Miss USA 1997 title, she also became the first Idaho delegate to hold the Miss USA title." .

ns1:51519 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ashton Court Festival was an outdoor music festival held annually in mid-July on the grounds of Ashton Court, just outside Bristol, England. Ashton Court Estate, which includes a deer park, was closed as a quarantine measure due to the outbreak of foot and mouth disease that affected the United Kingdom that year." .

ns1:51524 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "DirectSound is a deprecated software component of the Microsoft DirectX library for the Windows operating system, superseded by XAudio2. After many years of development, today DirectSound is a mature application programming interface, and supplies many other useful capabilities, such as the ability to play multichannel sounds at high resolution. DirectSound is a user mode application programming interface that provides an interface between applications and the sound card driver, enabling applications to produce sounds and play back music. DirectSound provides sample rate conversion and sound mixing (volume and pan) for an unlimited number of audio sources; however, the practical limits are the number of hardware audio sources and the performance of software mixers. If hardware acceleration is not available, DirectSound would create audio buffers in the system memory and use purely software mixing. DirectSound3D (DS3D) is an extension to DirectSound introduced with DirectX 3 in 1996 with the intention to standardize 3D audio in Windows. DirectSound3D allows software developers to utilize audio by writing once for a single audio application programming interface instead of rewriting code numerous times to work for each audio card vendor. In DirectX 8, DirectSound and DirectSound3D (DS3D) were officially merged and given the name DirectX Audio, however the application programming interface is still commonly referred to as DirectSound. In Windows 95, 98 and Me, the DirectSound mixer component and the sound card drivers were both implemented as a kernel-mode VxD driver (Dsound.vxd), allowing direct access to the primary buffer used by the audio hardware and thus, providing the lowest possible latency between the user-mode application programming interface and the underlying hardware, but in some cases causing instability and blue screen errors. Under WDM, DirectSound sends data to the software-based KMixer. DirectSound runs in emulation mode on the Microsoft software mixer. The emulator does not have hardware abstraction, so there is no hardware DirectSound acceleration, meaning hardware and software relying on DirectSound acceleration may have degraded performance. Windows CE 6.0 also does not support DirectSound, instead favoring that applications be rewritten to use the Waveform Audio application programming interface." .

ns1:51528 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 PFC CSKA Sofia season was PFC CSKA - Sofia's 66th consecutive season in A Group." .

