    rdfs:label "The 1953 Ionian Earthquake (also known as the Great Kefalonia earthquake) struck the southern Ionian Islands in Greece on 12 August 1953. In mid-August there were over 113 recorded earthquakes in the region between Kefalonia and Zakynthos, and the most destructive was the 12 August 1953 earthquake." .

