ns1:52320 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ahvaz National Resistance (Persian: مقاومت ملی اهواز) is an ethnic Arab opposition movement in Iran that seeks an independent state in Khuzestan Province. Speaking to Iran International TV in London, Yaqoub al-Tostari, spokesman for one of the two groups that identify themselves as the Arab Struggle Movement for the Liberation of Ahvaz, said the Ahvaz National Resistance was behind the attack, which killed 25 people excluding the five assailants, but did not specify which group." .

ns1:52321 a ns1:context_narration ;
