ns1:52669 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Canberra Day is a public holiday held annually on the second Monday in March in the Australian Capital Territory (ACT) to celebrate the official naming of Canberra. On 3 March 2007, the ACT Minister Andrew Barr (now Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory) introduced a bill to change the day of Canberra Day to the second Monday in March so it falls closer more often to the actual birthday of Canberra." .

ns1:52671 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Triple Crown Trophy is a silver trophy awarded to the winner of the Triple Crown of Thoroughbred Racing. Commissioned in 1950 by the Thoroughbred Racing Association, artisans at the world-famous Cartier Jewelry Company were charged with creating not just a trophy, but a true work of art. Today the Triple Crown Trophy is a permanent trophy awarded to the winner with information pertaining to each race engraved on corresponding sides. In addition to the Triple Crown Trophy, winners of the Kentucky Derby are given the Kentucky Derby Trophy, a solid gold trophy worth in excess of $90,000; winners of the Preakness Stakes are presented the Woodlawn Vase in a national TV ceremony and given a solid silver replica worth in excess of $30,000 for permanent possession; winners of the Belmont Stakes are presented the August Belmont Trophy and given a silver tray for their permanent possession." .

ns1:52674 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In computing, reactive programming is a declarative programming paradigm concerned with data streams and the propagation of change. Functional reactive programming (FRP) is a programming paradigm for reactive programming on functional programming." .

