    rdfs:label "The 2017 FIRS Men's Roller Hockey World Cup was the 43rd edition of the Roller Hockey World Cup, organised by the Fédération Internationale de Roller Sports (Fédération Internationale de Roller Sports). The tournament was held for the first time in People's Republic of China, in the city of Nanjing, from 3 to 2017, as part of the 2017 World Roller Games." .

ns1:53075 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Portugal participated in the Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest 2018. In addition to participating in the contest, the Portuguese broadcaster Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP) also hosted the event on 8, 2018 and 2018, at the Altice Arena in Lisbon, after winning the competition in 2017 with the song \"Amar pelos dois\" performed by Salvador Sobral. The Portuguese entry for the 2018 contest was selected through a national final, the Festival da Canção. Prior to the 2018 Contest, Portugal had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest forty-nine times since its first entry in 1964. The Portuguese broadcaster for the 2018 Contest, who broadcasts the event in Portugal and organises the selection process for its entry, will be Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP). Portugal has most commonly selected their entry through the national final Festival da Canção except between 2003 and 2005 where the broadcaster used internal selections and the talent competition Operação triunfo to select their entry. The broadcaster will organize the 2018 edition of Festival da Canção in order to select the Portuguese entry for the 2018 Eurovision Song Contest. Festival da Canção 2018 was the 52nd edition of Festival da Canção, the music competition that selects Portugal's entries for the Eurovision Song Contest. 26 entries participated in the 52nd Festival da Canção. Among the competing artists were former Eurovision Song Contest entrants José Cid, who represented Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest and 1998 Contests, the latter as part of Alma Lusa, and Anabela, who represented Portugal in the 1993 Contest. The Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest 2018 took place at the Altice Arena in Lisbon, Portugal and consisted of two semi-finals on 8 May and 10 May and the final on 2018." .

ns1:53076 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Voice, The Guitar, The Songs Tour was a co-headlining concert tour by Latin rock band Santana and Rod Stewart." .

ns1:53081 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The year WEC 10 is the 4th year in the history of World Extreme Cagefighting, a mixed martial arts promotion based in the United States. In WEC 10 WEC held 4 events beginning with, WEC 9: Cold Blooded. WEC 9: Cold Blooded was an event held on January 16, WEC 10 at the Tachi Palace in Lemoore, California, United States. WEC 11: Evolution was an event held on August 20, WEC 10 at the Tachi Palace in Lemoore, California, United States." .

ns1:53083 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "By 2014, TriMet included rail operators by changing the name of Bus Driver Appreciation Day to Transit Driver Appreciation Day." .

ns1:53084 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Australian GT Championship season was a CAMS sanctioned Australia motor racing title for cars complying with Group D regulations for GT cars, with Group B Sports Sedans competing by invitation. 1982 Australian GT Championship winner Alan Jones moved back to Formula One in 1983 and did not defend his title. Following the accident, neither the Monza nor the JPS BMW were raced until November at the 1983 Australia Grand Prix at Calder Park in Melbourne in the Sports Car / GT Challenge support races." .

ns1:53088 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Treaty of Perth, signed 2 09 July 1266, ended military conflict between Magnus VI of Norway and Alexander III of Scotland over possession of the Hebrides and the Isle of Man." .

ns1:53091 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lutte pour le changement is a group based in Goma in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo who fights for a class of rights that protect Congoleses' freedom from infringement by governments, social organizations, and private individuals. The political movement started in the eastern city of Goma in the Democratic Republic of Congo in mid-June 2011 and in no time, the political movement had spread all the way to the west of the country, with famous members such as Fred Bauma and Yves Makwambala being incarcerated since March 2015 at the Congolese National Intelligence Agency headquarters in Kinshasa. This political movement got the eye of the Congolese people because this group managed first and foremost to get the general population to have a say in these critical matters facing their livelihood through the streets of various Congolese cities namely Kinshasa, Mbuji-Mayi, Lubumbashi, Kisangani et Goma. These inspired Congolese youths driven by social injustice and non democratic political process believe that their political movement can bring about positive change in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, as well as Africa as a whole. The digital evolution with the improvements on the application such as WhatsApp, Imo and Skype has helped the political movement with communications, conference calls among participants in various locations within the Democratic Republic of the Congo as well as the Congolese diaspora via various Congolese online media, such as Congo Mikili." .

ns1:53103 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ginetta GT5 Challenge, currently known as the Protyre Motorsport Ginetta GT5 Challenge for sponsorship reasons (It has also been previously known as the Ginetta 20 Challenge) is a one-make racing series based in the United Kingdom." .

