ns1:53279 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Uganda Super League was the 39th season of the official Ugandan football championship, the top-level football league of Uganda. The 2006 Uganda Super League was contested by 15 teams and was won by Uganda Revenue Authority SC, while Kampala United, KB Lions and Super Cubs were relegated. The top goalscorer in the 2006 season was Dan Walusimbi of Police FC with 15 goals." .

ns1:53281 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Nippon Professional Baseball draft was held on 2014 at the Grand Prince Hotel Takanawa to assign amateur baseball players to the Nippon Professional Baseball. Only the first round picks were allowed to be contested with all picks from the second round onward being based on table placing in the 2014 Nippon Professional Baseball season in a waiver system. The Draft waiver priority was decided upon the winners of the 2014 Nippon Professional Baseball All-Stars game, but as the series ended 1-1 preference was based on point difference between the Central and Pacific Leagues where the former had a higher differential." .

ns1:53291 a ns1:context_narration ;
