ns1:53314 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985 European Grand Prix (formally the Shell Oils Grand Prix of Europe) was a Formula One motor race held at Brands Hatch on 06 October 1985. The 75-lap race was won by Nigel Mansell, driving a Williams-Honda. Qualifying saw Ayrton Senna take his sixth pole position of the season in his Lotus-Renault, averaging 140.106 mph (225.479 km/h), the first time anyone had lapped the Brands Hatch circuit faster than 140 mph." .

ns1:53324 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Riojan regional election was held on Sunday, 2007, to elect the 7th Parliament of the autonomous community of La Rioja. The 2003 Riojan regional election was held on 25 May 2003, setting the election date for the Parliament on Sunday, 2007." .

ns1:53327 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 Honduran Liga Nacional season was the 48th Liga Nacional de Fútbol Profesional de Honduras edition, since its establishment in 1965. A total of 10 teams will contest the league, including 9 sides from the 2012–13 Honduran Liga Nacional plus Parrillas One, promoted from the 2012–13 Liga de Ascenso." .

ns1:53333 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Dingle's Mill was an American Civil War battle that took place near Sumterville, Sumter County, South Carolina. On Easter Day, 09 April 1865, the Battle of Dingle's Mill was fought 3 miles (4.8 km) south of Sumterville. After the battle, the camp followers also hanged Mr. Bee, an elderly Charleston gentleman who had fled to Sumter County from Charleston during the war." .

ns1:53334 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 Torneo Descentralizado was the 50th season of the highest division of Peruvian association football. The first match of the season was played on 1966 between Club Universitario de Deportes and Mariscal Sucre in the Estadio Nacional." .

