ns1:53450 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1956 Anjar earthquake occurred at 15:32 UTC on 21 July 1956, causing maximum damage in town of Anjar in Kutch, Gujarat, India. The epicenter of earthquake of 21 July 1956 was at somewhere between Anjar and Bhadresar, very close to that of 1819 Kutch earthquake, between 50 and 120 km away depending on the epicentral location chosen for the earlier event." .

ns1:53455 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009–10 CONCACAF Champions League was the second edition of the CONCACAF Champions League under its current format, and overall the 45th edition of the premier association football club competition organized by CONCACAF, the regional governing body of North America, Central America and the Caribbean. As winners, CF Pachuca qualified for the 2010 FIFA Club World Cup as the CONCACAF representative. 24 teams participated in the 2009–10 CONCACAF Champions League from the North American, Central American, and Caribbean zones. It was announced on 2009 that Belize had lost their lone qualification to Honduras due to the inability of the Belize federation to meet CONCACAF's minimum requirements in regards to stadium facilities. On 2009 CONCACAF announced that Luís Ángel Firpo of El Salvador was invited to take the place of Chalatenango due to Chalatengo's failure to sign and return the required participation agreement. The draw for the Preliminary Round was held on 2009, at the CONCACAF headquarters in New York City. The first legs of the Preliminary Round were played the week of 28 July 2009, while the second legs were played the week of 2009; this is a month earlier than the previous season." .

