ns1:53932 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season was the 30th season of competitive football by Southampton F.C., and the club's third in the Second Division of the Football League. Southampton F.C. used 22 different players during the 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season and had eight different goalscorers. At the end of the 1923–24 Southampton F.C. season, Southampton F.C. brought in centre-half John Callagher and inside-forward Stan Woodhouse from Bury, who had just been promoted to the First Division as runners-up of the second flight. The last transfer activity of the 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season came in February 1925, when wing-half Albert Barrett joined Southampton F.C. from West Ham United, making one appearance in the Second Division before leaving for Fulham the following summer. Southampton F.C.'s 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season started similarly poorly to the 1923–24 Southampton F.C. season. Southampton F.C. finished in seventh place with 13 wins, 18 draws and 11 losses, two places and four points lower than 1923–24 Southampton F.C. season. Outside of the league and the FA Cup, Southampton F.C. played four additional first-team matches during the 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season. Southampton F.C. used 22 different players during the 1924–25 Southampton F.C. season, eight of whom scored during the campaign." .

ns1:53933 a ns1:context_narration ;
