ns1:54129 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 NBA Playoffs was the NBA Playoffs of the National Basketball Association's 2017–18 season. The playoffs began on 14 April 2018 and ended on June 8 at the conclusion of the 2018 NBA Finals." .

ns1:54133 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 San Diego mayoral special election was a special election held on Tuesday, 2005, to elect the mayor for San Diego. On 2005, Dick Murphy announced that he would resign as mayor of San Diego, effective 2005. Murphy had only recently been reelected as mayor in the highly contested 2004 San Diego mayoral election. Council member Toni Atkins then served as acting mayor until the mayoral election was complete." .

ns1:54137 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Canadian Mixed Doubles Curling Trials were held from March 11 to 15 at the Ottawa Hunt and Golf Club in Ottawa, Ontario. The winning team of Charley Thomas and Kalynn Park will represent Canada at the 2015 World Mixed Doubles Curling Championship." .

ns1:54140 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kan'ei famine (寛永の大飢饉 Kan'ei no daikikin) was a famine which affected Japan during the reign of Empress Meishō in the Edo period. The Bakufu government used the practices learned during the Kan'ei famine for the management of the later famines, most notably during the Tenpō famine in 1833. Also, together with the expulsion of Christianity from Japan, the Kan'ei famine set a template for how the Bakufu would address country-wide problems, bypassing daimyō." .

ns1:54145 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Open Championship was a men's major golf championship and the 144th The Open Championship, held from 16 July–20 July at the Old Course at St Andrews in Fife, Scotland. It was the 29th The Open Championship played at the course and Zach Johnson won in a four-hole playoff for his second major title. The 2015 event is the 29th The Open Championship played at the Old Course at St Andrews. The most recent was in 2010 when Louis Oosthuizen won his only major title and became the first South African to win an The Open Championship at St Andrews." .

ns1:54147 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 7th edition of the 2015 Asian Women's Amateur Boxing Championships were held from August 07 to 2015 in Ulanqab, People's Republic of China." .

ns1:54160 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The weightlifting at the 2018 Asian Games – women's 53 kg event at the 2018 Asian Games took place on 2018 at the Jakarta International Expo." .

ns1:54162 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 130, adopted on 25 November 1958, noted with regret the death of Judge José Gustavo Guerrero on October 25, 1958." .

ns1:54165 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1964 United States presidential election in North Carolina took place on 03 November 1964, and was part of the 1964 United States presidential election. North Carolina voted for incumbent Democratic President Lyndon B. Johnson, with 56.15 percent of the vote, over Republican nominee Barry Goldwater, who obtained 43.85 percent." .

ns1:54169 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The swimming at the 2004 Summer Olympics – men's 100 metre butterfly event at the 2004 Olympic Games was contested at the Athens Olympic Aquatic Centre of the Athens Olympic Sports Complex in Athens, Greece on 19 August 2004 and 20." .

ns1:54174 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sacrifice was a professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event produced by the Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) promotion that took place on May 11, 2008 at the TNA Impact! It was the fourth event in the Sacrifice chronology and fifth event in the 2008 TNA PPV schedule. Sacrifice is noted for the Deuces Wild Tag Team Tournament and the debut of the TerrorDome, later renamed the Steel Asylum at TNA's Bound for Glory IV PPV event on October 12, 2008. Chris Sokol of the professional wrestling section of the Canadian Online Explorer rated Sacrifice a seven out of ten, the same ranking he gave the Sacrifice (2007). Sacrifice featured ten professional wrestling matches that involved wrestlers from pre-existing scripted feuds and storylines portraying villains, heroes, or less distinguishable characters; these scripted events built tension and culminated in a wrestling match or series of matches. The main event at Sacrifice was a Three Way match for the TNA World Heavyweight Championship between then-champion Samoa Joe and challengers Kurt Angle and Scott Steiner. The four winning teams would then compete in a single-elimination tournament against eight wrestlers chosen by Cornette to be assigned as teams at Sacrifice. Chris Sokol of the Canadian Online Explorer rated Sacrifice a seven out of ten; the same rating he gave to the 2007 Sacrifice event and higher than TNA's previous event, Lockdown, which he gave a six and a half out of ten. Sokol felt that Sacrifice was a \"decent PPV\", and \"interesting\" overall and rated main event a seven and a half out of ten; he described it as a \"solid match, with good wrestling\". Sacrifice received a higher rating than rival World Wrestling Entertainment's Judgment Day PPV event, held on May 19, which Bob Kapur gave a six out of ten. The decision to remove Kurt Angle from the Sacrifice main event was not made until the day of the show. TNA later renamed the TerrorDome to the \"Steel Asylum\" when it was used on October 12, 2008 at their Bound for Glory IV PPV event." .

ns1:54178 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Uijeongbu (1951), also known as the Battle of Uijongbu, was a battle fought between 1951–04 January 1951, at Uijeongbu, South Korea, as part of the United Nations Command (UN) retreat after the third Chinese People's Volunteer Army (PVA) offensive after entering the Korean War." .

ns1:54181 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sheer Heart Attack Tour was the first world tour by the British rock band Queen, and supported their 1974 album Sheer Heart Attack." .

ns1:54186 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1912 All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final was the 25th All-Ireland Final and the culmination of the All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1912, an inter-county hurling tournament for the top teams in Ireland. The match was held at Croke Park, Dublin, on 1912, between Kilkenny, represented by club side Tullaroan, and Cork, represented by club side Blackrock." .

ns1:54191 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Mobley's Meeting House (also sometimes called Gibson's Meeting House) was an engagement that occurred during the American Revolutionary War in the Mobley Settlement, Fairfield County, South Carolina during the southern campaign of Lord Cornwallis." .

ns1:54197 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The participation of Indonesia in the ABU TV Song Festival has occurred thrice since the inaugural ABU TV Song Festival and began in 2012. Indonesia was the only country to hold a televised selection process for the first ABU TV Song Festival, the selection called \"Goes To Korea: ABU Asia Pacific TV Song Festival 2012 Indonesian Final\" was held with six singers competing to represent Indonesia in Seoul. Indonesia once again participated in the ABU TV Song Festival in Hanoi, Vietnam. On 26 June 2014 it was announced that Theresia Hutabarat also known as Tere Cia would represent Indonesia in Macau at the third ABU TV Song Festival. On 31 August 2015 Indonesia confirmed their intention to host the 2016 ABU TV Song Festival. At a press conference held on 18 July 2013 it was announced that Indonesia were submitting a bid to host the ABU TV Song Festival 2015." .

ns1:54198 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 757 was adopted on 30 May 1992." .

ns1:54199 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bere Ferrers rail accident occurred at Bere Ferrers railway station in England on 24 September 1917 when ten soldiers from New Zealand alighted from their troop train on the wrong side of the train, having assumed they should leave by the same side they had entered, and were struck and killed by an oncoming express." .

ns1:54200 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2002 Peoria County Board Election determined the membership of the Peoria County Board." .

