ns1:54468 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation RY was the Imperial Japanese plan to invade and occupy Nauru and Banaba Island islands in the south Pacific during the Pacific conflict of World War II. Nauru and Banaba Island Islands were isolated but rich with phosphate deposits; the deposits were identified around 1900. Nauru was under Australian mandate control, and Banaba Island Island (or Banaba) was headquarters of the British Gilbert and Ellice Islands Colony. In late February 1942, as a Japanese invasion of Nauru and Banaba Island Island was feared, the Free French destroyer Le Triomphant departed the New Hebrides to evacuate both places. The landing forces landed on Nauru on 29 August and Banaba Island Island on 30 August unopposed." .

ns1:54474 a ns1:context_narration ;
