    rdfs:label "Pure photography or straight photography refers to photography that attempts to depict a scene or subject in sharp focus and detail, in accordance with the qualities that distinguish photography from other visual media, particularly painting. In his autobiography, Ansel Adams used the terms straight photography and pure photography." .

