ns1:54940 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The United Kingdom general election, 2001 (London) was held on Thursday 07 June 2001, four years after the previous election on 1 May 1997, to elect 659 members to the House of Commons. The election had been expected on 3 May, to coincide with local elections, but on 2 April 2001, both were postponed to 07 June 2001 because of rural movement restrictions imposed in response to the foot-and-mouth outbreak that had started in February. During the election Sharron Storer, a resident of Birmingham, criticised Prime Minister Tony Blair in front of television cameras about conditions in the National Health Service." .

