ns1:54990 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Midwest FurFest (abbreviated MFF) is the world's largest furry convention, which takes place in Rosemont, Illinois each December. Midwest Furry Fandom, Inc. was created, and Midwest FurFest's first occurrence took place in 2000, on the weekend before Thanksgiving. The convention has grown from 473 attendees in 2000 to 10,989 in 2018, making it the largest furry convention in the world by more than 2,300 attendees over the previous largest convention, Anthrocon." .

