ns1:54998 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1949 Air France Lockheed Constellation crash was a scheduled international flight that crashed into a mountain while attempting to land at Santa Maria Airport, Azores on a stopover during a scheduled international passenger flight from Orly Airport to New York City. The aircraft was operating a scheduled international passenger flight from Orly Airport, France to New York City, with a stopover at Santa Maria Airport, Azores." .

ns1:54999 a ns1:context_narration ;
