ns1:55042 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Saint-Michel-de-Maurienne derailment of 12 December 1917 was a railway accident involving a troop train carrying at least 1,000 French soldiers on their way home for leave from the Italian Front in World War I." .

ns1:55047 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Memel was fought between the Samogitians and the Livonian branch of the Teutonic Knights in 1323." .

ns1:55050 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985–86 La Liga season, the 55th since its establishment, started on 31 August 1985, and finished on 20 April 1986." .

ns1:55054 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1952–53 FA Cup was the 72nd season of the world's oldest association football cup competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup, commonly known as the FA Cup. Blackpool F.C. won the competition for the first time, beating Bolton Wanderers 4–3 in the 1953 FA Cup Final at Wembley. Blackpool F.C. and Bolton Wanderers won their ties to meet in the 1953 FA Cup Final at Wembley. The 1953 FA Cup Final, known as the \"Matthews Final\" due to Stanley Matthews' dribbling in the last 30 minutes of the game, was contested by Blackpool F.C. and Bolton Wanderers at Wembley. Blackpool F.C. won 4–3, with Stan Mortensen the first player to score a FA Cup Final hat-trick." .

ns1:55057 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Athens was a siege of the First Mithridatic War that took place from Autumn of 87 BC to the Spring and Summer of 86 BC. At Chaeronea, ambassadors from all the major cities of Greece (except Athens) met with Sulla, who impressed on them Rome's determination to drive Mithridates from Greece and Asia Province. As such, Sulla was forced to conduct two separate sieges, throwing up siege works surrounding both Athens and its port Piraeus. Wood was also needed, so he cut down everything, including the sacred groves of Greece, up to 100 miles from Athens main town. Despite the complete encirclement of Athens and its port, and several attempts by Archelaus to raise the siege, a stalemate seemed to have developed. On 1 March 86 BC, after five months under siege, a midnight sack of Athens began. The siege of Athens was a long and brutal campaign, Sulla's rough battle hardened legions, veterans of the Social War thoroughly devastated the city." .

ns1:55065 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 131 was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 11 June 2011 at the Rogers Arena in Vancouver, Canada." .

ns1:55078 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1916 American Grand Prize was a Grand Prix auto race that took place at Santa Monica, California, on 18 November 1916." .

ns1:55080 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2019–20 UEFA Youth League was the seventh season of the Union of European Football Associations Youth League, a European youth club association football competition organised by Union of European Football Associations. A total of 64 teams from at least 32 of the 55 Union of European Football Associations member associations may enter the tournament. The draw for both the first round and second round was held on 3 17 September 2019, 14:00 CEST, at the Union of European Football Associations headquarters in Nyon, Switzerland." .

ns1:55081 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Nebelhorn Trophy took place between 04 September 2001 and 7, 2001 at the Bundesleistungszentrum Oberstdorf. It is an international senior-level figure skating competition organized by the Deutsche Eislauf-Union and held annually in Oberstdorf, Germany." .

ns1:55084 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Super League V was the official name for the year 2000's Super League championship season, the 106th season of top-level professional rugby league football in Britain, and the fifth championship run by Super League." .

ns1:55086 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The British Expedition to Abyssinia was a rescue mission and punitive expedition carried out in 1868 by the armed forces of the British Empire against the Ethiopian Empire. Likewise, Abyssinia was also threatened by the encroachment of Islam: Ottoman Turks and Egyptians repeatedly invaded Ethiopia from the Red Sea and from Sudan, while the Muslim Oromo tribe was expanding throughout Central Ethiopia. In the eyes of Alan Moorehead, \"There has never been in modern times a colonial campaign quite like the British expedition to Ethiopia in 1868. After the withdrawal of the English, fighting for the succession to Tewodros's throne raged in Ethiopia from 1868 to 1872." .

