ns1:55312 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017–18 Kerala Blasters FC season was the fourth season of competitive association football played by the Kerala Blasters FC. Kerala Blasters FC began their preparations for the 2017–18 Kerala Blasters FC season by bringing in former Manchester United assistant coach René Meulensteen as the club's new head coach. At halftime, James took off Karan Sawhney and brought on 19-year old Deependra Negi for his professional debut and three minutes into the second half the former India U17 captain scored the equalizer for the Kerala Blasters FC from a corner. The Super Cup is a knockout association football competition in India. The competition only featured teams from both the Indian Super League and the I-League, India's two top-tier association football leagues." .

