ns1:55362 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Asia-Pacific Fistball Championships are an international fistball competition run in conjunction with the International Fistball Association (IFA), and the Asia-Pacific Fistball Association (APFC) with the first men's championships held in Pakistan in 2014. While originally known as the Asian Fistball Championships, the tournament has been renamed to the Asia-Pacific Fistball Championships for subsequent iterations, to recognise the inclusion of Oceanic region fistball associations such as Australia and New Zealand." .

