ns1:55508 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "An Act to amend the Copyright Act (Bill C-32) was a bill tabled on June 2, 2010 during the third session of the 40th Canadian Parliament by Minister of Industry Tony Clement and by Minister of Canadian Heritage James Moore. In March 2011, the 40th Canadian Parliament was dissolved, with all the bills which did not pass by that point (including bill C-32) automatically becoming dead. In the aftermath of the bill, the United States diplomatic cables leak revealed ongoing pressure from US officials wanting Canada to pass stricter copyright laws." .

ns1:55516 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The name \"Sexagesima\" is derived from the Latin sexagesimus, meaning \"sixtieth,\" and appears to be a back-formation of Quinquagesima, the term formerly used to denote the last Sunday before Lent (the latter name alluding to the fact that there are fifty days between that Sunday and Easter, if one counts both days themselves in the total as was the usual custom of the Roman Empire). While Quinquagesima (50th day) is mathematically correct (allowing for the inclusive counting), Sexagesima and Septuagesima are only approximations (the exact number of days is 57 and 64 respectively). The earlier form of the Roman Rite, with its references to Quinquagesima, Sexagesima and Septuagesima, continues to be observed in some communities. The 1662 Book of Common Prayer, used in some Anglican provinces, retains Sexagesima Sunday (along with Septuagesima and Quinquagesima), as does the 1928 American Book of Common Prayer." .

ns1:55518 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The ski jumping at the 1984 Winter Olympics – normal hill ski jumping competition for the 1984 Winter Olympics was held at Igman Olympic Jumps." .

