ns1:55527 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1946 South Carolina gubernatorial election was held on 1946 to select the Governor of South Carolina of the state of South Carolina. Strom Thurmond won the contested Democratic primary and ran unopposed in the general election becoming the 103rd Governor of South Carolina. The South Carolina Democratic Party held their primary for Governor of South Carolina in the summer of 1946 and ten candidates entered the contest. The race featured Governor Ransome Judson Williams, who became Governor of South Carolina in 1945 upon the resignation of Olin D. Johnston, but it mainly became a contest between Strom Thurmond and James McLeod. Race was not an issue in the campaign and Strom Thurmond emerged victorious with the support of the returning veterans of World War II who wanted to reform South Carolina. The general election was held on 1946 and Strom Thurmond was elected the next Governor of South Carolina without opposition." .

