ns1:56010 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting 2011, commonly known as CHOGM 2011, was the twenty-second Meeting of the Heads of Government of the Commonwealth of Nations. Held in Perth, Western Australia, between 2011 and 2011 and hosted by the Prime Minister Julia Gillard. The summit failed to reach an agreement to endorse or even publish the Eminent Persons Group report; the United Kingdom, Australia and Canada urged the publication of the report but were opposed by India, Nigeria, Sri Lanka, South Africa and Namibia. Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh skipped the summit in protest against Australia's refusal to sell India uranium as it had not signed the Nuclear Nonproliferation Treaty. Australia later denied that Singh's pull out from the summit was over its refusal to sell uranium." .

ns1:56011 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Major League Soccer season featured 20 total clubs (17 based in the United States, 3 based in Canada). It includes the team, the average attendance for the 2016 regular season and the 2015 Major League Soccer season, the percentage change in attendance from season-to-season, the home venue, the home venue's capacity, and the percent of capacity." .

