ns1:56056 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Niasviž uprising, or Nieśwież Uprising (Polish: Powstanie nieświeskie, Belarusian: Нясвіжскае паўстанне) was a failed anti-Soviet pro-Polish insurrection residents of the town of Niasviž (Polish: Nieśwież, now Belarus. In early 1919, Niasviž was captured without fight by the Bolsheviks, who advanced westwards, behind German troops of the Ober Ost." .

