ns1:56098 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Football League Centenary Trophy (also known as the Mercantile Credit Centenary Trophy for sponsorship reasons) was an English football tournament held during the 1988–89 season to celebrate the 100th birthday of The Football League. The competition was played on a knockout basis between the top eight sides from the Football League First Division the previous season, with the final between Arsenal F.C. and Manchester United taking place at the birthplace of League football, Aston Villa's home ground, Villa Park on 09 October 1988. The tournament reached its climax on 09 October 1988, when Arsenal F.C. competed against Manchester United." .

