ns1:56950 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The International Pageant of Pulchritude, also known as Miss Universe or the International Beauty Contest, was a beauty contest that began in 1920, featuring contestants from multiple nations. The last pageant event in the United States was held in 1931 although additional Miss Universe events were held until 1935. In 1926, taking advantage of this trend, the Galveston event became an international competition known as the International Pageant of Pulchritude. \"Miss Universe\" events were instead held in Belgium in 1932 and 1935. After 1935 international competitions were discontinued until the modern Miss Universe contest was created in 1952 in California." .

