ns1:57075 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 59 was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 15 April 2006 at Honda Center, in Anaheim, and broadcast live on pay-per-view in the United States of America and Canada. This was the first UFC event held in California after the state's legalization of mixed martial arts contests." .

ns1:57078 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Jebus is a siege described in biblical passages as having occurred when Israelites under King David of Israel besieged and conquered the Canaanite city of Jerusalem, then known as Jebus (Hebrew: יבוס Yəḇūs, \"threshing-floor\"). The capture of Jebus is mentioned in 2 Samuel 5 and 1 Chronicles 11 with similar wordings: And David and all Israel went to Jerusalem, that is, Jebus, where the Jebusites were, the inhabitants of the land." .

ns1:57084 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1971 Bulgarian Cup Final was the 31st final of the Bulgarian Cup (in this period the tournament was named Cup of the Soviet Army), and was contested between PFC Levski Sofia and PFC Lokomotiv Plovdiv on 1971 at Balgarska Armia Stadium in Sofia." .

ns1:57085 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The PUK insurgency was a low-level rebellion of the Patriotic Union of Kurdistan (PUK) against Ba'athist Iraq from 1975-1979, following the defeat of the Kurdistan Democratic Party (KDP) in the Second Iraqi–Kurdish War, which forced that organization to declare a ceasefire and move into exile in Iran." .

ns1:57089 a ns1:context_narration ;
