ns1:57493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "DC murder of Stephen Oake, Queen's Gallantry Medal, was a police officer serving as an anti-terrorism detective with Greater Manchester Police in the United Kingdom who was murdered while attempting to arrest a suspected terrorist in Manchester on 14 January 2003. In the years following his murder, there was debate over whether Oake should be formally recognised for his bravery in Bourgass' arrest, including a call from his chief constable for him to receive the highest civil decoration in the United Kingdom — the George Cross (GC)." .

ns1:57495 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jordan–Mexico relations refers to the diplomatic relations between Jordan and Mexico. Diplomatic relations between Jordan and Mexico were established on 9 July 1975. In 2015, both Jordan and Mexico opened embassies in each other's capitals respectively. In 2015, Jordan and Mexico celebrated 40 years of diplomatic relations. In 2017, Princess Dina Mired of Jordan paid a visit to Mexico to attend the World Summit of Leaders Against Cancer. High-level from Jordan to Mexico. High-level visits from Mexico to Jordan. Both nations have signed several bilateral agreements such as a Memorandum of Understanding between Mexico's Secretariat of Tourism and Jordan's Ministry of Tourism and Antiquities (2014); Agreement of Technical Cooperation (2014); Agreement on Educational and Cultural Cooperation (2014); Memorandum of Understanding for the Establishment of a Mechanism of Consultation in Matters of Mutual Interest (2015); Memorandum of Understanding and Cooperation between both nations Diplomatic Institutions (2015); and a Memorandum of Understanding between the Mexican-Arab Chamber of Commerce and Industry (CAMIC) and the Jordanian Business Association (JBA) (2018). In 2018, trade between Jordan and Mexico totaled US$44 million. Jordan's main exports to Mexico include: natural calcium phosphates, mineral or chemical fertilizers, mechanical appliances, and tailor suits. Mexico's main exports to Jordan include: vehicles for the transport of goods; tubes; antibiotics; nucleic acids and their salts; and passenger cars. Jordan is Mexico's 95th largest trading partner globally." .

ns1:57496 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The first Greenbelt Festival was held on a pig farm just outside the village of Charsfield near Woodbridge, Suffolk over the August 1974 bank holiday weekend, begun by Jim Palosaari, Kenneth Frampton, and James Holloway." .

ns1:57502 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hardee's Pro Classic (formerly known as the Movie Gallery Pro Tennis Classic and the Dothan Pro Tennis Classic) is a tennis tournament held on outdoor clay court at the Westgate Tennis Center in Dothan." .

ns1:57504 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 UEFA Europa League qualifying phase and play-off round of the 2013–14 UEFA Europa League were played from 2 July to 29 August 2013, to decide 31 of the 48 places in the group stage." .

ns1:57505 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The IAU Trail World Championships are annual trail running World Championships, from 2007 up to 2015 was biennial, held for the first time in Huntsville, United States in 2007 and organised by International Association of Ultrarunners." .

ns1:57507 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Super J-Cup (1995) was the second Super J-Cup professional wrestling tournament, it was hosted by Wrestle Association R and produced by WAR wrestler Último Dragón. Super J-Cup (1995) was a very successful event and managed to draw a crowd of 11,500 people at Sumo Hall, similar to the Super J-Cup (1994)'s number." .

