ns1:57532 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Storm Herwart was a European windstorm that affected Southern Denmark, Germany, Poland, Austria, Hungary and the Czech Republic on 28 29 October 2017–29 October 2017. Train connections were closed in Northern Germany, and major bridges in Denmark were closed for traffic. This can lead to a situation where Austria and Switzerland find it attractive to use the energy in their pumped storage reservoirs, where it can later be sold back to Germany. Herwart was not as strong as Xavier which struck Germany earlier in 29 October 2017." .

ns1:57534 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Ottawa municipal election was held on 13 November 2006, in Ottawa, Canada, to elect the mayor of Ottawa, Ottawa City Council and the Ottawa-Carleton Public and Catholic School Boards." .

ns1:57536 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Expo 2008 was an international exposition held from Saturday, 14 June to Sunday, 2008 in Zaragoza , Spain, with the theme of \"Water and Sustainable Development\". Zaragoza, host city for the international exposition, is the administrative and financial capital of the autonomous community of Aragon and Spain's fifth most populous city. Zaragoza was elected the host city of Expo 2008 on 16 December 2004 by the BIE, beating Thessaloniki (Greece) and Trieste (Italy). This themed plaza was designed according to Expo Zaragoza 2008's sustainability criteria: the use of PVC was avoided in electrical wiring, as well as tropical wood, synthetic varnish or solvent-based paints; taps made use of water-saving systems. The Expo 2008 mascot was Fluvi, a little male drop of water. Qatar issued a postage stamp miniature sheet commemorating Expo Zaragoza 2008, which pictured Fluvi." .

ns1:57538 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The speed skating at the 1990 Asian Winter Games – women's 1500 metres at the 1990 Asian Winter Games was held on 11 March 1990 in Sapporo, Japan." .

ns1:57542 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss World Mexico 2016, now referred to as Miss Mexico 2016, is the very first edition of a new pageant organization formed by Hugo Castellanos after Lupita Jones, president of Nuestra Belleza México (now Mexicana Universal), lost the franchise with Miss World. The pageant held at Teatro Morelos of Morelia, Michoacán on 2016 . 31 contestants of the Mexico competed for the national title. Two winners were crowned in the end of the event, Miss World Mexico 2016/Miss Mexico 2016 and Miss World Mexico 2017/Miss Mexico 2017. Ana Girault of Ciudad de México (Mexico City) was crowned as the titleholder for 2016 and Andrea Meza of Chihuahua was crowned as the titleholder for 2017. Ana Girault represented Mexico at Miss World 2016 in the United States." .

ns1:57554 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Barbados–Trinidad and Tobago relations describe relations between the governments of Trinidad and Tobago and Barbados. Barbados maintains non-resident representation to Port of Spain, and the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago maintains non-resident representation to Bridgetown. Barbados and Trinidad and Tobago formally established diplomatic relations on Barbados' national date of independence 30 November 1966. While Barbados was the only island in the West Indies which never witnessed a change in colonial power since the founding settlement there in 1627, both Trinidad and Tobago witnessed a rocky beginning after being sought after in rotation by several colonial powers. Female Barbadian Gospel singer Sherryann Maughn was also born in Trinidad and Tobago and she came to Barbados at eleven (11) years old she's the first Trinidadian-Barbadian singer to come to Barbados and the second female Barbadian singer to arrive in Barbados at eleven (11) years old. Recently relations between Barbados, Trinidad and Tobago have mainly been cordial and cooperative, with an edge of wariness on both sides, due to a contentious decade long maritime boundary dispute. Barbados and the Government of Trinidad and Tobago signed an agreement to construct an undersea 177 mile oil or Liquid Natural Gas (LNG) pipeline which will stretch from Tobago to Barbados. It will see energy delivered directly from Trinidad and Tobago to the domestic Barbadian natural gas network and feeding into the power plants in Barbados. In 2014, Barbados' Ambassador to CARICOM, Robert Morris was accredited as the Barbados' official High Commissioner to the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago." .

ns1:57556 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The inaugural Warrior Dash took place on 18 July 2009, in Joliet, Illinois, at CPX Sports with 2,000 participants." .

