ns1:57664 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The diving at the 2015 Pan American Games – men's 3 metre springboard competition of the diving diving at the 2015 Pan American Games at the 2015 Pan American Games was held between the 10 and 11 of July at the CIBC Pan Am/Parapan Am Aquatics Centre and Field House in Toronto, Canada." .

ns1:57665 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Idomene was a battle in the Peloponnesian War in 426 BC, between the Athens and the Ambracia. Unbeknownst to the Ambracia, the first army had been defeated, surrounded and scattered by the allied Athens, Amphilochians and Acarnanians the day before. Before dawn, while the Ambracia were still asleep, they were attacked and destroyed by the Athens." .

ns1:57670 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's 50 kilometre freestyle cross-country skiing competition at the cross-country skiing at the 1998 Winter Olympics – men's 50 kilometre freestyle in Nagano, Japan, was held on 22 February at Snow Harp." .

ns1:57671 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Great Britain competed at the Great Britain at the 2018 Winter Olympics in Pyeongchang County, South Korea, from 9 to 2018, with 58 competitors in 11 sports. On 2018, the funding body UK Sport announced their medal targets for Team GB at the 2018 Winter Olympic Games in Pyeongchang County with the target to win at least five medals which if achieved would be a record-breaking haul for a Winter Olympic Games. In the Winter Olympic Cycle running from 2014 to 2018 the UK government body UK Sport allocated a record budget of over £28 million to fund Team GB for the individual athletes as well as the bobsleigh and curling teams for the Great Britain at the 2018 Winter Olympics in Pyeongchang County. On 2018, the British Olympic Association announced the selection of the athletes who will compete for Team GB in the luge in Pyeongchang County." .

ns1:57680 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Super 12 season was the third season of the Super Rugby, contested by teams from Australia, New Zealand and South Africa. The winner of each semi final qualified for the final, which was contested by the Auckland Blues and the Canterbury Crusaders at Eden Park, Auckland. The Canterbury Crusaders won 20 – 13 to win their first Super Rugby title. The 1998 Super Rugby competition consisted of 12 teams, they were: The Blues (New Zealand) The Brumbies (Australia) The Bulls (South Africa) The Cats (South Africa) The Chiefs (New Zealand) The Crusaders (New Zealand) The Highlanders (New Zealand) The Hurricanes (New Zealand) The Reds (Australia) The Sharks (South Africa) The Stormers (South Africa) The Waratahs (Australia)" .

ns1:57684 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 British National Track Championships were a series of track cycling competitions held from 2013-2013, at the Manchester Velodrome." .

ns1:57685 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1921 Michigan Wolverines football team represented the University of Michigan in the 1921 Big Ten Conference football season. Yost's assistant coaches for 1921 included Angus Goetz and Tad Wieman, both of whom had played at the tackle position on Yost's 1920 Michigan Wolverines football team." .

ns1:57689 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "G1 Special in San Francisco was a professional wrestling event promoted by New Japan Pro-Wrestling (NJPW). While tickets for the G1 Special in USA sold out in two hours, Pro Wrestling Torch reported that NJPW management was upset with the initial ticket sales for G1 Special in San Francisco. G1 Special in San Francisco featured professional wrestling matches that involved wrestlers from pre-existing scripted feuds, plots, and storylines that played out on NJPW shows." .

ns1:57693 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1974 Nebraska gubernatorial election was held on 1974, and featured incumbent Governor James Exon, a Democrat, defeating Republican nominee, state Senator Richard D. Marvel. This was the first gubernatorial election in Nebraska in which the nominees for Governor and Lieutenant Governor ran as a single ticket, though were chosen in separate primary elections." .

