ns1:57698 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1984 Barneveld, Wisconsin tornado outbreak is a significant severe weather and tornado event that took place across the central United States of America from North Dakota to Kansas on June 7–8, 1984. It was the first F5 in the US since 2 April 1982 when one touched down near Broken Bow, Oklahoma; the next one occurred on 31 May 1985 in Wheatland, Pennsylvania, during the 1985 United States of America-Canadian tornado outbreak." .

