ns1:57813 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1980 African Cup of Champions Clubs was the 16th edition of the annual international club football competition held in the Confederation of African Football region (Africa), the CAF Champions League. Canon Yaoundé from Cameroon won that final, and became for the third time Confederation of African Football club champion." .

ns1:57814 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009–10 Superleague Greece was the 74th season of the highest association football league of Greece and the fourth under the name Super League. On 11 April 2010, Panathinaikos F.C. defeated Iraklis 2–0 to secure their 20th Greek title and their first one in six years. Teams promoted from 2008–09 Superleague Greece Beta Ethniki: Teams relegated to 2009–10 Beta Ethniki: Due to Greece having ascended in the UEFA league coefficient rankings, the 2009–10 champions will enter 2010–11 UEFA Champions League at the group stage instead of the third qualifying round." .

ns1:57815 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Revolution of the Park (Revolución del Parque), also known as the Revolution of '90, was an uprising against the national government of Argentina that took place on 26 July 1890, and started with the takeover of the Buenos Aires Artillery Park. The uprising started on 26 July 1890 at the Buenos Aires Artillery Park." .

ns1:57817 a ns1:context_narration ;
