ns1:57923 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kivinebb was fought on 11 March 1555, between forces of Sweden commanded by Jöns Månsson Ulfsparre on one side, and on the other side a Russia squad led by Ivan Grigoryevich Bibikov and consisting mostly of militiamen from Zemshchina. The battle is briefly mentioned in the Lebedev Chronicle, which says that in 1555 Ivan Bibikov with a number of common men was sent to push Swedes to exchange some Russia citizens who were forcibly held in Sweden and to punish the Swedes for attacking the nearest Russia settlements, but was defeated." .

