ns1:57995 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Volta-Bani War was an anti-colonial rebellion which took place in French West Africa (specifically, the areas of modern Burkina Faso and Mali) between 1915 and 1917. It was the main reason for the creation of the colony of French Upper Volta (now Burkina Faso) after World War I, by splitting off seven districts from the large colony of Haut-Sénégal and Niger." .

ns1:57999 a ns1:context_narration ;
