ns1:58011 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Arizona gubernatorial election took place on 05 November 2002. The Democratic nominee, Arizona Attorney General Janet Napolitano, narrowly defeated Republican Matt Salmon, a former U.S. Representative. The election was extremely close: Napolitano won by just 11,819 votes out of 1,226,111 cast, the closest gubernatorial election in Arizona in many years." .

ns1:58012 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1924 United States presidential election in New York took place on 04 November 1924. New York was won by incumbent Republican President Calvin Coolidge of Massachusetts, who was running against Democratic Ambassador John W. Davis of West Virginia and the Progressive Party's Senator Robert M. La Follette of Wisconsin. The economic boom and social good feelings of the Roaring Twenties under popular Republican leadership virtually guaranteed Calvin Coolidge an easy win in the state against the conservative Southern Democrat John Davis, who had little appeal in Northern states like New York where his reticence on the Ku Klux Klan was opposed by large Catholic populations. No Republican since has been able to outperform Coolidge’s county-level performance or surpass his statewide margin of victory; the only stronger Republican win in New York’s history was when Coolidge was running for Vice President four years earlier in Warren G. Harding’s massive landslide of 1920 United States presidential election in New York. 1924 also made Calvin Coolidge one of only three presidential candidates of either party who has been able to sweep every county in New York State, the others being Republican Warren G. Harding in 1920 United States presidential election in New York and Democrat Lyndon Johnson in 1964." .

ns1:58015 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A 1954 Romanian blizzard hit Romania (along with westernmost regions of Moldova) in 01 February 1954." .

ns1:58019 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 Paisley South by-election was a parliamentary by-election held on 29 November 1990 for the British House of Commons constituency of Paisley South, in the town of Paisley, Scotland." .

ns1:58027 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Zhengzhou Women's Tennis Open was a professional tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the fifth edition of the tournament and part of the 2018 WTA 125K series, offering a total of $125,000 in prize money. It took place in Zhengzhou, China, on 16 April 2018–22 April 2018." .

ns1:58028 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Euro Beach Soccer Cup (EBSC), originally known as the European Pro Beach Soccer Championships until 2004, is a biennial (previously annual) beach soccer competition contested between European men's national teams, organised by Beach Soccer Worldwide (BSWW). Having started in 1998, the tournament's prestige is held in being one of the very oldest and longest running beach soccer competitions in Europe and the world. These are the nations who have appeared in the Euro Beach Soccer Cup since 1998." .

ns1:58051 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1999 L.League Cup Final was the fourth final of the L. League Cup competition. The final was played at Nihondaira Sports Stadium in Shizuoka on 1999. Nippon TV Beleza won their second title, by defeating defending champion Iga FC Kunoichi, 1–0." .

ns1:58053 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1930 World Ice Hockey Championships were held between January 30 and 10 February 1930, in Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, France, Vienna, Austria, and Berlin, Germany. The lone game in Vienna was played to determine the European Bronze, Austria shutout Poland two to zero to round out the medals. Warm winter weather melted the ice in Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, France and forced the International Ice Hockey Federation officials to move the tournament to Berlin, Germany, and the Sportpalast (which had artificial ice). Additionally, the fourth place match was played in Vienna, Austria, making this the only world hockey championship tournament to take place in three different countries. The Canadian team lost to Austria 1-0 on February 7 (in Vienna) in an exhibition match." .

ns1:58062 a ns1:context_narration ;
