ns1:58241 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Poland participated in the Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009, as confirmed by Polish broadcaster Telewizja Polska (TVP). TVP continued to use the Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest contest to select the Polish representative for the 2009 contest in Moscow. The winner was Lidia Kopania with \"I Don't Wanna Leave\", represented Poland at the Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009 in 2009. After coming 24th (second last) in the 2008 contest, talks within TVP suggested that Poland may withdraw from the 2009 contest. After the EBU revealed a new voting system for the final of the 2009 contest, introducing a mixture of televoting and jury voting, TVP officially confirmed their participation in Moscow, with the Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest contest to select the Polish representative for the 2009 contest. Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009 was the national final organised by TVP in order to select the Polish entry for the Poland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2009. The show took place on 2009 at the TVP Headquarters in Warsaw, hosted by Radosław Brzózka and Paulina Chylewska. Poland had competed in the second semi-final of the 2009 Contest, held on 2009,performed 5th, after Serbia and before Norway she ended 12th with 43 points failing to qualify to the Grand Final." .

