ns1:58409 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 FA Charity Shield (also known as the General Motors FA FA Community Shield for sponsorship reasons) was the 65th FA Community Shield, a association football match contested by the holders of the Football League First Division and FA Cup. This edition was contested between Everton F.C. and Coventry City F.C. at Wembley Stadium on Saturday 01 August 1987. Everton F.C. had won the 1986–87 Football League and Coventry had won the 1987 FA Cup Final to qualify for the season opener for the first time. This was Everton F.C.'s fourth successive appearance in the FA Community Shield." .

