ns1:58538 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 6th G7 summit was held at Venice between 22 June 1980 and 23rd, 1980. The Group of Seven (G7) was an unofficial forum which brought together the heads of the richest industrialized countries: France, West Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom, the United States of America, Canada (since 1976) and the President of the European Commission (starting officially in 1981). The summits were not meant to be linked formally with wider international institutions; and in fact, a mild rebellion against the stiff formality of other international meetings was a part of the genesis of cooperation between France's President Giscard d'Estaing and West Germany's Chancellor Helmut Schmidt as they conceived the first Group of Six (G6) summit in 1975. The G7 is an unofficial annual forum for the leaders of Canada, the European Commission, France, West Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom and the United States of America." .

ns1:58551 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "It consisted of 19 stages covering a total of 3,593 km, and was won by Éric Caritoux of the Sem cycling team." .

