ns1:58564 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Mughal-Rajput Wars were a series of battles fought between the Rajput Confederacy and the Mughal Empire which started with the Timurid ruler Babur's invasion of northwestern India and the head of the Rajput confederacy Rana Sanga's resistance to it. In 1525, after the conquest of Transoxania, Babur invaded the Punjab several times." .

