ns1:58941 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "America's Newsroom is an American television hard news program on Fox News currently hosted by Sandra Smith and a rotating co-anchor (most often, Trace Gallagher in Los Angeles) live from 9 a.m. - noon on Monday through Friday. The show has been a part of the Fox News program lineup since 12 February 2007, and is the number one cable news broadcast in its time slot. On March 23, 2009, America's Newsroom began broadcasting in high definition and moved to Studio J, the Election Night 2008 set used by the Fox News. America's Newsroom is broadcast from Studio J at 1211 Avenue of the Americas (also known as the News Corp. Building), New York City." .

ns1:58950 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 UTEP Lady Miners basketball team represents the University of Texas at El Paso during the 2014–15 NCAA Division I women's basketball season. 2014–15 UTEP Miners basketball team." .

ns1:58953 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gambia–Russia relations (Russian: Российско-гамбийские отношения) are the bilateral relationship between the two countries, The Gambia and Russia. Russia has no corresponding embassy in Banjul, but the Russian embassy in Dakar in neighboring Senegal also represents Russian interests in The Gambia. The Gambia and Russia have signed a cooperative military agreement for training and a visa waiver agreement for diplomats. The Gambia and Russia are also mutual participants in a number of international multilateral treaties and organizations. Since independence, The Gambia has sent students for training Soviet and Russian universities such as the Peoples' Friendship University of Russia." .

ns1:58954 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 ATP Challenger Tour Finals was a tennis tournament played at the Ginásio do Ibirapuera in São Paulo, Brazil, between November 27 and 2012. 50, won 2 Challenger Tour titles in Tunis and San Luis Potosí, finished runner-up in Pereira, and reached the semifinals in Guayaquil twice (both in the 2011 and 2012 editions). 2 during the 2012 season. 2, was also the second Romanian player to qualify for the ATP Challenger Tour Finals, together with Victor Hănescu. In the latter, he won the title in Braunschweig and reached the semifinals at the 2011 ATP Challenger Tour Finals in São Paulo. Thiago Alves won 2 titles in the 2012 ATP Challenger Tour, in São Paulo and Guadalajara." .

