ns1:59297 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The St Magnus Festival is an annual, week-long arts festival which takes place at midsummer on the islands of Orkney Islands, off the north coast of mainland Scotland. The festival was founded in 1977 by a group including the composer Sir Peter Maxwell Davies, who was a resident of Orkney Islands, and the Orcadian poet George Mackay Brown. Orkney Islands Conducting Course, St Magnus Composers' Course, a Writers' Course and, from 2012, a Singers' Course also run alongside the festival." .

