ns1:59723 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Feyenoord season was Feyenoord's 107th season of play, it marked its 59th season in the Eredivisie and its 93rd consecutive season in the top flight of Dutch football. Feyenoord is one of the Big Three football clubs in the Netherlands having played at the highest level of competition uninterrupted since 1921. Feyenoord lost the first leg of the two-legged tie 1–2 at home on 30 July; Te Vrede converted a association football penalty kick for the single Feyenoord goal. Feyenoord opened their league campaign on the road against ADO Den Haag, they won this game 1–0 after a association football goal by Te Vrede. Manu scored two minutes into association football to give Feyenoord the 4–3 game win and 5–4 aggregate score that qualified them for the group stage of the Europa League." .

