    rdfs:label "The Lava Lake murders refers to a triple-murder that occurred near Little Lava Lake in Central Oregon in 1924. The victims were Edward Nickols (aged 50), Roy Wilson (aged 35), and Dewey Morris (aged 25), all of whom were working as fur trappers in the Deschutes National Forest in late 1923–1924. A traffic officer in Portland, Oregon recognized Kimzey as a man who had approached him on 1924, carrying a gunnysack and asking for directions to a fur dealer in the city." .

