    rdfs:label "The 2015 CONCACAF Champions League Finals was the final of the 2014–15 CONCACAF Champions League, the 7th edition of the CONCACAF Champions League under its current format, and overall the 50th edition of the premium association football club competition organized by CONCACAF, the regional governing body of North America, Central America, and the Caribbean. The final was contested in two-legged home-and-away format between Mexican team Club América and Canadian team CF Montréal. The first leg was hosted by Club América at Estadio Azteca in Mexico City on 2015, while the second leg was hosted by CF Montréal at Olympic Stadium in Montreal on 2015. This was the first final of Club América in the CONCACAF Champions League era, but they had won the CONCACAF Champions' Cup title five times (1977, 1987, 1990, 1992, 2006). CF Montréal was the first Canadian team to reach a CONCACAF club final." .

