ns1:63001 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Football West season was the first season under the new competition format in Western Australia. The 2014 National Premier Leagues season was the second season of the new national structure, and the first season with Western Australia participating. The 2014 WA State League Division 1 season, known as the All Flags State League Division 1 for sponsorship reasons, was the second level domestic football competition in Western Australia. The 2014 WA State League Division 2 season, known as the All Flags State League Division 2 for sponsorship reasons, was the third level domestic football competition in Western Australia. Clubs entered from the newly formed Football West State League Premier Division, the two divisions of the State League, as well as a limited number of teams from various divisions of the 2014 Sunday League competition." .

