ns1:63207 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Melbourne International Arts Festival (formerly Melbourne Festival) is a major international arts festival and a celebration of dance, theatre, music, circus, visual arts, multimedia, outdoor and free events held each October in a number of venues across Melbourne, Australia. The festival changed its name from the Spoleto Festival Melbourne to the Melbourne International Festival of the Arts in 1990, became known as Melbourne International Arts Festival from 2003, then was simply referred to as Melbourne Festival before returning to Melbourne International Arts Festival in 2018. Melbourne Festival is one of the most significant festivals in Australia together with the Sydney Festival and the Adelaide Festival of Arts." .

ns1:63209 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996 World Wrestling Championships were held in Sofia, Bulgaria." .

ns1:63212 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Shchastia or Donbas war is an armed conflict in the Donbas region of Ukraine, part of the Ukrainian crisis and the broader Russo-Ukrainian War. 73% of respondents said that the Battle of Shchastia was one of the three most important issues facing Ukraine." .

ns1:63218 a ns1:context_narration ;
