ns1:63239 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Sugar Bowl was the 62nd edition of the post-season American college football Sugar Bowl bowl game. It featured the Virginia Tech Hokies and the Texas Longhorns and was held at the Louisiana Superdome in New Orleans, Louisiana, on 1995. Because the 1995 Sugar Bowl was Virginia Tech's first major bowl game in school history, tickets and travel packages were in high demand. The 1995 Sugar Bowl kicked off at 6:30 p.m. CST on 1995, at the Louisiana Superdome in New Orleans, Louisiana. As the final game of the 1995 college football season for Texas and Virginia Tech, the 1995 Sugar Bowl provided a final opportunity for players to demonstrate their skills on the field prior to the next NFL Draft." .

