ns1:41362 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1924 European Rowing Championships were rowing championships held on Lake Zurich in the Switzerland city of Zürich. The competition was for men only and they competed in six of the seven Olympic boat classes (M1x, M2x, M2-, M2+, M4+, M8+) as they had been rowed earlier in the summer at the 1924 Summer Olympics in Paris; the new Olympic boat class of coxless four (M4-) was not part of the European Rowing Championships that year and would first be introduced in the 1925 European Rowing Championships." .

