ns1:41384 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1973 World Series was the World Series of Major League Baseball's (MLB) 1973 Major League Baseball season. The 70th edition of the World Series, it was a best-of-seven playoff played between the American League (AL) champion (and defending World Series champion) Oakland Athletics and the National League (NL) champion New York Mets. Starting in 1974 World Series, MLB printed an official World Series program that was sold in both stadiums. The 1973 Mets' .509 season winning percentage is the lowest posted by any pennant winner in Major League Baseball history. The final standings: At 82–79, the 1973 New York Mets had the worst record of any team to play in a World Series. In four World Series (1951, 1954, 1962, and 1973), Mays did not hit a single home run. AL Oakland A's (4) vs. NL New York Mets (3) The Mets and A's opened the Series in Oakland with Jon Matlack and Ken Holtzman as the Game 1 starters (Matlack, with a 14–16 record during the 1973 Major League Baseball season, is one of only four pitchers in history to start Game 1 of a World Series after a regular season losing record). Along with blinding sunshine \"turn every fly ball into adventure\" (especially for a 42-year-old Willie Mays), Curt Gowdy described the contest in the official MLB 1973 Fall Classic highlight film as one of the \"longest and weirdest games in World Series history\". Vern Hoscheit, a coach with the A's in 1973, would win a World Series with the Mets as a coach in 1986." .

ns1:41387 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Uncle Tobys Hardcourts was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the ninth edition of the event then known as the Uncle Tobys Hardcourts, and was a WTA Tier III tournaments event on the 2005 WTA Tour. It took place in Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia, from 02 January 2005 through 08 January 2005." .

ns1:41388 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Paso de Cuevas was fought on 12 August 1865 during the Paraguayan invasion of the Argentine province of Corrientes." .

ns1:41423 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Apertura 2015 Copa MX Final was the final of the Apertura 2015 Copa MX, the seventh edition of the Copa MX under its current format and 74th overall organized by the Mexican Football Federation, the governing body of association football in Mexico. The final was contested in a single leg format between Liga MX clubs, Club León and C.D. Guadalajara. Club León has won the tournament five times which makes them tied with América and Puebla for most of all time, while C.D. Guadalajara has won it twice. C.D. Guadalajara last reached a final of the most previous edition of Copa MX, losing 4–2 to Puebla." .

ns1:41455 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Copa San Juan Gobierno was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in San Juan, Argentina between 08 October 2012 and 14 October 2012." .

