    rdfs:label "The 1936 Paris–Nice was the fourth edition of the Paris–Nice cycle race and was held from 17 March 1936 to 22 23 March 1936." .

ns1:41482 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Circuit de la Sarthe (English: Circuit of Sarthe) is an early-season short road bicycle racing stage race held annually in Sarthe, Pays de la Loire, France. Since 2005, it has been organised as a 2.1 event on the UCI Europe Tour." .

ns1:41485 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Winter Campaign of 1941–1942 from 05 December 1941 to 07 May 1942 was the name given by Soviet military command to the period that marked the commencement of the Moscow Strategic Offensive Operation (better known as the Battle of Moscow). The campaign began with the Moscow Strategic Offensive Operation (05 December 1941 – 7 January 1942) with the simultaneous Kerch-Feodosia Amphibious Operation (25 05 December 1941 – 2 January 1942) The operations in central and northern European Russia began with the conclusion of the Moscow counter-offensive almost simultaneously with the Oboyan–Kursk Offensive Operation (3 January 1942 – 26 January 1942), the Lyuban Offensive Operation (7 January 1942 – 30 April 1942), the Demyansk Offensive Operation (7 January 1942 – 20 07 May 1942), the Orel–Bolkhov Offensive Operation (8 January 1942 – 28 April 1942), and the Rzhev-Vyazma Strategic Offensive Operation (8 January 1942 – 20 April 1942)." .

ns1:41534 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1960 Summer Olympics – men's 4 × 100 metres relay event at the 1960 Olympic Games took place between 07 September 1960 and 08 September 1960." .

ns1:41545 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Insert key Insert (often abbreviated Ins) is a key commonly found on computer keyboards. It is primarily used to switch between the two text-entering mode on a personal computer (PC) or word processor: The insert/overtype mode toggling is not global for the computer or even for a single application but rather local to the text input window in which the Insert key was pressed. Modern word processing applications operate in insert mode by default, but can still be switched to overtype mode by pressing the Insert key." .

ns1:41567 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The year 2013 is the 2nd year in the history of the Glory, an international kickboxing event. Road to Glory USA 95 kg Tournament was a kickboxing event held on February 2, 2013 at the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino in Tulsa, Oklahoma, US. Road to Glory USA 85 kg Tournament was a kickboxing event held on February 9, 2013 at the Hollywood Park Casino in Los Angeles, California, US. Road to Glory Japan 65 kg Tournament was a kickboxing event held on March 10, 2013 at the Differ Ariake Arena in Tokyo, Japan. Road to Glory USA 77 kg Tournament was a kickboxing event held on March 22, 2013 at the Capitale in New York City, New York, US. Glory 5: London was a kickboxing event held on March 23, 2013 at the ExCeL Arena in London, England. Glory 6: Istanbul was a kickboxing event held on April 6, 2013 at the Ülker Arena in Istanbul, Turkey. Glory 7: Milan was a kickboxing event held on April 20, 2013 at the Mediolanum Forum in Milan, Italy. Glory 8: Tokyo was a kickboxing event held on May 3, 2013 at the Ariake Coliseum in Tokyo, Japan. Glory 9: New York was a kickboxing event held on June 22, 2013 at the Hammerstein Ballroom in New York City, New York. Glory 10: Los Angeles was a kickboxing event held on September 28, 2013 at the Citizens Business Bank Arena in Ontario, California. Glory 11: Chicago was a kickboxing event held on October 12, 2013 at the Sears Centre at Hoffman Estates, Illinois. Glory 12: New York was a kickboxing event held on November 23, 2013 at The Theater at Madison Square Garden at New York City, New York. Glory 13: Tokyo was a kickboxing event held on December 21, 2013 at the Ariake Coliseum in Tokyo, Japan." .

ns1:41571 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Champ Car season season was the 27th overall and the second season of the Champ Car World Series era of American open-wheel racing. The Bridgestone Presents the Champ Car World Series Powered by Ford Motor Company Drivers' Champion was Sébastien Bourdais, his second consecutive championship. The two companies continued the marketing agreement that branded the series Bridgestone Presents the Champ Car World Series Powered by Ford Motor Company. Similar to the 2003 and 2004 Champ Car season seasons, there were once again many changes for the 2005 season. The initial 2005 schedule announced by Champ Car included 14 races, but only 13 races actually took place during the season. A date at the Ansan circuit was placed on Champ Car's initial 2006 Champ Car season but that race would never take place either." .

ns1:41580 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The British Togoland status referendum, 1956 (French: 1956 plébiscite sur le statut du Togoland britannique) was held in British Togoland on 09 May 1956." .

