ns1:60092 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2011 Thai general election were held in Thailand on 03 July 2011 to elect the 24th House of Representatives. Its leader Yingluck Shinawatra became the first female prime minister in the history of Thailand. On 9 May, Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva announced that he would dissolve the lower house of parliament to hold an election on 03 July 2011. Constituency Preliminary Results Source: Bangkok Post live counting on day of election (links now inactive) After the election was held on 03 July 2011, the next procedure is that the Election Commission acknowledges the election result within thirty days from the election date in order that Abhisit Vejjajaiva, Caretaker Prime Minister, would enact a royal decree convoking the House of Representatives to have the new President of the House, Vice President of the House and Prime Minister selected respectively, and the President of the House would then advice and consent the King to appoint a new Prime Minister according to the resolution of the House." .

ns1:60098 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 European Amateur Boxing Championships were held in Minsk, Belarus from June 1 to 08 June 2013." .

ns1:60099 a ns1:context_narration ;
