ns1:60270 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Men's Sabre Team wheelchair fencing competition at the wheelchair fencing at the 2004 Summer Paralympics – men's sabre team was held on 23 September at the Hellinikon Fencing Hall." .

ns1:60273 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 Stanley Cup Finals was the championship series of the National Hockey League's (NHL) 1980–81 season, and the culmination of the 1981 Stanley Cup playoffs. 1981 New York Islanders." .

ns1:60280 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2016 Kazakhstan Super Cup was a Kazakhstan association football match that was played on 2016 between the champions of 2015 Kazakhstan Premier League, FC Astana, and the winner of the 2015 Kazakhstan Cup, FC Kairat. Main and extra time of the match ended with goalless draw, and FC Kairat won the 2016 Kazakhstan Super Cup by a penalty shootout (5:4)." .

ns1:60288 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Ning-Jin was a military conflict between the Later Jin and Ming dynasty. After several days of successful resistance by Jinzhou, Hong Taiji decided to try his luck at Xingcheng." .

ns1:60308 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Stechford rail crash occurred on 28 February 1967 at Stechford railway station in the area of Stechford in Birmingham, England." .

ns1:60322 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Roses, registered as Doomben Roses, is a Brisbane Racing Club Group 3 Thoroughbred horse race for three-year-old filles, run under Set Weights conditions over a distance of 2000 metres at Doomben Racecourse, Brisbane, Australia during the Queensland Winter Racing Carnival." .

ns1:60334 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1927 Kita Tango earthquake occurred in Kyōto Prefecture on 07 March 1927 with a moment magnitude of 7.0." .

ns1:60342 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Blue Hen Stakes at Delaware Park Racetrack is an American Thoroughbred horse race for two-year-old fillies held annually in early October at Delaware Park Racetrack in Stanton, Delaware." .

ns1:60357 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Greek football scandal emerged on 06 April 2015 when prosecutor Aristidis Korreas' 173-page work was revealed. In 2015, Petros Konstantineas stated that the referees in Greece should be professionals and criticized the situation about Hugh Dallas for getting paid without having any jurisdiction. On 2015, the English sports-site Inside World Football had revealed that UEFA's integrity officer for the HFF (Dimitris Davakis) didn't state to the UEFA's Ethics and Disciplinary Inspector, Miguel Liétard Fernandez-Palacios, the judicial process and the alleged involvement of Asteras Tripoli in the Greek match-fixing scandal of Koriopolis, regarding their participation in the UEFA Europa League." .

ns1:60358 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1931 Paris–Roubaix was the 32nd edition of the Paris–Roubaix, a classic one-day cycle race in France. The single day event was held on 05 April 1931 and stretched 256 km (159 mi) from Paris to its end in a velodrome in Roubaix." .

ns1:60367 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Yasukuni Maru (靖国丸) was a Japan ocean liner owned by Nippon Yusen Kaisha (NYK). The ship was launched in 1930 by Mitsubishi Heavy Industries at Nagasaki, on the southern island of Kyūshū, Japan, entering service in 1930. On 5 April 1934, Yasukuni Maru responded to a distress call from the Imperial Japanese Navy training cruiser Asama at Port Said, Egypt, and took off several ill sailors including an appendicitis patient. Yasukuni Maru carried the Japan Olympic team back from Germany after the 1936 Berlin Olympics. On 16 November 1937, Yasukuni Maru became the first ship on the Europe-Japan route to be equipped with a two-way ship-to-shore wireless telephone for passengers to make telephone calls. In September – October 1939, at the request of the Foreign Ministry, Yasukuni Maru evacuated 240 Japan civilians, members of the diplomatic staff and some German nationals from Germany on the verge of World War II. She returned to Yokohama on 18 October and was requisitioned by the Imperial Japanese Navy on 25 October to 11 December for use as an auxiliary transport, and was briefly used to transport troops and war materials from Japan to China during the Second Sino-Japan War. On 29 October 1940, Yasukuni Maru was again requisitioned by the Imperial Japanese Navy, and was classified this time as an auxiliary submarine tender. Kwajalein was attacked on 1 February 1942 by aircraft from United States Navy Task Force 8 (USS Enterprise (CV-6)), with Yasukuni Maru hit by one bomb in her aft turret and damage to her stern. In early 1943, Yasukuni Maru was assigned to “Operation C”, the reinforcement of the Japan landing on New Guinea." .

ns1:60372 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The de jure Bulgarian Declaration of Independence (Bulgarian: Независимост на България, Nezavisimost na Balgaria) from the Ottoman Empire was declaration of independence on 5 October  1908 in the old capital of Tarnovo by Prince Ferdinand of Bulgaria, who afterwards took the title \"Tsar\". In 22 September 1908 at a meeting in Buchlov (German: Buchlau, contemporary Czech Republic), envoys of Austria-Hungary and Russia supported each other's plans and agreed not to hinder Bulgaria's proclamation of independence which was likely to take place. The Bulgarian Declaration of Independence was formally declaration of independence at the Holy Forty Martyrs Church in Tarnovo. Bulgaria's declaration of independence was followed by Austria-Hungary's annexation of Bosnia the following day and Greece's union with the Cretan State (unrecognized until 1913). Bulgaria's Independence Day is subsequently celebrated annually on 22 September 1908." .

ns1:60410 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Arlington Hotel Open was a PGA Tour event that was played from 1955 to 1963 at the Arlington golf course of the Hot Springs Country Club near the Arlington Hotel, now known as the Arlington Resort Hotel and Spa, a 484-room resort in the Ouachita Mountains of Hot Springs National Park in Arkansas." .

ns1:60418 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Universe Slovenia 2009, the 9th Miss Universe Slovenia pageant held at Exhibition and Convention Centre, Ljubljana in Ljubljana, Slovenia on 2009. The winner will be the representative for Slovenia at the Miss Universe 2009 pageant in Nassau, Bahamas. In the final round, Mirela Korač, was crowned Miss Universe Slovenia 2009 by Anamrija Avbelj, Miss Universe Slovenia 2008." .

ns1:60439 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Topshelf Open was a tennis tournament played on outdoor grass courts. It was the 24th edition of the Rosmalen Grass Court Championships, and was part of the 250 Series of the 2013 ATP World Tour, and of the WTA International tournaments of the 2013 WTA Tour. Both the men's and the women's events took place at the Autotron park in Rosmalen, 's-Hertogenbosch, Netherlands, from June 16 through 2013." .

ns1:60441 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Greatest Hits Tour (also known as The Farewell Tour) was the twelfth concert tour by Irish boy band, Westlife." .

ns1:60445 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 TCU Horned Frogs baseball team represented Texas Christian University during the 2016 NCAA Division I baseball season. The 2015 TCU Horned Frogs baseball team notched a 51–15 (18–5) regular season record and were the regular season Big 12 Conference champions. On 2016, TCU Head Coach Jim Schlossnagle became the winningest coach in TCU baseball history with his 518th win; Schlossngale passed former TCU letterman and head coach Lance Brown to become the Frogs' all-time winningest coach. In time for the start of the 2016 regular season, TCU debuted the latest in its baseball facilities additions with the opening of the new $8 million left field line complex at Lupton Stadium, which houses the TCU home locker room, team classroom, team lounge, sports medicine center, equipment room, and coaches' offices (photo gallery). The Frogs won their opening series against Loyola Marymount two games to one, and Jim Schlossnagle became the all-time winningest coach in TCU baseball history in the series finale on 2016." .

ns1:60447 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010–11 Georgian Cup (also known as the David Kipiani Cup) was the sixty-seventh season overall and twenty-first since independence of the Georgian annual association football tournament. The defending champions were WIT Georgia, who won their first Georgian Cup 2009–10 Georgian Cup." .

ns1:60449 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kudal-Sangamam was fought in 1062 by the forces of the Chola king Rajendra Chola II and the Western Chalukya king Someshvara I at Kudalasangama, where the Krishna and the Tungabhadra meet." .

ns1:60458 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 CAF Champions League Final was the final of the 2015 CAF Champions League, the 51st edition of Africa's premier club association football tournament organized by the Confederation of African Football (CAF), and the 19th edition under the current CAF Champions League format. The final was contested in two-legged home-and-away format between USM Alger of Algeria and TP Mazembe of Democratic Republic of the Congo. The first leg was hosted by USM Alger at the Omar Hamadi Stadium in Algiers on 2015, while the second leg was hosted by TP Mazembe at the Stade TP Mazembe in Lubumbashi on 2015. TP Mazembe won the competition for the fifth time in its history and first time since 2010, defeating USM Alger of Algeria 4–1 on aggregate. It is currently used mostly for association football matches and is the home ground of USM Alger. Since its completion in 2011, it has mostly been used for association football matches and is the home venue of TP Mazembe and CS Don Bosco." .

ns1:60465 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1851 was unanimously adopted on 16 December 2008. Acting under Chapter VII through the unanimous adoption of United States-led resolution 1851 (2008), the Council called on those States and organizations able to do so to actively participate in defeating piracy and armed robbery off Somalia's coast by deploying naval vessels and military aircraft, and through seizure and disposition of boats and arms used in the commission of those crimes, following on a 9 16 December 2008 letter from the Transitional Federal Government for international assistance to counter the surge in piracy and armed robbery there." .

ns1:60466 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1879–80 Scottish Cup – officially the Scottish Football Association Challenge Cup – was the seventh season of Scotland's most prestigious association football knockout competition. The third round began on 1879 with a clutch of ties, included amongst them; Dumbarton's 5–0 win over Renton, Queen's Park F.C.'s 5–1 triumph against Partick, Thornliebank's 1–0 defeat of Barrhead Rangers and Parkgrove's first match in the competition after they benefitted from a walkover and a bye in the previous rounds, a 6–2 defeat of Alexandra Athletic. On 1879, three teams recorded double-figures scorelines; Dumbarton won 11–0 at home to Clyde, Queen's Park F.C. defeated Strathblane 10–1 at Hampden Park and Thornliebank won 12–0 at home to Possilpark. Thomas Highet – who scored three goals in the 1876 final and replay, the last time Queen's Park F.C. won the competition – scored twice against Thornliebank to help Queen's Park F.C. to a 3–0 win and a fourth title, maintaining their 100 per cent record in Scottish Cup finals." .

ns1:60469 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 FIVB Men's World Cup was played from 19 to 28 November 1981 in Japan. As in 1981, it was the Soviet Union men's national volleyball team defended the third title." .

ns1:60482 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Algerian Cup Final was the 35th final of the Algerian Cup. The final took place on 01 July 1999, at Stade 5 Juillet 1962 in Algiers with kick-off at 15:00. USM Alger beat JS Kabylie 2-0 to win their fourth Algerian Cup. Algerian Ligue Professionnelle 1 clubs JS Kabylie and USM Alger was the teams that contested the final, in what was the 44th edition of the Kabylo-Algiers Derby." .

ns1:60493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Aceh earthquake (Indonesian: Gempa Aceh 2016) struck the Indonesian island of Sumatra with a Mw of 6.5 in Aceh province on 07 December 2016, at 05:03 WIB (22:03 UTC 6 07 December 2016). It was the deadliest earthquake in Aceh since the 2005 Nias–Simeulue earthquake and the deadliest in Sumatra since the 2010 Mentawai earthquake and tsunami. The Head of the Geology Office, Ego Syahrial, stated that Pidie Jaya Regency was included as one of the most earthquake-prone cities in Aceh and was in the red zone. In the initial hours after the earthquake, structures across Aceh were reported to have been severely damaged. At least 108 aftershocks followed the main shock in Aceh, with the largest measuring 5.3 Mw occurring in the mid-morning hours of 11 07 December 2016 at a depth of 20 km. The Japanese Government had also offered its condolence to Indonesia in response to the quake and stated that Japan is ready to help Aceh, according to the statement released by Japanese Foreign Minister Fumio Kishida. Before the start of the semifinal match of the 2016 AFF Suzuki Cup Championship between Indonesia and Vietnam on 07 December 2016, a minute of silence was observed. On 8 07 December 2016, Interior Minister Tjahjo Kumolo visited Aceh to observe the damage. Consequently, 4 airlines, which were Indonesia AirAsia, Lion Air, Tri-MG Intra Asia Airlines, and Sriwijaya Air offered free logistics distribution to Aceh. On 14 07 December 2016, Spokesman of the Chinese Foreign Ministry Geng Shuang confirmed that the Chinese Government will send funds of $1.000.000 to Indonesia. On 15 07 December 2016, President Joko Widodo revisited Aceh immediately after his visit in Iran." .

ns1:60505 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sherman's March to the Sea (also known as the Savannah Campaign or simply Sherman's March) was a military campaign of the American Civil War conducted through Georgia from 15 November 1864 until 21 December 1864, by Maj. Gen. William Tecumseh Sherman of the Union Army. The campaign began with Sherman's troops leaving the captured city of Atlanta on 15 November 1864 and ended with the capture of the port of Savannah on 21 December 1864. For the Savannah Campaign, Sherman's remaining force of 62,000 men (55,000 infantry, 5,000 cavalry, and 2,000 artillerymen manning 64 guns) was divided into two columns for the march: The Confederate opposition from Lt. Gen. William J. Hardee's Department of South Carolina, Georgia, and Florida was meager. Gen. Charles C. Walcutt arrived to stabilize the defense, and the division of Georgia militia launched several hours of badly coordinated attacks, eventually retreating with about 1,100 casualties (of which about 600 were prisoners), versus the Union's 100. On November 23, Slocum's troops captured the city and held a mock legislative session in the capitol building, jokingly voting Georgia back into the Union. Smith's 1,500 Georgia militiamen, 3 miles (4.8 km) south of Grahamville Station, South Carolina. Union soldiers sang many songs during the March, but it is one written afterward that has come to symbolize the campaign: \"Marching Through Georgia\", written by Henry Clay Work in 1865." .

ns1:60521 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Wellington Sevens was an rugby sevens tournament that took place at the Wellington Regional Stadium in Wellington between the 2000–2000." .

ns1:60522 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2000 Surinamese general election were held in Suriname on 25 May 2000." .

ns1:60543 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 GT4 European Series was the ninth season of the GT4 European Cup, a sports car championship created and organised by the SRO Motorsports Group (SRO)." .

ns1:60562 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1982 Seiko Super Tennis, also known as the 1982 Tokyo Indoor was a men's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet court at the Yoyogi National Stadium in Tokyo, Japan that was part of the 1982 Volvo Grand Prix circuit. It was the fifth edition of the tournament and was held from 25 October 1982 through 29 October 1982." .

ns1:60585 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Stampede 3 was a U.S. military operation conducted in Baghdad, Iraq, in 06 July 2007 to try to correct the security situation." .

ns1:60613 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1986 Texas gubernatorial election was held on 04 November 1986, to elect the Governor of Texas." .

ns1:60620 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Soul Train Music Awards was held at the Orleans Arena in Las Vegas, Nevada, on 06 November 2016. It was later aired on Centric and BET on 2016." .

ns1:60633 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Antonio Savoldi–Marco Cò – Trofeo Dimmidisì was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Manerbio, Italy between 22 August 2016 and 28 August 2016." .

ns1:60635 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Texas International Pop Festival was a music festival held at Lewisville, Texas, on Labor Day weekend, August 30 to September 1, 1969. On January 29, 2010, the Texas Historical Commission approved the placement of a state historical marker near Hebron Station, a Denton County Transportation Authority train station in eastern Lewisville, close to the former site of the festival stage." .

ns1:60637 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dream 9 was a mixed martial arts event promoted by Fighting and Entertainment Group's mixed martial arts promotion Dream on 26 May 2009." .

ns1:60656 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Stockholm Open was an ATP men's tennis tournament played on hard courts, and held in Stockholm, Sweden. The tournament was held from 20 November 2000 through 26 November 2000." .

ns1:60662 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Paris-Tours is the 103rd edition of this single day road bicycle racing event and is organized by the Amaury Sport Organisation (ASO), which also runs the Tour de France. The 230 km event took place on October 11, 2009 and was won by Philippe Gilbert, the Belgian rider for Silence–Lotto in 5 hours, 12 minutes, 23 seconds. Gilbert, along with countryman Tom Boonen (Quick Step) and Slovenia's Borut Božič (Vacansoleil), escaped with 7 km to go at the base of the Côte de l'Epan behind an attack from Gilbert's teammate Greg Van Avermaet." .

ns1:60668 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 3rd Golden Melody Awards ceremony (Chinese: 第三屆金曲獎) was held at the Sun Yat-sen Memorial Hall in Taipei on 09 November 1991." .

ns1:60679 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Cokeville Elementary School hostage crisis occurred on Friday, 16 May 1986, in Cokeville, United States of America, when former town marshal David Young, 43, and his wife Doris Young, 47, took 136 children and 18 adults hostage at Cokeville Elementary School. David and Doris both returned to Cokeville on 16 May 1986." .

ns1:60690 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1960 U-2 incident occurred on 01 May 1960, when an American U-2 spy plane was shot down by the Soviet Union Air Defence Forces while performing photographic aerial reconnaissance deep inside Soviet Union territory. The weather improved and on 01 May 1960, 15 days before the scheduled opening of the east–west summit conference in Paris, Captain Powers, flying Article 360, 56–6693 left the base in Peshawar on a mission with the operations code word GRAND SLAM to overfly the Soviet Union, photographing targets including the ICBM sites at the Baikonur Cosmodrome and Plesetsk Cosmodrome, then land at Bodø in Norway. Cannon said, Mr. Chairman, on 01 May 1960 the Soviet Union Government captured, 1300 miles inside the boundaries of the Russian Empire, an American plane, operated by an American pilot, under the direction and control of the U.S. Central Intelligence Agency, and is now holding both the plane and the pilot. Upon his capture, Francis Gary Powers told his Soviet Union captors what his mission had been and why he had been in Soviet Union airspace." .

ns1:60692 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 San Luis Potosí Challenger was a professional tennis tournament played on outdoor red clay courts. It took place in San Luis Potosí, Mexico between 06 April 2009 and 2009." .

ns1:60695 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 U.S. Women's Open Golf Championship was the 50th United States Women's Open Championship, held July 13–16 at the East Course of Broadmoor Golf Club in Colorado Springs. The 1995 edition was the first million dollar purse at the United States Women's Open Championship, double that of 1990." .

ns1:60715 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "This Battle of Santa Cruz was a battle fought in the early stages of the Philippine–American War during General Henry W. Lawton's Laguna de Bay Campaign. At 10:30 a.m. on 09 April 1899, landing craft began offloading Lawton's troops south of the stronghold of Santa Cruz. Ashore in the afternoon of 09 April 1899, the troops set out for Santa Cruz in a long skirmish line, advancing through driving rain." .

ns1:60723 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1969–70 Michigan State Spartans men's basketball team represented Michigan State University in the 1969–70 NCAA Division I men's basketball season as members of the Big Ten Conference. They played their home games at Jenison Fieldhouse in East Lansing, Michigan and were coached by Gus Ganakas in his first year as head coach of the 1968–69 Michigan State Spartans men's basketball team. Prior to the season, on September 10, 1969, the 1968–69 Michigan State Spartans men's basketball team head coach, John E. Benington suffered a heart attack and died after jogging at Jenison Fieldhouse at the age of 47." .

ns1:60728 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 3rd Magritte Awards ceremony, presented by the Académie André Delvaux, honored the best films of 2012 in Belgium and took place on 2013, at the Square – Brussels Meeting Centre in the historic site of Mont des Arts, Brussels beginning at 8:00 p.m. CET. The nominees for the 3rd Magritte Awards were announced on 2013." .

ns1:60740 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Canoe Sprint European Championships is an international canoeing and kayaking event organized by the European Canoe Association (ECA)." .

ns1:60743 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 China Open Super Series is the twelfth tournament of the 2008 BWF Super Series in badminton. It was held in Shanghai, China from 18 November 2008 to 23 November 2008." .

ns1:60751 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Hurricane Fefa was a major Northeast Pacific tropical cyclone of the 1991 Pacific hurricane season that despite causing minimal effects its name was removed from the list of tropical cyclone names." .

ns1:60765 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Thailand World 2018 was the 28th edition of the Miss Thailand World auditioned on July 21-2018. The crowned winner was Nicolene Pichapa Limsnukan of Bangkok represented Thailand at Miss World 2018 competition in Sanya, China on 2018." .

ns1:60776 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "BlizzCon is an annual gaming convention held by Blizzard Entertainment to promote its major franchises including Warcraft, StarCraft, Diablo, Hearthstone, Heroes of the Storm, and Overwatch. The first BlizzCon was held in 2005, and since then, all of the conventions have been held at the Anaheim Convention Center in Anaheim, in the same metropolitan area as Blizzard's headquarters in Irvine. The convention features game-related announcements, previews of upcoming Blizzard Entertainment games and content, Q&A sessions and panels, costume contests, and playable versions of various Blizzard games. Tickets for the BlizzCon events in 2005, 2007 and 2008 were US$100 for admission to both days of activities. The Virtual Ticket provided four live feeds from the convention floor, offering 50+ hours of HD BlizzCon programming. The GOMTV Global Starcraft II League October final match took place in Anaheim alongside BlizzCon. In September 2016, Blizzard Entertainment released a sneak peek at the BlizzCon 2016 in-game item rewards and offered for the first time the \"goody bag\", normally only for physical attendees, was offered for sale to virtual ticket holders. On March 14, Blizzard Entertainment announced that BlizzCon 2017 was held on November 3 and 4, with tickets being available to purchase on April 5 and 8 using the ticketing service Universe; an unprecedented third round happened on July 5 due to the convention center adding a new hall. Blizzard Entertainment announced that BlizzCon 2018 would be held on November 2 and 3 at the Anaheim Convention Center, with tickets being available to purchase from Universe.com on May 9 and 12. Blizzard Entertainment announced that BlizzCon 2019 would be held on November 1 and 2 at the Anaheim Convention Center, with tickets being available to purchase from AXS.com on May 4 and 8." .

ns1:60783 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Ora, known in the Philippines as Typhoon Konsing, was a 22 June 1972 Category 1 typhoon that left 131 people dead and $15 million (1972 USD, $68.4 million 2005 USD) in damage." .

ns1:60788 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's coxless pair competition at the 2017 World Rowing Championships – men's coxless pair in Sarasota took place in Nathan Benderson Park." .

ns1:60789 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Transbrasil Flight 801 (TR801/TBA801) was a scheduled cargo flight from Eduardo Gomes International Airport to São Paulo-Guarulhos International Airport that crashed on 21 March 1989." .

ns1:60803 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 FIBA Europe Under-18 Championship was the 28th edition of the FIBA Europe Under-18 Championship. 16 teams featured the competition, held in Poland from 21 July 2011–31." .

ns1:60825 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 World Single Distance Speed Skating Championships – women's 1000 metres race of the 2016 World Single Distance Speed Skating Championships was held on 12 February 2016." .

ns1:60837 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Music as a Weapon is a series of concert tours created by the American metal band Disturbed. The name of the tour is from the lyrics of \"Droppin' Plates\" on Disturbed's first album, The Sickness. This was the first time Music as a Weapon had co-headliners, Disturbed and Korn. Music as a Weapon II was recorded as a live album and DVD, created by Disturbed." .

ns1:60839 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The January 2010 attack in central Kabul was a suicide bombing and gun attack which occurred in central Kabul, Afghanistan for several hours on 18 January 2010." .

ns1:60849 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Nabisco Championship was a women's professional golf tournament, held 22 March 2001–25 at Mission Hills Country Club in Rancho Mirage, California. She won eight times on tour in 2001 and this was the third in a streak of four consecutive; she successfully defended this title the 2002 Kraft Nabisco Championship." .

ns1:60853 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Perast (Serbian: Перашка битка) was a battle for control over Republic of Venice held Perast (modern day Montenegro) fought in 1654 between defending forces of Republic of Venice Republic from Perast accompanied by hajduks and attacking forces of Ottoman Empire from Sanjak of Herzegovina. Republic of Venice forces from Perast were victorious and successfully repelled Ottoman attack in the battle which is in some sources referred to as most glorious victory in their history. On the other hand, Perast had important strategic importance for the Republic of Venice Republic because it protected important Republic of Venice-held city of Kotor. Battle of Perast followed an unsuccessful attempt of Republic of Venice forces to capture Knin in early 1654. Around 1,500 refugees fled eastern Herzegovina in early 1654 and settled Republic of Venice-held territories in Kotor Bay, near Perast. Although they were of Orthodox faith, hajduks were treated well by Republic of Venice authorities in Perast who granted them some land, creating some kind of Military Frontier between Republic of Venice and Ottoman territories in Kotor Bay. The Ottoman forces that attacked Perast were from Sanjak of Herzegovina governed by Čengić, a secret Republic of Venice agent. Republic of Venice forces of 43 men from Perast were under command of Krsto Vickov Visković. Substantial number of hajduks, who migrated from eastern Herzegovina to Perast in the first half of 15 May 1654, participated in defence of Perast. About 30 Republic of Venice warships from Perast were unable to participate in defence of Perast because they were far away, on the open sea, together with their crews. During this battle mother of Perast captain Vicko Mažarević was kidnapped by the Ottomans and taken to Trebinje where she soon died. Eight days after the battle Petar Zrinski, thrilled with the victory, visited Perast for three days and presented a sword of Vukša Stepanović to the town. Another poem (Spjevanje događaja boja peraškoga) about this battle was written by Perast Catholic friar Ivan Krušala." .

ns1:60858 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hill 731 (Greek: Μάχη του υψώματος 731), was a fierce battle fought during World War II in southern Albania, part of the Greco-Italian War. It began in the early morning of 9 24 March 1941, when Fascist Italy launched an assault (Italian Spring Offensive) against Greece, aimed at capturing the critical mountain pass leading into the Kalpaki valley." .

ns1:60865 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1951 Volta a Catalunya was the 31st edition of the Volta a Catalunya cycle race and was held from 13 September 1951 to 23 September 1951." .

ns1:60884 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Pontins Professional was the twenty-fourth edition of the professional invitational snooker tournament which took place in 01 May 1997 in Prestatyn, Wales." .

ns1:60912 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's marathon event at the athletics at the 1928 Summer Olympics – men's marathon took place in Amsterdam, Netherlands on Sunday, 05 August 1928." .

ns1:60914 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1983 Cypriot presidential election were held in Cyprus on 13 February 1983. The result was a victory for Spiros Kyprianou of the Democratic Party (and also supported by AKEL), who received 56.5% of the vote." .

ns1:60918 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2021 Central American Games, the XII edition of the Central American Games, will be hosted in Santa Tecla." .

ns1:60926 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tuska Open Air Metal Festival, commonly shortened to Tuska (Finnish: pain, agony), is a Finnish heavy metal festival taking place annually in Helsinki. The first Tuska took place in 1998 and the festival has since grown larger every year. However, since 2011, Tuska has taken place at the Suvilahti event field in the Kalasatama neighbourhood of the Sörnäinen district." .

ns1:60929 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gerrie Coetzee vs. Michael Dokes, billed as \"The Buckeye Homecoming\", was a professional boxing match that took place on September 23, 1983, at the Coliseum at Richfield in Richfield Township, Ohio, United States of America for Dokes' WBA heavyweight title. The fight came off on September 23, 1983, at Coliseum at Richfield in Richfield Township, Ohio, about halfway between Dokes' hometown of Akron and the much larger city of Cleveland." .

ns1:60936 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Open Seguros Bolívar was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Bogotá, Colombia between 04 November 2013 and 10 November 2013." .

ns1:60941 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Kor Royal Cup was the 80th Kor Royal Cup, an annual association football match contested by the winners of the previous season's Thai Premier League and Thai FA Cup competitions. The match was played at Suphachalasai Stadium, Bangkok, on 2015, and contested by 2014 Thai Premier League champions Buriram United F.C., and BG Pathum United F.C. as the winner of the 2014 Thai FA Cup." .

ns1:60947 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jewish American Heritage Month (JAHM) is an annual recognition and celebration of Jewish American achievements in and contributions to the United States of America during the month of May. In April 2006, President George W. Bush announced that May would be considered Jewish American Heritage Month. According to Library of Congress hosted website, JewishHeritageMonth.gov, May was chosen as the month of Jewish American Heritage Month because of the successful 350th Anniversary Celebration of Jews in America marking the Jewish arrival in New Amsterdam. In addition to signing the proclamation marking May as the annual Jewish American Heritage Month, the White House shared plans for an address by President Obama on May at Adas Israel Congregation, a large Washington, D.C. synagogue." .

ns1:60949 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Louisbourg was a pivotal operation of the Seven Years' War (known in the United States as the French and Indian War) in 1758 that ended the French colonial era in Atlantic Canada and led to the subsequent British campaign to capture Quebec in 1759 and the remainder of French North America the following year. The chief engineer was John Henry Bastide who had been present at the first siege of Louisbourg in 1745 and was chief engineer at Fort St Philip, Minorca, in 1756 when the British had surrendered the fort and island to the French after a long siege." .

ns1:60956 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "dancesport at the dancesport at the 2007 Asian Indoor Games was held in Macau Forum, Macau, China from 27 October to 2007." .

ns1:60962 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Festival da Canção or Festival RTP da Canção is the name given to the national festival, produced and broadcast by Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP) to choose the Portuguese entry for the Eurovision Song Contest." .

ns1:60965 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Samsung Super League was the 2008 edition of the Samsung Super League, the premier international team show jumping competition run by the International Federation for Equestrian Sports and sponsored by Samsung Electronics. The emerging nations to the 2009 Meydan International Federation for Equestrian Sports Nations Cup were Sweden, France and Canada." .

ns1:60973 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1933 Copa del Presidente de la República (President of the Republic's Cup) was the 33rd staging of the Copa del Rey, the Spain association football cup competition. The competition started on 09 April 1933, and concluded on 25 June 1933, with the final, held at the Montjuïc Stadium in Barcelona." .

ns1:60977 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Western Air Express Flight 7, a domestic scheduled passenger flight from Salt Lake City to Burbank, crashed on 12 January 1937 near Newhall, California. The off-course Boeing 247D, en route from Salt Lake City, was on approach to the Union Air Terminal at Burbank in severely lowered visibility due to heavy rain and fog." .

ns1:60979 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Washington Park Handicap is an American Thoroughbred horse race held annually during the first week of September at Arlington Park in Arlington Heights, Illinois." .

ns1:60994 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pikes Peak Marathon is a trail running competition that begins at the base of Pikes Peak, in Manitou Springs, Colorado, and climbs over 7,815 feet (2382 m) to the top of the 14,115 foot (4302 m) peak. On Aug. 10, 1956, Dr. Arne Suominen of Del Ray Beach, Fla., challenged smokers and nonsmokers to race up and down Pikes Peak, a 26-mile (42 km) race, in conjunction with the 150th anniversary of the discovery of America's most famous mountain by Zebulon Montgomery Pike. The Pikes Peak Marathon was the first American marathon to allow female competitors, allowing them from the beginning of the marathon in 1956, although no woman entered until 1958. The Pikes Peak Ascent race has twice incorporated the World Long Distance Mountain Running Challenge competition, first in 2006 then again in 2010." .

ns1:61016 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Thomas & Uber Cup (officially known as the 2018 BWF Thomas & Uber Cup) was the 30th edition of the Thomas Cup and the 27th edition of the Uber Cup, the biennial international badminton championship contested by the men and women's national teams of the member associations of Badminton World Federation (BWF). The tournament was hosted by Bangkok, Thailand. It was the second time that Thailand hosted the Thomas Cup and the first time hosted the Uber Cup tournament and the first time this event was held in Southeast Asia since 2010 in Malaysia. Bangkok was named as the host in March 2017 during BWF Council meeting in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, where BWF also decided the host for 2018 BWF World Championships, 2019 Sudirman Cup and 2019 BWF World Championships. The draw for the tournament was conducted on 2018, at 18:00 ICT, at Arnoma Grand Hotel in Bangkok. For the Thomas Cup draw, the teams were allocated to three pots based on the World Team Rankings of 2018. A similar procedure was applied for Uber Cup draw, where top seed Japan (which were assigned to position A1), the second seed China (which were assigned to position D1), Korea and Thailand were in Pot 1." .

ns1:61021 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Early 2012 European cold wave was a deadly cold wave that started on 27 January 2012, and brought snow and freezing temperatures to much of the European continent." .

ns1:61024 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Treaty of Huế, concluded on 1883 between France and Vietnam, recognised a French protectorate over Annam and Tonkin. The treaty was dictated to the Vietnamese in the wake of the French victory at the Battle of Thuận An (1883) by Jules Harmand, the French civil commissioner-general for Tonkin. Cowed by the French appeal to naked force, the Vietnamese court gave way immediately, and on 1883 Vietnamese plenipotentiaries signed a treaty whose terms were dictated by Harmand. The Harmand treaty was eventually replaced by a new Treaty of Huế, signed on 6 June 1884." .

ns1:61029 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "From 2003 to 2010, it took place annually at Easter in Bingen am Rhein. Breakpoint 2003 proved to be an unmatched success among demosceners who attended. Breakpoint 2005 caused some sad moments to the demoscene when it was announced that the military depot was scheduled for condemnation by the German government, and the next edition was scheduled to be held in the city's gym in the middle of Bingen am Rhein. Breakpoint 2010 was the final Breakpoint event. After a series of viral teaser videos, the invitation to the official follow-up demoparty called Revision was released, and the party took place in Saarbrücken, largely sharing the same organizing crew as Breakpoint." .

ns1:61036 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Exciter Tour was a 2001 concert tour by the English electronic band Depeche Mode in support of the group's tenth studio album, Exciter, which was released in May 2001." .

ns1:61049 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1959 Milan–San Remo was the 50th edition of the Milan – San Remo cycle race and was held on 19 March 1959. The race started in Milan and finished in Sanremo." .

ns1:61061 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1931 Cork Senior Hurling Championship was the 43rd staging of the Cork Senior Hurling Championship since its establishment by the Cork County Board in 1887. The championship began on 1931 and ended on 13 December 1931." .

ns1:61066 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1946 Philippine presidential election were held on 23 April 1946 (pursuant to Commonwealth Act No. Soon after the reconstitution of the Commonwealth government in 1945, Senators Manuel Roxas, Elpidio Quirino and their allies called for an early national election to choose the president and vice president of the Philippines, as well as the members of Congress." .

ns1:61069 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 suicide air raid on Colombo was an unsuccessful kamikaze-style suicide attack launched by the air wing of the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam on 20 February 2009, targeting military locations in and around Colombo, Sri Lanka. However the attacks failed as the Sri Lanka Air Force detected the two explosive packed aircraft and shot them down before they reached their presumed targets, although one crashed into a government building in Colombo. However the LTTE did not use aircraft as offensive weapons until March 2007, when they launched a surprise attack against Colombo using light aircraft to drop a bomb on the main base of the Sri Lanka Air Force." .

ns1:61073 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Condorism (in Portuguese: Condorismo or Condoreirismo) was a Brazilian literary movement that lasted from the mid-1860s until the early 1880s. The name \"Condorism\" comes from the condor, a bird of solitary and high flight, said to be capable of seeing things from a great distance." .

ns1:61090 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1864 United States presidential election in Wisconsin was held on 08 November 1864 as part of the 1864 United States presidential election." .

ns1:61108 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 19th Tony Awards was broadcast on 1965, from The Hotel Astor in New York City on local television station WWOR-TV (Channel 9)." .

ns1:61113 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1951 Svenska Cupen was the eleventh season of the main Sweden association football Cup. The competition was concluded on 22 July 1951 with the 1951 Svenska Cupen Final, held at Råsunda Stadium, Solna in Stockholms län. The 1951 Svenska Cupen Final was played on 22 July 1951 at the Råsunda Stadium." .

ns1:61114 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1933 Open Championship was the 68th The Open Championship, held 5 July–8 July at the Old Course at St Andrews in St Andrews. This was the first playoff at the Open in a dozen years, since 1921, also won by an American at St Andrews; Jock Hutchison (1884–1977) was born in Scotland but became a U.S. citizen the previous year. The Old Course at St Andrews was par 73 in 1933; the #17 Road Hole was a par-5 through the 1946 Open." .

ns1:61124 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Barnaul was a series of conflicts during the Russian Civil War from 13 June 1918–15, 1918, involving different factions in the Siberian region." .

ns1:61126 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battleground was a professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event produced by WWE. It took place on 06 October 2013 at the First Niagara Center in Buffalo, New York. The professional wrestling matches at Battleground featured professional wrestlers performing as characters in scripted events pre-determined by the hosting promotion, WWE." .

ns1:61128 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tropical Storm Wendy, known in the Philippines as Tropical Storm Mameng, was a deadly tropical cyclone that affected China in early 04 September 1999." .

ns1:61143 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Fergana Challenger is a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It takes place in Fergana, Uzbekistan between 18 June 2018–24 June 2018." .

ns1:61171 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Tropicale Amissa Bongo was held from 7 to 21 January 2007 in Gabon." .

ns1:61179 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Bavarian state election was held on 28 September 2008 to elect the members of the Landtag of Bavaria. Summary of the 28 September 2008 election results for the Landtag of Bavaria." .

ns1:61194 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Nazran raid was a large-scale raid carried out in the Republic of Ingushetia, Russia on the night of 21 June 2004–22, 2004, by a group of mostly Chechen and Ingush militants led by the Chechen commander Shamil Basayev. Several days after the 2004 Beslan school siege, Deputy Prosecutor General of Russia Vladimir Kolesnikov said 10 of the weapons stolen in Nazran were used in the Beslan attack." .

ns1:61209 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC on Fox: Johnson vs. Reis (also known as UFC on Fox 24) was a mixed martial arts event produced by the Ultimate Fighting Championship held on 15 April 2017, at the T-Mobile Center in Kansas City, Missouri." .

ns1:61239 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Indonesia Super Series was the fifth Super Series tournament of the 2017 BWF Super Series. The tournament took place in Jakarta, Indonesia from 12 June 2017–18 June 2017 with a total purse of $1,000,000." .

ns1:61242 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1904 Summer Olympics – men's long jump was a track and field athletics event held as part of the athletics at the 1904 Summer Olympics programme. Myer Prinstein of the United States, who took silver in 1900, was the only jumper from Paris to return in 1904." .

ns1:61248 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1912 United States presidential election in Virginia took place on 05 November 1912. Virginia voted for the Democratic nominee, New Jersey Governor Woodrow Wilson, over the Republican nominee, incumbent President of the United States William Howard Taft, and the Progressive nominee, former President of the United States Theodore Roosevelt." .

ns1:61253 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Carpathian Trophy was the 49th edition of the Carpathian Trophy held in Craiova, Romania between 24 November 2017–26 November 2017 as a women's friendly handball tournament organised by the Romanian Handball Federation." .

ns1:61262 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1936 Summer Olympics – men's 400 metres hurdles event at the 1936 Summer Olympic Games took place on 03 August 1936 and 04 August 1936." .

ns1:61266 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963 Giro del Trentino was the second edition of the Tour of the Alps cycle race and was held on 22 June 1963." .

ns1:61270 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Path of Totality Tour was a concert tour in support of Korn's tenth studio album The Path of Totality. Korn: The Path of Totality Tour – Live at the Hollywood Palladium was released on DVD and Blu-ray on September 4, 2012 by Shout!" .

ns1:61280 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Saguntum (25 October 1811) saw the Imperial French Army of Aragon under Marshal Louis Gabriel Suchet fighting a Spain army led by Captain General Joaquín Blake. The Spain attempt to raise the siege of the Sagunto Castle failed when the French, Italians, and Poles drove their troops off the battlefield in rout. Sagunto lies a short distance from the east coast of Spain, about 30 kilometres (19 mi) north of Valencia. On 22 September, Suchet's entire army set out from Castellón de la Plana, brushing aside 500 Spain troops at Villarreal and the next day was before Sagunto Castle. The French marshal divided his army into a blockade force to surround Sagunto Castle and a covering force to defend against Spain interference. Martín's guerillas drove off a 1,000-strong relief column and then the Spain forced the 560 survivors to surrender on 3 25 October 1811 by exploding two mines under the walls. After providing a garrison for Sagunto Castle and detaching a brigade to escort the Spain prisoners to the rear, he had only 15,000 men available for field operations." .

ns1:61287 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sheemore ambush was an ambush carried out by the Irish Republican Army (IRA) on 04 March 1921, during the Irish War of Independence." .

ns1:61300 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 24th Edition 1969 Vuelta a España (Tour of Spain), a long-distance bicycle stage race and one of the three grand tours, was held from 23 April 1969 to 11 May 1969." .

ns1:61302 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1934–35 FAI Cup was the fourteenth edition of Ireland premier cup competition, The Football Association of Ireland Challenge Cup or FAI Cup." .

ns1:61303 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Players Tour Championship 2011/2012 – Event 7 (also known as the 2011 Kay Suzanne Memorial Trophy) was a professional minor-ranking snooker tournament that took place between 05 October 2011–09 October 2011 at the South West Snooker Academy in Gloucester, England." .

ns1:61311 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1909 World Allround Speed Skating Championships for men took place at 27 February 1909 and 28 February 1909 at the ice rink Gamle Frogner in Kristiania, Norway." .

ns1:61317 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Teen Choice Awards ceremony was held on 06 August 2000 and broadcast on Fox Broadcasting Company." .

ns1:61326 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Scottish Open Badminton Championships was a badminton tournament that took place at the Emirates Arena in Scotland from 21 to 25 November 2018 and had a total prize of $75,000. The 2018 Scottish Open Badminton Championships was the eleventh Super 100 tournament of the 2018 BWF World Tour and also part of the Scottish Open Badminton Championships championships, which had been held since 1907." .

ns1:61346 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985 Virginia Slims Championships were the fourteenth WTA Tour Championships, the annual tennis tournament for the best female tennis players in singles on the 1985 WTA Tour." .

ns1:61352 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1973 UCI Road World Championships took place on 02 September 1973 in Montjuïc, Barcelona, Spain, with four events contested." .

ns1:61360 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988–89 FIS Ski Jumping World Cup was the 10th FIS Ski Jumping World Cup season in ski jumping. The individual FIS Ski Jumping World Cup was won by Jan Boklöv and Nations Cup by Norway." .

ns1:61376 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 San Marino and Rimini Riviera motorcycle Grand Prix was the thirteenth round of the 2018 MotoGP season. It was held at the Misano World Circuit Marco Simoncelli in Misano Adriatico on 09 September 2018." .

ns1:61384 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1952 Dominican Republic general election were held in the Dominican Republic on 16 May 1952." .

ns1:61401 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1982 Toyota Series Championships was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at the Byrne Meadowlands Arena in East Rutherford, New Jersey in the United States that was the season-ending tournament of the 1982 Virginia Slims World Championship Series. It was the sixth and last edition of the tournament and was held from 14 December 1982 through 19 December 1982." .

ns1:61427 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 anti-Igbo pogrom was a series of massacres committed against Igbo people and other people of southern Nigerian origin living in Northern Region starting in May 1966 and reaching a peak after 29 September 1966. It also was the precursor to Ojukwu's declaration of Eastern Nigeria's secession from the federation as the Republic of Biafra, and the resulting Nigerian Civil War (1967–1970), which Biafra lost." .

ns1:61435 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Barcelona Open Banc Sabadell (also known as the Torneo Godó) was a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts. It was the 64th edition of Barcelona Open and part of the ATP World Tour 500 series of the 2016 ATP World Tour. It took place at the Real Club de Tenis Barcelona in Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain, from 18 April 2016 through 24 April 2016." .

ns1:61445 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Finnish Figure Skating Championships took place between 18 December 2004 and 19, 2004 in Hämeenlinna. Skaters competed in the disciplines of men's singles and women's singles on the senior and junior levels." .

ns1:61448 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1900 European Figure Skating Championships were held on 21 January 1900 in Berlin, German Empire." .

ns1:61450 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1881 Chios earthquake occurred at 13:40 local time (11:30 UTC) on 03 April 1881. The devastation from the earthquake was the last of the three 'catastrophes' that affected the island of Chios in the 19th century. The epicenter of the earthquake was in the southeastern part of Chios where intensities reached IX (Violent) on the Mercalli intensity scale. After the earthquake many of the inhabitants of Chios left the island." .

ns1:61455 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1976 United States presidential election in Wyoming took place on 02 November 1976, as part of the 1976 United States presidential election. Despite losing in Wyoming, Carter went on to win the national election and became the 39th President of the United States of the United States. With 59.3 percent of the popular vote, Wyoming would prove to be Ford's third strongest state in the 1976 election after Utah and Idaho." .

ns1:61458 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Wimbledon Championships was a tennis tournament played on grass courts at the All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club in Wimbledon, London in the United Kingdom. It was the 126th edition of the Wimbledon Championships and were held from 25 June 2012 to 08 July 2012. Seedings based on ATP and WTA rankings are as of 2012, Rankings and Points are as of 25 June 2012." .

ns1:61462 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Koran Interpreted is a translation of the Quran (the Islamic religious text) by Arthur John Arberry." .

ns1:61469 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC Fight Night: Bader vs. Saint Preux (also known as UFC Fight Night 47) was a mixed martial arts event held on 16 August 2014, at the Cross Insurance Center in Bangor, Maine." .

ns1:61491 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Guamanian gubernatorial election took place on 04 November 2014, to elect the Governor of Guam." .

ns1:61493 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 FA Cup Final was contested by Newcastle United F.C. and Arsenal F.C. at Wembley Stadium in what became known as the \"Over The Line\" final. Newcastle won 2–1, both of their goals scored by Jack Allen. Arsenal F.C. had led 1–0 with a Bob John goal, but Newcastle's equaliser came after a long ball that had appeared to foul over the goal line, and was put back into action for a goal kick. Allen scored again in the second half to win the match 2–1." .

ns1:61499 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final took place in Croke Park, Dublin on Sunday, 2011. Prior to the senior final, Galway claimed the 2011 Minor Hurling Championship after a 1–21 to 1–12 win against Dublin. Offaly-based referee Brian Gavin was named as the referee for the 2011 All-Ireland final on 16 August." .

ns1:61512 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sinking of Prince of Wales and Repulse was a naval engagement in World War II, as part of the war in the Pacific, that took place on 10 December 1941 in the South China Sea off the east coast of the British colony of Malaya (present-day Malaysia), 70 miles (61 nautical miles; 110 kilometres) east of Kuantan, Pahang." .

ns1:61515 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The wrestling at the 1996 Summer Olympics – men's Greco-Roman 62 kg as part of the wrestling at the 1996 Summer Olympics were held at the Georgia World Congress Center from July 22 to July 23." .

ns1:61516 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1973 Nauruan parliamentary election were held in Nauru on 15 December 1973." .

ns1:61526 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Open du Pays d'Aix was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Aix-en-Provence, France between 04 May 2015 and 10 May 2015." .

ns1:61527 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Nabisco Dinah Shore was a women's professional golf tournament, held 27 March 1997–30 at Mission Hills Country Club in Rancho Mirage, California." .

ns1:61535 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1954 Italian Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 05 September 1954 at Autodromo Nazionale Monza. It was race 8 of 9 in the 1954 Formula One season. The 80-lap race was won by Mercedes driver Juan Manuel Fangio after he started from pole position." .

ns1:61545 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 Men's World Open Squash Championship is the men's edition of the 1989 World Squash Championships, which serves as the individual world championship for squash players. The event took place in Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia from 1989-1989. Jansher Khan won his second World Squash Championships title, defeating Chris Dittmar in the final." .

ns1:61559 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 The Hague Open was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Scheveningen, Netherlands between 25 July 2016 and 31 July 2016." .

ns1:61567 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kathmandu (Nepali: काठमाडौंको युद्ध) or Siege of Kathmandu or Siege of Kantipur occurred during the Gorkhali conquest of Nepal. It was fought in Kathmandu in 1768, and resulted in the defeat of its king Jaya Prakash Malla by Prithvi Narayan Shah, king of the adjoining Gorkha Kingdom. (26th 1768), the Gorkhali forces commanded by Vamsharaj Pande, Surapratap Shah and Tularam Pande attacked Kathmandu and captured the royal palace in the night. After a brief battle, Jaya Prakash Malla realized that he had been betrayed by the nobles, and that Kathmandu was lost." .

ns1:61573 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Studio Gigante was a Chicago-based video game developer established in 2000 by John Tobias, Dave Michicich, and Joshua Tsui, several developers of Midway's popular Mortal Kombat fighting game series." .

ns1:61580 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1976 Puerto Rican general election were held in Puerto Rico on 02 November 1976." .

ns1:61592 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cahuenga Pass of 1831 was fought at Cahuenga Pass near Los Angeles between the unpopular Mexican Governor of California (Manuel Victoria), and a force assembled by wealthy local landowners. The forces met on 05 December 1831, at Cahuenga Pass, with Captain Portilla in charge of the rebels. This battle should not be confused with the Battle of Providencia (also known as the Second Battle of Cahuenga Pass)." .

ns1:61594 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Colonial Athletic Association (CAA) is a collegiate athletic conference affiliated with the NCAA's NCAA Division I whose full members are located in East Coast states from Massachusetts to South Carolina." .

ns1:61595 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A Corsican autonomy referendum, 2003 was held on 06 July 2003. The question asked was: Do you approve of the proposed suggestions to change the institutional organisation of Corsica represented in law 2003-486 of 2003?" .

ns1:61598 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cambodia is participating at the Cambodia at the 2011 Southeast Asian Games which are being held in the cities of Palembang and Jakarta, Indonesia from 2011 to 2011." .

ns1:61604 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sandro Girgvliani Murder Case is one of the most notorious criminal cases in the modern history of Georgia. Sandro Girgvliani was found dead on 28 January 2006 on the outskirts of Tbilisi with multiple injuries inflicted as a result of physical abuse. According to an Imedi Television investigation on February 12, the murder of the 28-year-old head of the United Georgian Bank's Foreign Department, can be traced to a series of events which developed in Tbilisi's elite Sharden Bar. At this point the influential former Foreign Minister and leader of the Georgia's Way political party, Salome Zourabichvili, announced her intention to work with the opposition parties regarding Girgvliani's murder. Tbilisi City Court launched on June 27 hearings into the murder case. The Tbilisi City Court sentenced Gia Alania, ex-chief of the first unit of the Interior Ministry's Department for Constitutional Security (DCS), to eight-years imprisonment for Sandro Girgvliani's murder. During the scandal the group held a series of protest rallies in Tbilisi demanding a fair investigation into Girgvliani's murder. If the testimony by Bukhaidze were to be confirmed , it would undermine the entire official motives behind the crime - that the murder occurred as a result of a spontaneous row between the victim and four former police officials outside the Sheredan café in downtown Tbilisi. Patrol Policeman Grigol Bashaleishvili was found guilty and sentenced to four-years imprisonment on August 10 by the Tbilisi City Court of the negligent murder of 19-year-old Amiran Robakidze on 23 November 2004." .

ns1:61610 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Hall of Fame Tennis Championships (also known as 2000 Miller Lite Hall of Fame Championships for sponsorship reasons) was a tennis tournament played on grass courts at the International Tennis Hall of Fame in Newport, Rhode Island in the United States of America and was part of the ATP International Series of the 2000 ATP Tour." .

ns1:61615 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 LPGA Championship was the eleventh Women's PGA Championship, held September 23–26 at Stardust Country Club in Las Vegas, Nevada. Sandra Haynie, age 22, won the first of her two Women's PGA Championship titles, one stroke ahead of runner-up Clifford Ann Creed." .

ns1:61624 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Food City 500 was the fourth stock car race of the 2012 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. It was held on 18 March 2012 at Bristol Motor Speedway in Bristol, Tennessee before a crowd of 102,000. The 2012 Food City 500 was the fourth of thirty-six scheduled stock car races of the 2012 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. It took place on 18 March 2012, in Bristol, Tennessee, at Bristol Motor Speedway, a short track which holds NASCAR races." .

ns1:61627 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1880 United Kingdom general election was a general election in the United Kingdom held from 31 March 1880 to 27 April 1880." .

ns1:61645 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Hong Kong Open Badminton Championships was held from 28 August 2006 to 02 September 2006." .

ns1:61654 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Durian, known in the Philippines as Typhoon Reming, was a violent tropical cyclone that wreaked havoc in the Philippines in late 25 November 2006, causing massive loss of life when mudflows from the Mayon Volcano buried many villages." .

ns1:61656 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Camping World Grand Prix at the Glen was the ninth round of the 2009 IndyCar Series season. It took place on 05 July 2009 at the 3.370-mile (5.423 km) Watkins Glen International road course in Watkins Glen, New York." .

ns1:61661 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Senior League World Series took place from 13 August 2000–19 in Kissimmee, Florida, United States." .

ns1:61665 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Alhandic (Spanish: Batalla de Alhandic), also known as Zamora's trench Battle (Batalla del Foso de Zamora), was a battle that occurred on 05 August 0939, 939 in the city of Zamora, Spain. The battle occurred when the troops of Abd-ar-Rahman III assaulted the walls of Zamora. This battle should not be confused with the Day of Zamora (Día de Zamora or Jornada del Foso de Zamora) which took place a few decades before in the year 901. This bloodthirsty strategy lends its name to the battle which is sometimes known as the Batalla del Foso de Zamora (Zamora's trench Battle)." .

ns1:61673 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Nordic Figure Skating Championships were the Nordic Figure Skating Championships of the 2016–2017 season. Skaters competed in two disciplines, ladies singles and men's singles, across three levels: senior (Olympic-level), junior, and novice. The 2017 Nordics were held at the Egilshöll in Reykjavik, Iceland from March 2nd through 5th, 2017." .

ns1:61676 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Keio Challenger was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Yokohama, Japan between 27 February 2017 and 05 March 2017 for the men's edition and between 2017 and 12 for the women's." .

ns1:61687 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "National Astronaut Day is an American commemorative day held on May 5 since 2017. It commemorates the first United States human spaceflight, on May 5, 1961, piloted by astronaut Alan Shepard." .

ns1:61700 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "At the diving at the 1984 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles, four diving events (2 for men and 2 for women) were contested during a competition that took place at the McDonald's Olympic Swim Stadium of the University of Southern California (USC), from 5 to 12 August, comprising 80 divers from 29 nations." .

ns1:61728 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The murder of George Harry Storrs occurred on 01 November 1909 in Stalybridge, Cheshire, England." .

ns1:61733 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Animation Kobe (Japanese: アニメーション神戸) was an event established by Kōbe in 1996 to promote anime and other visual media. The Animation Kobe Awards (アニメーション神戸賞) are given annually by Kōbe and the Organising Committee to creators and creations. Animation Kobe has been held annually in Kōbe since 1996. Animation films released in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. The TV animations broadcast in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year, excluding rebroadcasts, become candidates. The packaged media distributed in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. Re-created in 2000 as Network Media Award, the anime-related media making the best use of interactive distribution in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. The theme songs of either anime or other forms of animated media distributed in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates." .

ns1:61737 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1933 UCI Road World Championships took place in Montlhéry, France between 14 August 1933 and 1933." .

ns1:61740 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 British Grand Prix (formally the 2007 Formula 1 Santander British Grand Prix) was the ninth race of the 2007 Formula One World Championship. It was held on 08 July 2007 at the Silverstone Circuit. The race was won by Kimi Räikkönen after overtaking pole position driver Lewis Hamilton during the first round of pit stops. Following United Kingdom driver Lewis Hamilton's win at the 2007 Canadian Grand Prix, circuit director Richard Phillips reported that ticket sales had \"gone through the roof\"." .

ns1:61743 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2010 Guamanian legislative election also known as Senatorial election for the Legislature of Guam took place on 02 November 2010, coinciding with the 2010 United States general elections and the Guam gubernatorial election." .

ns1:61745 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Star Awards 2003 was an awards ceremony part of the annual Star Awards held by MediaCorp Channel 8 on 2003." .

ns1:61748 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1984 Greenlandic general election were held in Greenland on 06 June 1984." .

ns1:61749 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A novel strain of 2011 Germany E. coli O104:H4 outbreak caused a serious outbreak of foodborne illness focused in northern Germany in May through June 2011. In all, 3,950 people were affected and 53 died, 51 of whom were in Germany. Essentially all affected people had been in Germany or France shortly before becoming ill. The most substantial outbreak outside of Germany was in Bordeaux, France where 15 cases of EHEC gastroenteritis were associated with the same strain of E. coli which caused the outbreak in Germany. The French cases had not previously travelled to Germany, suggesting they acquired the bacteria from contaminated sprouts grown in France. Most or all victims were believed to have become infected in Germany or France. A joint risk-assessment by EFSA/ECDC, issued 29 01 June 2011, made a connection between the German outbreak and a HUS outbreak in the Bordeaux area of France, first reported on 24 June, in which infection with E. coli O104:H4 has been confirmed in several patients." .

ns1:61753 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2010 Anguillan general election were held in Anguilla on 15 February 2010. Retiring Chief Minister Osbourne Fleming officially set 15 February 2010, as the date for the election during a public meeting of the ruling Anguilla United Front (AUF) in Blowing Point held on 5 January 2010. In his announcement, Fleming told supporters, \"Tonight, I take great pleasure in advising you that by the help of God, because we don't know what could happen, elections in Anguilla will be on the 15th of 15 February 2010.\"" .

ns1:61760 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Spengler Cup was a men's ice hockey competition being held in Davos, Switzerland between 2017 and 2017. All matches were being played at HC Davos's home known as Vaillant Arena." .

ns1:61764 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A sweep is either of two categories of martial arts techniques. A sweep can be used to take the opponent to the ground or it can simply disrupt the opponent's balance long enough to make an opening for a punch or kick." .

ns1:61772 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 Montenegrin Second League (Serbian: Druga Crnogorska Liga / Друга црногорска лига) was the sixth season of the competition as the second top association football league in Montenegro. The league played its first games of the season on 14 August 2011 and its final matches were played on 30 May 2012." .

ns1:61774 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Big E is inclusive of all six of the New England states: Connecticut, Maine, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, Rhode Island, and Vermont. Located in the Pioneer Valley of Western Massachusetts, a short distance from the Memorial Bridge spanning the Connecticut River, The Big E is held every autumn in West Springfield, Massachusetts. The first Eastern States Exposition occurred in October 1916 in Springfield, Massachusetts and was called the Eastern States Agricultural and Industrial Exposition." .

ns1:61780 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1956 Democratic Party presidential primaries were the selection process by which voters of the Democratic Party chose its nominee for President of the United States in the 1956 U.S. presidential election. Former Illinois Governor Adlai Stevenson II was selected as the nominee through a series of primary election and caucuses culminating in the 1956 Democratic National Convention held from August 13 to 1956, in Chicago, Illinois." .

ns1:61785 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Producers Guild of America Awards 2008 (also known as 2009 Producers Guild Awards), honoring the best film and television producers of 2008, were held at Hollywood Palladium in Hollywood, California on 24 January 2009." .

ns1:61794 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Hamburg state election was held on 21 September 1997 to elect the members of the 16th Hamburg Parliament. Summary of the 21 September 1997 election results for the Hamburg Parliament." .

ns1:61808 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Eurymedon vase is an Attic red-figure pottery oenochoe, a wine jug attributed to the circle of the Triptolemos Painter made ca." .

ns1:61811 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988–89 Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball team represented the US University of Oklahoma in competitive college basketball during the 1988–89 NCAA Division I season. The Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball team played its home games in the Lloyd Noble Center and was a member of the National Collegiate Athletic Association's (NCAA) former Big Eight Conference at that time. Mookie Blaylock established the current Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball single-season minutes played (1359) and career steals (281) records." .

ns1:61819 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Sparkassen Cup – doubles was the tennis doubles event of the tenth edition of the Sparkassen Cup; a WTA Tier II tournament held in Leipzig, Germany. Elena Likhovtseva and Ai Sugiyama were the defending champions but were defeated in this year's final by Larisa Neiland and Mary Pierce, 6–1, 6–3." .

ns1:61839 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In culture of Wales, an eisteddfod (/aɪˈstɛðvɒd/ (listen) eye-STEDH-vod, also US: /eɪˈ-/ ay-, UK: /aɪˈstɛdvəd, -fəd, -vɒd, -fɒd/ eye-STED-vəd, -fəd, -vod, -fod, Welsh:  (listen); plural eisteddfods or eisteddfodau ) is, according to Martha A. Davies, \"a Welsh festival with adjudicated competitions for poets, musicians, and others.\" The revival proved enormously successful and is credited as the primary reason for the continued survival of the Welsh, literature, poetry, and culture of Wales. In some countries, the term eisteddfod is used for performing arts competitions that have nothing to do with culture of Wales or the Welsh. But interest in the Welsh arts declined during the 17th and 18th centuries, leading to the standard of the main eisteddfod deteriorating. By the 1850s people began to talk of a national eisteddfod to showcase Wales's culture of Wales. Eisteddfods (Australian plural) in the traditional Welsh sense have also been adopted into Australian culture of Wales. At least 20 years earlier, as described in the diaries of Joseph Jenkins, Ballarat's Welsh community was conducting an annual eisteddfod each St David's Day (1 March). The largest U.S. eisteddfod was held In 1893 at the World Columbian Exposition in Chicago, featuring visiting Welsh choirs invited by The Cymmrodorion Society of Chicago. The eisteddfod idea was retained by some subsequent world's fairs, and helped to link the Welsh Eisteddfod community to its American offshoot. The Jackson School Eisteddfod in Jackson, Ohio, is the result of an historically strong Welsh business community, who funded the Southern Ohio Eisteddfod Association and a 4,000-seat auditorium that was the only dedicated eisteddfod venue in the United States. Welsh Heritage Week and Cwrs Cymraeg, two ambulatory Welsh language and culture of Wales courses held annually, usually in the United States, also each feature a mini-eisteddfod. The North American Festival of Wales held by the Welsh North American Association also includes an eisteddfod. Since it was founded as part of the Gaelic Revival by Conradh na Gaeilge in 1902, Seachtain na Gaeilge, which is similar to the eisteddfod, has celebrated Irish traditional music, Gaelic games, and Irish culture of Wales and promoted the Irish language." .

ns1:61841 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Toyota Grand Prix of Long Beach was the 40th annual running of the Grand Prix of Long Beach and the second race of the 2014 IndyCar Series season." .

ns1:61844 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1977 Egypt Cup Final, was the final match of 1976–77 Egypt Cup, when Zamalek SC played Ismaily SC, Zamalek SC won the game 3–1." .

ns1:61847 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Internationaler Apano Cup was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Dortmund, Germany between 25 July 2011 and 31 July 2011." .

ns1:61854 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000–01 Umaglesi Liga was the twelfth season of top-tier football in Georgia. It began on 19 August 2000 and ended on 23 May 2001." .

ns1:61861 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Curling was a Olympic demonstration sport competition at the curling at the 1992 Winter Olympics. The 1992 Winter Olympics was the third time curling was a Olympic demonstration sport competition at the Winter Olympics. The women's curling event at the curling at the 1992 Winter Olympics had eight countries in two groups." .

ns1:61862 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 26 June 1625 is the battle which took place on 26 June 1625 near Syracuse, Sicily, when 6 Bizertan vessels defeated 5 Maltese galleys." .

ns1:61871 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Asian Women's Volleyball Championship was the 12th Asian Women's Volleyball Championship, which took place from 20 September 2003 to 2003 in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam." .

ns1:61880 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 ICF Canoe Sprint World Championships were held in Duisburg, Germany on August 9–12, 2007 for the record-tying fourth time. The Germany city had hosted the ICF Canoe Sprint World Championships previously in 1979, 1987, and 1995." .

ns1:61888 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Boston Marathon was the 121st running of the Boston Athletic Association's Boston Marathon." .

ns1:61890 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Senior men's race at the 1991 IAAF World Cross Country Championships – senior men's race was held in Antwerp, Belgium, at the Linkeroever Racecourse on 1991." .

ns1:61909 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Shahi Tandar, also called Operation Atal, was a series of operations by Coalition troops from the British 42 Commando Royal Marines, Royal Canadian Regiment, 2nd Battalion 2nd Infantry Regiment (United States), and the Afghan national military in central Helmand province and the Western Panjwayi and Western Zhari districts of Kandahar, Afghanistan from 07 January 2009–31, 2009. One raid targeted a Taliban bomb-making factory in the Khakrez and Shah Wali Khot districts of Kandahar, Afghanistan, 07 January 2009–9, 2009." .

ns1:61916 a ns1:context_narration ;
