ns1:62190 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008–09 Toto Cup Al was the twenty-seventh season of the third most important association football tournament in Israel since its introduction and fifth under the current format. Maccabi Tel Aviv F.C. won the 2008–09 Toto Cup Al making it their third Toto Cup title overall." .

ns1:62191 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Newark mayoral election took place in Newark, the most populous city in New Jersey, on 2014. In order to be placed on the ballot candidates must submit petitions with signatures from 1% of the registered voters in the last general election (1,498 for citywide candidates and several hundred for Ward candidates) Relevant 2014 dates: Of several candidates who announced their candidacy mayor in 2013, two have been certified: former Assistant State Attorney General Shavar Jeffries and Municipal Council member Ras Baraka. He became acting mayor on October 31, 2013, and was sworn in on November 4, 2013, assuming the unexpired term of Booker, Quintana's term ends on 2014. A New Jersey State Comptroller report issued in 2014 revealed irregularities and corruption within the Newark Watershed and Development Corporation, which is the process of being dismantled after being taken over the city." .

ns1:62192 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1975 Finnish parliamentary election were held in Finland on 21 September 1975 and 22 September 1975. Although Helsinki was to host the Conference on Security and Co-operation in Europe (CSCE) at the end of July and at the start of 1975, Kekkonen did not worry about the possibly negative effect on Finland's international image of having a caretaker government." .

ns1:62214 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The James W. Murphy Stakes is an American Thoroughbred horse race run annually at Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore. Beginning with the 2010 race, the Woodlawn Stakes was renamed the James W. Murphy Stakes in honor of the late trainer, James W. Murphy, a stalwart on the Maryland racing circuit." .

ns1:62223 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Kremlin Cup was a tennis tournament played on indoor hard courts. It was the 25th edition of the Kremlin Cup for the men (19th edition for the women) and part of the ATP World Tour 250 Series of the 2014 ATP World Tour, and of the Premier Series of the 2014 WTA Tour. It was held at the Olympiysky Sports Complex in Moscow, Russia, from 13 October through 2014." .

ns1:62231 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Adjara crisis was a political crisis in Georgia's Adjara Autonomous Republic, then led by Aslan Abashidze, who refused to obey the central authorities after President Eduard Shevardnadze's ousting during the Rose Revolution of 01 November 2003. However, Georgia's post-revolutionary government of President Mikheil Saakashvili managed to avoid bloodshed and with the help of Adjara opposition reasserted its supremacy. In retaliation, Georgia's central authorities imposed partial economic sanctions against its defiant region in a bid \"to exhaust Adjara regime's resources\". In retaliation, the two key bridges connecting Adjara with the rest of Georgia over the Choloki River were blown up by Abashidze's forces to prevent incursion in Adjara allegedly planned by the country's central authorities. \"Aslan has fled, Adjara is free,\" President Saakashvili announced at the dawn of St George's Day on May 6 and congratulated Georgians with what he described as \"a second bloodless revolution\" in Georgia." .

ns1:62240 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Albania participated in the Eurovision Song Contest 2015 in Vienna, Austria, with the song \"I'm Alive\" performed by Elhaida Dani. In Albania's Albania in the Eurovision Song Contest on 23 May, \"I'm Alive\" finished in seventeenth place, receiving 34 points. Prior to the 2015 contest, Albania had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest eleven times since its first entry in 2004. The Albanian broadcaster for the 2015 Contest, who broadcast the event in Albania and organised the selection process for its entry, was Radio Televizioni Shqiptar (RTSH). Festivali i Këngës 53 was the 53rd annual edition of the Albanian music competition Festivali i Këngës and the twelfth time the competition was used to determine the artist and song that would represent Albania at the Eurovision Song Contest, this time selecting their 2015 contest entry. On 2015, Elhaida Dani issued a statement on social media that \"Albania in the Eurovision Song Contest 2015\" had been withdrawn by the songwriters due to \"personal and irrevocable reasons\". Albania was placed into the first semi-final, to be held on 2015, and was scheduled to perform in the second half of the show." .

ns1:62242 a ns1:context_narration ;
