ns1:62619 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Miss Georgia's Outstanding Teen competition is the pageant that selects the representative for the U.S. state of Georgia in the Miss America's Outstanding Teen pageant. Mary Wilhelmina Hodges of Louisville, Georgia was crowned Miss Georgia's Outstanding Teen on June 16, 2019 at the RiverCenter of the Performing Arts in Columbus, Georgia. The results of Miss Georgia's Outstanding Teen as they participated in the national Miss America's Outstanding Teen competition." .

ns1:62624 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Rey de Reyes (Spanish for \"King of Kings\") was the ninth annual Rey de Reyes professional wrestling tournament and show, produced by the Mexican wrestling promotion AAA. The event took place on 11 March 2005 in the Convention Center in Ciudad Madero, Tamaulipas, Mexico. Starting in 1997 and every year since then the Mexican Lucha Libre, or professional wrestling, company AAA has held a Rey de Reyes (Spanish for \"King of Kings') show in the spring. As part of their annual Rey de Reyes event AAA holds the eponymious Rey de Reyes tournament to determine that specific year's Rey. The Rey de Reyes show featured six professional wrestling matches with different wrestlers involved in pre-existing, scripted feuds, plots, and storylines." .

ns1:62628 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1900 South Dakota gubernatorial election was held on 1900, to elect a Governor of South Dakota to a two-year term." .

ns1:62631 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The boccia at the 2016 Summer Paralympics – individual BC1 at the 2016 Summer Paralympics was contested from 13 September to 16 at Sambodromo in Rio de Janeiro. boccia at the 2012 Summer Paralympics – individual BC1 silver medalist, Great Britain's David Smith, won the gold medal, his second ever and first in an individual event, over the Netherlands' Daniel Perez, with Korea's Yoo Won Jeong beating Antonio Marques of Portugal for the bronze medal." .

