ns1:62785 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 Irani Cup, also called 2013-14 Irani Trophy, was the 52nd season of the Irani Cup, a first-class cricket competition in India. M. Chinnaswamy Stadium, the home ground of Karnataka cricket team, hosted the match." .

ns1:62786 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Manningham riot was a short but intense period of racial rioting which took place from 9 June 1995–11 June 1995, in the district of Manningham in Bradford, West Yorkshire, England. The riot of summer 1995 was limited to a relatively confined area of the city, but was seen as indicative of the circumstances which led to the later and more widespread Bradford Riot of July 2001." .

ns1:62787 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 United States House of Representatives election in South Dakota took place on Tuesday, 05 November 2002. Though Republicans were unsuccessful in defeating Tim Johnson during the concurrent Senate election, however they did succeed in defending South Dakota's U.S. House seat." .

ns1:62797 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1978 European Figure Skating Championships was a senior-level international competition held in Strasbourg, France from January 31 to 05 February 1978. Elite senior-level figure skaters from European International Skating Union member nations competed for the title of European Champion in the disciplines of men's singles, ladies' singles, pair skating, and ice dancing." .

ns1:62800 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010–11 Rugby Pro D2 season was the season of the second-level French rugby union club competition, behind the Top 14, for the 2010–11 season. But whilst Albi struggled to keep their momentum after the Christmas break, Lyon managed to maintain their winning ways and held on to their top spot until the end of the season despite a remarkable finish by Grenoble, who had missed on a semi-final spot because of an unfavourable head-to-head against Pau the 2009–10 Rugby Pro D2 season, and who came back from a poor start to finish within two points of Lyon, the smallest margin between the top two teams since the establishment of the Pro D2, and seven points clear of Albi. While Carcassone enjoyed a very successful season, to the point that they looked like a credible candidate for the promotion playoffs for the first half of the season, ultimately finishing in tenth, Saint-Étienne had a nightmarish season, with a single win, one draw and twenty-eight losses, amounting to 17 points, the poorest-ever record in the Pro D2 (Lannemezan had finished with 19 points the 2009–10 Rugby Pro D2 season). Aix-en-Provence, who had been reprieved the 2009–10 Rugby Pro D2 season, looked like they were going to be part of a three-way battle with Dax and Colomiers to avoid the second relegation spot, but a string of victories in the second half of the season ensured that they would stay in Pro D2 for at least a third consecutive year." .

ns1:62815 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 2014 Macau Open Badminton Championships was the eighteenth tournament of the 2014 BWF Grand Prix Gold and Grand Prix circuit. The tournament was held in Tap Seac Multi-sports Pavilion, Macau 25 November 2014–30, 2014 and had a total purse of $120,000." .

ns1:62816 a ns1:context_narration ;
