ns1:62873 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Reference re Alberta Statutes, also known as the Alberta Press case and the Alberta Press Act Reference, is a landmark reference question of the Supreme Court of Canada where several provincial laws, including one restricting the press, were struck down and the existence of an implied bill of rights protecting civil liberties such as a free press was first proposed. The Supreme Court of Canada, in answering reference question posed by the federal government, unanimously ruled that such disallowance was valid." .

