ns1:63034 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Tiderace was the codename of the British plan to retake Singapore following the Japanese surrender in 1945. Operation Tiderace commenced when Mountbatten ordered Allied troops to set sail from Trincomalee and Rangoon on 31 August for Singapore. The fleet arrived in Singapore on 04 September 1945, meeting no opposition. The formal surrender was finalised on 12 September 1945 at Singapore City Hall." .

ns1:63038 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Aéro-Frêt Antonov An-12 crash was the crash of an Antonov An-12 into a cemetery at Brazzaville, Republic of the Congo on 26 August 2009." .

ns1:63047 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hale America National Open Golf Tournament was a professional golf tournament on the PGA Tour that played for a single year, 1942. Additionally, the original site chosen for the event, Interlachen Country Club in Edina, Minnesota, opted not to serve as the host course." .

