ns1:63315 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Starty nadezhd (Russian: Старты надежд) was the national children's multi-sport event in the Soviet Union. As every school age boy and girl of the then-Soviet Union of classes 4 to 9 of secondary school could take part in \"Starty nadezhd\", competing in one's parallel class, the competition served as great means of popularizing sports among people, and exposing them to practicing sports, competitive activity and team spirit." .

