ns1:63356 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2008–09 Celtic F.C. season was the 120th season of competitive association football by Celtic F.C.. The Championship flag was unfurled before Celtic F.C.'s first League game, against St Mirren at Celtic F.C. Park on 10 August by Rosemary Burns, the widow of former Celtic F.C. player Tommy Burns, who had died of skin cancer at the end of 2007–08 Celtic F.C. season." .

ns1:63357 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The three-line United Nations Security Council Resolution 338, adopted on 22 October 1973, called for a ceasefire in the Yom Kippur War in accordance with a joint proposal by the United States and the Soviet Union. The legal force added to United Nations Security Council resolution 242 by this resolution is the reason for the otherwise puzzling fact that SC 242 and the otherwise seemingly superfluous and superannuated United Nations Security Council resolution 338 are always referred to together in legal documents relating to the conflict. The more obvious need for the use of United Nations Security Council resolution 338 is that it requires all parties to cease fire and states when that should occur, without which United Nations Security Council resolution 242 can't be accomplished. Egypt and Israel accepted on 22 October 1973 United Nations Security Council resolution conditions. On 22 October 1973 the superpowers brokered UN Security Council United Nations Security Council resolution 338." .

ns1:63358 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "After first competing in 1938, Fiji returned to the Fiji at the 1950 British Empire Games in 1950 in Auckland, New Zealand. The 1950 Games have been Fiji's most successful to date." .

ns1:63359 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Greek Football Cup was the 74th edition of the Greek Football Cup. The Greek authorities announced on deadline day that the Greek Football Cup will be resumed after an agreement reached with FIFA, UEFA and Hellenic Football Federation." .

ns1:63365 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Million Women Rise (MWR) is a women-only march and rally against violence against women, held annually in London on a Saturday close to International Women's Day, 8 March. Million Women Rise (MWR) believes that male violence against women and children is a global pandemic that devastates lives and threatens to undermine efforts to bring about sustainable development." .

ns1:63366 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Black May refers to a period (24 May 1943) in the Battle of the Atlantic campaign during World War II, when the German U-boat arm (U-Bootwaffe) suffered high casualties with fewer Allied ships sunk; it is considered a turning point in the Battle of the Atlantic. After February battles around convoys SC 118, ON 166, and UC 1, Black May was the culmination of the March– 24 May 1943 crisis in the Battle of the Atlantic." .

ns1:63367 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002–03 FIS Ski Jumping Continental Cup was the 12th in a row (10th official) FIS Ski Jumping Continental Cup winter season and the 1st summer season in ski jumping for men." .

ns1:63369 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Lone Star Park Handicap is a Grade III United States of America Thoroughbred horse race for horses three-years-old and older over a distance 1 1⁄16 miles on the dirt held annually during the last week of May at Lone Star Park in Grand Prairie. The event was inaugurated in 1997, the year Lone Star Park opened." .

ns1:63376 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Rainguard Water Sealers 600 was the ninth round of the 2017 IndyCar Series season, contested over 248 laps at the 1.5-mile (2.4 km) Texas Motor Speedway in Fort Worth, Texas. Following a series of incidents in 2016 with weepers (water penetrating on the pavement after rain) that caused the 2016 INDYCAR race to have been postponed initially one day, and then to late August, ten weeks and the November 2016 NASCAR race with a long delay caused by weepers while attempting to dry the track, in 2017 during the NASCAR media tour, Texas Motor Speedway announced it would alter = the circuit while installing a new French drain system to send rain water down pipes to fix the problem." .

ns1:63389 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ayr Gold Cup is a flat handicap horse race in Great Britain open to thoroughbreds aged three years or older. The latter horse, trained at Ayr Racecourse by Nigel Angus, is the most recent winner trained in Scotland." .

ns1:63397 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Amstel Gold Race was the 30th edition of the annual road bicycle racing \"Amstel Gold Race\", held on Sunday 22 April 1995, in the Dutch province of Limburg." .

ns1:63399 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Akitu or Akitum (Sumerian: EZEN Á.KI.TUM, akiti-šekinku, Á.KI.TI.ŠE.GUR10.KU5, lit. \"barley-sowing\"; Akkadian: akitu or rêš-šattim, \"head of the year\") was a spring festival in ancient Mesopotamia.The Babylonian and Assyrian Akitu festival has played a pivotal role in the development of theories of religion, myth and ritual." .

