ns1:63542 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Baybeats is an annual 3-day alternative music festival organized by Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay, held in Singapore. Baybeats was launched in 2002 by John Chiong (WMUM) primarily to create a platform to showcase indie-rock musicians in Asia, especially local musicians, and to expose Singapore audiences to quality acts in the genre as well as to develop the industry. Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay saw a gap in the market in terms of platforms for indie musicians to perform at and the need to satisfy the audience needs for this kind of music, which no other commercial presenter was bringing into Singapore at that time. With a discerning selection of quality performances from diverse Asian countries and a wide spectrum of alternative music genres, the festival is starting to attract international musicians as well as music-lovers to Singapore by offering Baybeats as the essential destination to experience the spirit of indie music in Asia. Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay’s redeveloped Outdoor Theatre (2.5 times larger than before) was and will be a key staple of the festival with performances held there on all three days of Baybeats. 8 talented Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay Youths go through a 4-month long mentorship with veteran musician, writer and academic Kevin Mathews, to create the Baybeats Buzz articles profiling bands as well as documenting the festival behind-the-scenes. Baybeats 2013 presented 35 bands (21 acts from Singapore and 14 from Malaysia, the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand, Korea, Taiwan, Japan and Australia), with 30 bands that played at Baybeats for the first time." .

ns1:63547 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The swimming at the 1983 Pan American Games – women's 100 metre butterfly competition of the swimming events at the 1983 Pan American Games took place on 20 August." .

ns1:63556 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The MassKara Festival (Hiligaynon: Pista sang MassKara, Filipino: Pista ng MassKara) is an annual festival with highlights held every fourth Sunday of October in Bacolod, Philippines. This was the first MassKara Festival and a time of tragedy; on April 22 of that year, the inter-island vessel MV Don Juan carrying many Negrenses, including those belonging to prominent families in Bacolod City, collided with the tanker Tacloban City and sank in Tablas Strait off Mindoro while en route from Manila to Bacolod, which resulted in 18 lives lost, and 115 missing." .

ns1:63572 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1047, adopted unanimously on 29 February 1996, after recalling United Nations Security Council resolution 808 (1993), 827 (1993), 936 (1994) and 955 (1994), the Council appointed Louise Arbour as Prosecutor at the International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda (ICTR) and the International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia (ICTY)." .

