ns1:63758 a ns1:context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1929–30 Southampton F.C. season was the 35th season of competitive football by Southampton F.C., and the club's eighth in the Second Division of the Football League. After finishing fourth in the Second Division the 1928–29 Southampton F.C. season – their highest position in the league to date – Southampton F.C. continued their efforts towards achieving promotion to the First Division, but finished three places lower in seventh. Southampton F.C. used 28 different players during the 1929–30 Southampton F.C. season and had thirteen different goalscorers. Several players left Southampton F.C. at the end of the 1928–29 Southampton F.C. season season. Southampton F.C. began the 1929–30 Second Division campaign against Barnsley, who had finished the 1928–29 Southampton F.C. season just four points above relegation. Outside of the league and the FA Cup, Southampton F.C. played seven additional first-team matches during the 1929–30 Southampton F.C. season. Southampton F.C. used 28 different players during the 1929–30 Southampton F.C. season, 13 of whom scored during the campaign." .

